#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:6
msgid "Data model"
msgstr "資料模型"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:12
msgid "Objects, values and types"
msgstr "物件、值和型別"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:18
msgid ""
":dfn:`Objects` are Python's abstraction for data.  All data in a Python "
"program is represented by objects or by relations between objects. Even code "
"is represented by objects."
msgstr ""
":dfn:`物件` 是 Python 為資料的抽象表示方式。一個 Python 程式當中的所有資料皆"
"由物件或物件之間的關係來呈現。程式碼也都是以物件呈現的。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:31
msgid ""
"Every object has an identity, a type and a value.  An object's *identity* "
"never changes once it has been created; you may think of it as the object's "
"address in memory.  The :keyword:`is` operator compares the identity of two "
"objects; the :func:`id` function returns an integer representing its "
"identity."
msgstr ""
"每個物件都有一個識別性、型別和值。物件的\\ *識別性*\\ 在物件建立後永遠不會改"
"變；你也可以把它想成是該物件在記憶體中的位址。:keyword:`is` 運算子會比較兩個"
"物件的識別性是否相同；:func:`id` 函式則會回傳代表一個該物件的識別性的整數。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:38
msgid "For CPython, ``id(x)`` is the memory address where ``x`` is stored."
msgstr "在 CPython 當中，``id(x)`` 就是 ``x`` 所儲存在的記憶體位址。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:40
msgid ""
"An object's type determines the operations that the object supports (e.g., "
"\"does it have a length?\") and also defines the possible values for objects "
"of that type.  The :func:`type` function returns an object's type (which is "
"an object itself).  Like its identity, an object's :dfn:`type` is also "
"unchangeable. [#]_"
msgstr ""
"一個物件的型別決定了該物件所支援的操作（例如「它有長度嗎？」），也同時定義該"
"型別的物件能夠擁有的值。:func:`type` 函式會回傳一個物件的型別（而該型別本身也"
"是一個物件）。如同它的識別性，一個物件的型別 (:dfn:`type`) 也是不可變的。\\ "
"[#]_"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:46
msgid ""
"The *value* of some objects can change.  Objects whose value can change are "
"said to be *mutable*; objects whose value is unchangeable once they are "
"created are called *immutable*. (The value of an immutable container object "
"that contains a reference to a mutable object can change when the latter's "
"value is changed; however the container is still considered immutable, "
"because the collection of objects it contains cannot be changed.  So, "
"immutability is not strictly the same as having an unchangeable value, it is "
"more subtle.) An object's mutability is determined by its type; for "
"instance, numbers, strings and tuples are immutable, while dictionaries and "
"lists are mutable."
msgstr ""
"某些物件的\\ *值*\\ 可被改變，這種物件稱作「可變的」(*mutable*)；建立後值不能"
"變更的物件則稱作「不可變的」(*immutable*)。（不可變的容器物件中如果包含對於可"
"變物件的參照，則後者的值改變的時候前者的值也會跟著一起改變；這種時候該容器仍"
"會被當成是不可變的，因為它包含的物件集合仍然無法變更。因此可變或不可變嚴格說"
"起並不等同於值是否能被改變，它的定義有其他不明顯的細節。）一個物件是否為可變"
"取決於它的型別；舉例來說，數字、字串和 tuple 是不可變的，而字典與串列則是可變"
"的。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:61
msgid ""
"Objects are never explicitly destroyed; however, when they become "
"unreachable they may be garbage-collected.  An implementation is allowed to "
"postpone garbage collection or omit it altogether --- it is a matter of "
"implementation quality how garbage collection is implemented, as long as no "
"objects are collected that are still reachable."
msgstr ""
"物件永遠不會被明示的摧毀；但當它們變得不再能夠存取的時候可能會被作為垃圾回"
"收。每個實作都能延後垃圾回收或是乾脆忽略它 --- 垃圾回收如何進行完全取決於各個"
"實作，只要沒有被回收的物件仍是可達的。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:69
msgid ""
"CPython currently uses a reference-counting scheme with (optional) delayed "
"detection of cyclically linked garbage, which collects most objects as soon "
"as they become unreachable, but is not guaranteed to collect garbage "
"containing circular references.  See the documentation of the :mod:`gc` "
"module for information on controlling the collection of cyclic garbage. "
"Other implementations act differently and CPython may change. Do not depend "
"on immediate finalization of objects when they become unreachable (so you "
"should always close files explicitly)."
msgstr ""
"CPython 目前使用一種參照計數的方案，並提供可選的循環連結垃圾延遲偵測，這個方"
"案會在大部分物件變得不可存取時馬上回收它們，但不保證能夠回收包含循環參照的垃"
"圾。關於控制循環垃圾回收的資訊請見 :mod:`gc` 模組的說明文件。其他實作的行為不"
"會相同，CPython 也有可能改變，因此請不要仰賴物件在變得不可存取時能夠馬上被最"
"終化（亦即你應該總是明確關閉檔案）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:78
msgid ""
"Note that the use of the implementation's tracing or debugging facilities "
"may keep objects alive that would normally be collectable. Also note that "
"catching an exception with a :keyword:`try`...\\ :keyword:`except` statement "
"may keep objects alive."
msgstr ""
"請注意，使用一個實作的追蹤或除錯工具可能會讓原本能夠回收的物件被維持存活。也"
"請注意，使用 :keyword:`try`...\\ :keyword:`except` 陳述式來抓捕例外也可能會讓"
"物件維持存活。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:83
msgid ""
"Some objects contain references to \"external\" resources such as open files "
"or windows.  It is understood that these resources are freed when the object "
"is garbage-collected, but since garbage collection is not guaranteed to "
"happen, such objects also provide an explicit way to release the external "
"resource, usually a :meth:`!close` method. Programs are strongly recommended "
"to explicitly close such objects.  The :keyword:`try`...\\ :keyword:"
"`finally` statement and the :keyword:`with` statement provide convenient "
"ways to do this."
msgstr ""
"某些物件包含對於「外部」資源的參照，像是開啟的檔案或是視窗。基本上這些資源會"
"在物件被回收時釋放，但因為垃圾回收不保證會發生，這種物件也會提供明確釋放外部"
"資源的方式 --- 通常是 :meth:`!close` method。強烈建議各個程式明確關閉這種物"
"件。:keyword:`try`...\\ :keyword:`finally` 陳述式與 :keyword:`with` 陳述式提"
"供進行明確關閉的方便手段。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:93
msgid ""
"Some objects contain references to other objects; these are called "
"*containers*. Examples of containers are tuples, lists and dictionaries.  "
"The references are part of a container's value.  In most cases, when we talk "
"about the value of a container, we imply the values, not the identities of "
"the contained objects; however, when we talk about the mutability of a "
"container, only the identities of the immediately contained objects are "
"implied.  So, if an immutable container (like a tuple) contains a reference "
"to a mutable object, its value changes if that mutable object is changed."
msgstr ""
"某些物件包含對於其他物件的參照；這種物件被叫做「容器」。容器的範例有 tuple、"
"串列與字典。這些參照是容器的值的一部分。通常當我們提到容器的值的時候，我們指"
"的是其中包含的物件的值，而不是它們的識別性；但當我們提到容器是否可變的時候，"
"我們指的是直接包含在其中的物件的識別性。因此，如果一個不可變的容器（像一個 "
"tuple）包含對於可變物件的參照，該可變物件被變更時該容器的值也會跟著變更。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:102
msgid ""
"Types affect almost all aspects of object behavior.  Even the importance of "
"object identity is affected in some sense: for immutable types, operations "
"that compute new values may actually return a reference to any existing "
"object with the same type and value, while for mutable objects this is not "
"allowed. For example, after ``a = 1; b = 1``, *a* and *b* may or may not "
"refer to the same object with the value one, depending on the "
"implementation. This is because :class:`int` is an immutable type, so the "
"reference to ``1`` can be reused. This behaviour depends on the "
"implementation used, so should not be relied upon, but is something to be "
"aware of when making use of object identity tests. However, after ``c = []; "
"d = []``, *c* and *d* are guaranteed to refer to two different, unique, "
"newly created empty lists. (Note that ``e = f = []`` assigns the *same* "
"object to both *e* and *f*.)"
msgstr ""
"型別幾乎影響物件行為的所有面向。就連物件識別性的重要性某種程度上也受型別影"
"響：對於不可變的型別，計算新值的操作可能其實會回傳一個某個相同型別且相同值的"
"現存物件的參照；對於可變型別這則不會發生。舉例來說，在進行 ``a = 1; b = 1`` "
"之後，*a* 和 *b* 可能會參照同一個物件，也可能不會，取決於所使用的實作。這是因"
"為 :class:`int` 是不可變的型別，因此 ``1`` 的參照可以重複利用。這個行為取決於"
"所使用的實作，因此不應該依賴它，但在進行物件識別性測試的時候還是需要注意有這"
"件事情。而在進行 ``c = []; d = []`` 之後，*c* 和 *d* 則保證會參照兩個不同、獨"
"特、且新建立的空白串列。（請注意，``e = f = []`` 則會將同一個物件同時指派給 "
"*e* 和 *f*。）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:120
msgid "The standard type hierarchy"
msgstr "標準型別階層"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:129
msgid ""
"Below is a list of the types that are built into Python.  Extension modules "
"(written in C, Java, or other languages, depending on the implementation) "
"can define additional types.  Future versions of Python may add types to the "
"type hierarchy (e.g., rational numbers, efficiently stored arrays of "
"integers, etc.), although such additions will often be provided via the "
"standard library instead."
msgstr ""
"以下是 Python 內建型別的列表。擴充模組（依實作不同，以 C、Java 或其他語言撰"
"寫）可以定義額外的型別。未來的 Python 版本可能會在型別階層中加入新的型別（例"
"如有理數、儲存效率高的整數陣列等），不過這類新增通常會改由標準函式庫提供。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:140
msgid ""
"Some of the type descriptions below contain a paragraph listing 'special "
"attributes.'  These are attributes that provide access to the implementation "
"and are not intended for general use.  Their definition may change in the "
"future."
msgstr ""
"下方部分型別描述中有一個列出「特殊屬性」的段落。這些屬性提供對實作的存取，並"
"非供一般使用。它們的定義在未來可能會改變。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:146 ../../reference/datamodel.rst:148
msgid "None"
msgstr "None"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:150
msgid ""
"This type has a single value.  There is a single object with this value. "
"This object is accessed through the built-in name ``None``. It is used to "
"signify the absence of a value in many situations, e.g., it is returned from "
"functions that don't explicitly return anything. Its truth value is false."
msgstr ""
"這個型別只有一個值。只有一個物件有這個值。這個物件由內建名稱 ``None`` 存取。"
"它用來在許多情況下代表值不存在，例如沒有明確回傳任何東西的函式就會回傳這個物"
"件。它的真值是 false。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:157 ../../reference/datamodel.rst:159
msgid "NotImplemented"
msgstr "NotImplemented"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:161
msgid ""
"This type has a single value.  There is a single object with this value. "
"This object is accessed through the built-in name :data:`NotImplemented`. "
"Numeric methods and rich comparison methods should return this value if they "
"do not implement the operation for the operands provided.  (The interpreter "
"will then try the reflected operation, or some other fallback, depending on "
"the operator.)  It should not be evaluated in a boolean context."
msgstr ""
"這個型別只有一個值。只有一個物件有這個值。這個物件由內建名稱 :data:"
"`NotImplemented` 存取。數值方法和 rich comparison 方法應該在沒有為所提供的運"
"算元實作該操作的時候回傳這個值。（直譯器接下來則會依運算子嘗試反轉的操作或是"
"其他的後備方案。）它不應該在預期布林值的情境中被計算。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:168
msgid "See :ref:`implementing-the-arithmetic-operations` for more details."
msgstr "更多細節請見\\ :ref:`implementing-the-arithmetic-operations`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:172
msgid "Evaluating :data:`NotImplemented` in a boolean context was deprecated."
msgstr "在預期布林值的情境中計算 :data:`NotImplemented` 已被棄用。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:175
msgid ""
"Evaluating :data:`NotImplemented` in a boolean context now raises a :exc:"
"`TypeError`. It previously evaluated to :const:`True` and emitted a :exc:"
"`DeprecationWarning` since Python 3.9."
msgstr ""
"在預期布林值的情境中計算 :data:`NotImplemented` 現在會引發 :exc:`TypeError`。"
"它先前會計算為 :const:`True`，並自 Python 3.9 起會發出 :exc:"
"`DeprecationWarning`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:182 ../../reference/datamodel.rst:183
msgid "Ellipsis"
msgstr "Ellipsis"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:187
msgid ""
"This type has a single value.  There is a single object with this value. "
"This object is accessed through the literal ``...`` or the built-in name "
"``Ellipsis``.  Its truth value is true."
msgstr ""
"這個型別只有一個值。只有一個物件有這個值。這個物件由字面值 ``...`` 或內建名"
"稱 ``Ellipsis`` 存取。它的真值是 true。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:193
msgid ":class:`numbers.Number`"
msgstr ":class:`numbers.Number`"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:197
msgid ""
"These are created by numeric literals and returned as results by arithmetic "
"operators and arithmetic built-in functions.  Numeric objects are immutable; "
"once created their value never changes.  Python numbers are of course "
"strongly related to mathematical numbers, but subject to the limitations of "
"numerical representation in computers."
msgstr ""
"這些物件由數值字面值建立，並作為算術運算子與算術內建函式的結果回傳。數值物件"
"是不可變的；一旦建立，其值就永遠不會改變。Python 的數字當然與數學上的數字密切"
"相關，但會受到電腦中數值表示方式的限制。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:203
msgid ""
"The string representations of the numeric classes, computed by :meth:"
"`~object.__repr__` and :meth:`~object.__str__`, have the following "
"properties:"
msgstr ""
"數值類別的字串表示法（由 :meth:`~object.__repr__` 和 :meth:`~object.__str__` "
"計算）具有以下特性："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:207
msgid ""
"They are valid numeric literals which, when passed to their class "
"constructor, produce an object having the value of the original numeric."
msgstr ""
"它們是有效的數值字面值，將其傳給所屬類別的建構函式時，會產生一個與原數值具有"
"相同值的物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:211
msgid "The representation is in base 10, when possible."
msgstr "表示法在可能的情況下會使用十進位。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:213
msgid ""
"Leading zeros, possibly excepting a single zero before a decimal point, are "
"not shown."
msgstr "不會顯示前導零，但小數點前的單獨一個零可能除外。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:216
msgid ""
"Trailing zeros, possibly excepting a single zero after a decimal point, are "
"not shown."
msgstr "不會顯示尾隨零，但小數點後的單獨一個零可能除外。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:219
msgid "A sign is shown only when the number is negative."
msgstr "只有在數字為負數時才會顯示正負號。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:221
msgid ""
"Python distinguishes between integers, floating-point numbers, and complex "
"numbers:"
msgstr "Python 區分整數、浮點數與複數："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:226
msgid ":class:`numbers.Integral`"
msgstr ":class:`numbers.Integral`"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:230
msgid ""
"These represent elements from the mathematical set of integers (positive and "
"negative)."
msgstr "這些代表數學上整數集合（正數與負數）中的元素。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:236
msgid ""
"The rules for integer representation are intended to give the most "
"meaningful interpretation of shift and mask operations involving negative "
"integers."
msgstr "整數表示法的規則旨在讓涉及負整數的移位與遮罩運算得到最有意義的解讀。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:239
msgid "There are two types of integers:"
msgstr "整數有兩種型別："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:241
msgid "Integers (:class:`int`)"
msgstr "整數 (:class:`int`)"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:242
msgid ""
"These represent numbers in an unlimited range, subject to available "
"(virtual) memory only.  For the purpose of shift and mask operations, a "
"binary representation is assumed, and negative numbers are represented in a "
"variant of 2's complement which gives the illusion of an infinite string of "
"sign bits extending to the left."
msgstr ""
"這些代表無限範圍內的數字，只受可用（虛擬）記憶體的限制。在進行移位與遮罩運算"
"時，會假設使用二進位表示法，而負數則以二補數的一種變體表示，這種變體會造成彷"
"彿有一串無限長的符號位元向左延伸的錯覺。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:248
msgid "Booleans (:class:`bool`)"
msgstr "布林值 (:class:`bool`)"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:254
msgid ""
"These represent the truth values False and True.  The two objects "
"representing the values ``False`` and ``True`` are the only Boolean objects. "
"The Boolean type is a subtype of the integer type, and Boolean values behave "
"like the values 0 and 1, respectively, in almost all contexts, the exception "
"being that when converted to a string, the strings ``\"False\"`` or "
"``\"True\"`` are returned, respectively."
msgstr ""
"這些代表真值 False 與 True。代表 ``False`` 與 ``True`` 值的兩個物件是僅有的布"
"林物件。布林型別是整數型別的子型別，且在幾乎所有情境中，布林值的行為分別與值 "
"0 和 1 相同，唯一的例外是轉換為字串時，會分別回傳字串 ``\"False\"`` 或 "
"``\"True\"``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:264
msgid ":class:`numbers.Real` (:class:`float`)"
msgstr ":class:`numbers.Real` (:class:`float`)"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:272
msgid ""
"These represent machine-level double precision floating-point numbers. You "
"are at the mercy of the underlying machine architecture (and C or Java "
"implementation) for the accepted range and handling of overflow. Python does "
"not support single-precision floating-point numbers; the savings in "
"processor and memory usage that are usually the reason for using these are "
"dwarfed by the overhead of using objects in Python, so there is no reason to "
"complicate the language with two kinds of floating-point numbers."
msgstr ""
"這些代表機器層級的雙精度浮點數。可接受的範圍與溢位的處理方式完全取決於底層的"
"機器架構（以及 C 或 Java 實作）。Python 不支援單精度浮點數；使用單精度浮點數"
"通常是為了節省處理器與記憶體用量，但與在 Python 中使用物件的開銷相比，這些節"
"省微不足道，因此沒有理由讓語言因兩種浮點數而變得複雜。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:282
msgid ":class:`numbers.Complex` (:class:`complex`)"
msgstr ":class:`numbers.Complex` (:class:`complex`)"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:288
msgid ""
"These represent complex numbers as a pair of machine-level double precision "
"floating-point numbers.  The same caveats apply as for floating-point "
"numbers. The real and imaginary parts of a complex number ``z`` can be "
"retrieved through the read-only attributes ``z.real`` and ``z.imag``."
msgstr ""
"這些以一對機器層級的雙精度浮點數來表示複數。浮點數的注意事項同樣適用於此。複"
"數 ``z`` 的實部與虛部可以透過唯讀屬性 ``z.real`` 和 ``z.imag`` 取得。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:296
msgid "Sequences"
msgstr "序列"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:305
msgid ""
"These represent finite ordered sets indexed by non-negative numbers. The "
"built-in function :func:`len` returns the number of items of a sequence. "
"When the length of a sequence is *n*, the index set contains the numbers 0, "
"1, ..., *n*-1.  Item *i* of sequence *a* is selected by ``a[i]``. Some "
"sequences, including built-in sequences, interpret negative subscripts by "
"adding the sequence length. For example, ``a[-2]`` equals ``a[n-2]``, the "
"second to last item of sequence a with length ``n``."
msgstr ""
"這些代表以非負數作為索引的有限有序集合。內建函式 :func:`len` 會回傳序列的項目"
"數量。當序列的長度為 *n* 時，索引集合包含數字 0, 1, ..., *n*-1。序列 *a* 的項"
"目 *i* 以 ``a[i]`` 選取。某些序列（包括內建序列）會將負的下標加上序列長度來解"
"讀。例如 ``a[-2]`` 等於 ``a[n-2]``，也就是長度為 ``n`` 的序列 a 中倒數第二個"
"項目。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:313
msgid ""
"The resulting value must be a nonnegative integer less than the number of "
"items in the sequence. If it is not, an :exc:`IndexError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"所得的值必須是一個小於序列項目數量的非負整數。若非如此，則會引發 :exc:"
"`IndexError`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:322
msgid ""
"Sequences also support slicing: ``a[start:stop]`` selects all items with "
"index *k* such that *start* ``<=`` *k* ``<`` *stop*.  When used as an "
"expression, a slice is a sequence of the same type. The comment above about "
"negative subscripts also applies to negative slice positions. Note that no "
"error is raised if a slice position is less than zero or larger than the "
"length of the sequence."
msgstr ""
"序列也支援切片：``a[start:stop]`` 會選取索引 *k* 滿足 *start* ``<=`` *k* "
"``<`` *stop* 的所有項目。作為運算式使用時，切片是相同型別的序列。上述關於負下"
"標的說明也適用於負的切片位置。請注意，切片位置小於零或大於序列長度時並不會引"
"發錯誤。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:329
msgid ""
"If *start* is missing or :data:`None`, slicing behaves as if *start* was "
"zero. If *stop* is missing or ``None``, slicing behaves as if *stop* was "
"equal to the length of the sequence."
msgstr ""
"如果省略 *start* 或其為 :data:`None`，切片的行為就如同 *start* 為零。如果省"
"略 *stop* 或其為 ``None``，切片的行為就如同 *stop* 等於序列的長度。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:333
msgid ""
"Some sequences also support \"extended slicing\" with a third \"step\" "
"parameter: ``a[i:j:k]`` selects all items of *a* with index *x* where ``x = "
"i + n*k``, *n* ``>=`` ``0`` and *i* ``<=`` *x* ``<`` *j*."
msgstr ""
"某些序列也支援帶有第三個「步長 (step)」參數的「延伸切片 (extended "
"slicing)」：``a[i:j:k]`` 會選取 *a* 中索引為 *x* 的所有項目，其中 ``x = i + "
"n*k``、*n* ``>=`` ``0`` 且 *i* ``<=`` *x* ``<`` *j*。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:337
msgid "Sequences are distinguished according to their mutability:"
msgstr "序列依照可變性區分為："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:341
msgid "Immutable sequences"
msgstr "不可變序列"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:347
msgid ""
"An object of an immutable sequence type cannot change once it is created.  "
"(If the object contains references to other objects, these other objects may "
"be mutable and may be changed; however, the collection of objects directly "
"referenced by an immutable object cannot change.)"
msgstr ""
"不可變序列型別的物件一旦建立就無法改變。（如果該物件包含對其他物件的參照，這"
"些其他物件可能是可變的，因而可以被改變；然而，由不可變物件直接參照的物件集合"
"是無法改變的。）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:352
msgid "The following types are immutable sequences:"
msgstr "以下型別是不可變序列："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:357
msgid "Strings"
msgstr "字串 (String)"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:365
msgid ""
"A string (:class:`str`) is a sequence of values that represent :dfn:"
"`characters`, or more formally, *Unicode code points*. All the code points "
"in the range ``0`` to ``0x10FFFF`` can be represented in a string."
msgstr ""
"字串 (:class:`str`) 是一個由代表\\ :dfn:`字元`\\ 的值所組成的序列，更正式地"
"說，是由 *Unicode 碼位 (code point)* 組成的序列。範圍在 ``0`` 到 "
"``0x10FFFF`` 之間的所有碼位都可以在字串中表示。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:370
msgid ""
"Python doesn't have a dedicated *character* type. Instead, every code point "
"in the string is represented as a string object with length ``1``."
msgstr ""
"Python 沒有專用的\\ *字元*\\ 型別。取而代之的是，字串中的每個碼位都以長度為 "
"``1`` 的字串物件表示。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:374
msgid ""
"The built-in function :func:`ord` converts a code point from its string form "
"to an integer in the range ``0`` to ``0x10FFFF``; :func:`chr` converts an "
"integer in the range ``0`` to ``0x10FFFF`` to the corresponding length ``1`` "
"string object. :meth:`str.encode` can be used to convert a :class:`str` to :"
"class:`bytes` using the given text encoding, and :meth:`bytes.decode` can be "
"used to achieve the opposite."
msgstr ""
"內建函式 :func:`ord` 會將碼位從字串形式轉換為範圍在 ``0`` 到 ``0x10FFFF`` 之"
"間的整數；:func:`chr` 則將範圍在 ``0`` 到 ``0x10FFFF`` 之間的整數轉換為對應的"
"長度為 ``1`` 的字串物件。:meth:`str.encode` 可以使用給定的文字編碼將 :class:"
"`str` 轉換為 :class:`bytes`，而 :meth:`bytes.decode` 則可用於達成相反的轉換。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:382
msgid "Tuples"
msgstr "Tuple（元組）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:388
msgid ""
"The items of a :class:`tuple` are arbitrary Python objects. Tuples of two or "
"more items are formed by comma-separated lists of expressions.  A tuple of "
"one item (a 'singleton') can be formed by affixing a comma to an expression "
"(an expression by itself does not create a tuple, since parentheses must be "
"usable for grouping of expressions).  An empty tuple can be formed by an "
"empty pair of parentheses."
msgstr ""
":class:`tuple` 的項目是任意的 Python 物件。包含兩個以上項目的 tuple 由逗號分"
"隔的運算式串列構成。只有一個項目的 tuple（「單例 (singleton)」）可以透過在運"
"算式後面加上逗號來構成（單獨的運算式並不會建立 tuple，因為圓括號必須能用於將"
"運算式分組）。空的 tuple 可以由一對空的圓括號構成。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:395
msgid "Bytes"
msgstr "位元組"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:398
msgid ""
"A :class:`bytes` object is an immutable array.  The items are 8-bit bytes, "
"represented by integers in the range 0 <= x < 256.  Bytes literals (like "
"``b'abc'``) and the built-in :func:`bytes` constructor can be used to create "
"bytes objects.  Also, bytes objects can be decoded to strings via the :meth:"
"`~bytes.decode` method."
msgstr ""
":class:`bytes` 物件是一個不可變的陣列。其項目為 8 位元的位元組，以範圍在 0 "
"<= x < 256 的整數表示。位元組字面值（例如 ``b'abc'``）與內建的 :func:`bytes` "
"建構函式都可以用來建立 bytes 物件。此外，bytes 物件也可以透過 :meth:`~bytes."
"decode` 方法解碼為字串。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:406
msgid "Mutable sequences"
msgstr "可變序列"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:415
msgid ""
"Mutable sequences can be changed after they are created.  The subscription "
"and slicing notations can be used as the target of assignment and :keyword:"
"`del` (delete) statements."
msgstr ""
"可變序列在建立後可以被改變。下標與切片標示法可以作為賦值與 :keyword:`del`\\ "
"（刪除）陳述式的目標。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:423
msgid ""
"The :mod:`collections` and :mod:`array` module provide additional examples "
"of mutable sequence types."
msgstr ":mod:`collections` 與 :mod:`array` 模組提供了更多可變序列型別的範例。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:426
msgid "There are currently two intrinsic mutable sequence types:"
msgstr "目前有兩種固有的可變序列型別："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:428
msgid "Lists"
msgstr "List（串列）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:431
msgid ""
"The items of a list are arbitrary Python objects.  Lists are formed by "
"placing a comma-separated list of expressions in square brackets. (Note that "
"there are no special cases needed to form lists of length 0 or 1.)"
msgstr ""
"串列的項目是任意的 Python 物件。串列的構成方式是將逗號分隔的運算式串列放在方"
"括號中。（請注意，構成長度為 0 或 1 的串列不需要特殊處理。）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:435
msgid "Byte Arrays"
msgstr "位元組陣列"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:438
msgid ""
"A bytearray object is a mutable array. They are created by the built-in :"
"func:`bytearray` constructor.  Aside from being mutable (and hence "
"unhashable), byte arrays otherwise provide the same interface and "
"functionality as immutable :class:`bytes` objects."
msgstr ""
"bytearray 物件是一個可變的陣列。它們由內建的 :func:`bytearray` 建構函式建立。"
"除了是可變的（因此不可雜湊）之外，位元組陣列提供的介面與功能都與不可變的 :"
"class:`bytes` 物件相同。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:445
msgid "Set types"
msgstr "Set（集合）型別"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:451
msgid ""
"These represent unordered, finite sets of unique, immutable objects. As "
"such, they cannot be indexed by any subscript. However, they can be iterated "
"over, and the built-in function :func:`len` returns the number of items in a "
"set. Common uses for sets are fast membership testing, removing duplicates "
"from a sequence, and computing mathematical operations such as intersection, "
"union, difference, and symmetric difference."
msgstr ""
"這些代表由唯一且不可變的物件所組成的無序有限集合。因此，它們無法以任何下標進"
"行索引。不過它們可以被疊代，且內建函式 :func:`len` 會回傳集合中的項目數量。集"
"合常見的用途包括快速的成員測試、移除序列中的重複項目，以及計算交集、聯集、差"
"集與對稱差集等數學運算。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:458
msgid ""
"For set elements, the same immutability rules apply as for dictionary keys. "
"Note that numeric types obey the normal rules for numeric comparison: if two "
"numbers compare equal (e.g., ``1`` and ``1.0``), only one of them can be "
"contained in a set."
msgstr ""
"集合元素適用與字典鍵相同的不可變性規則。請注意，數值型別遵循一般的數值比較規"
"則：如果兩個數字比較結果相等（例如 ``1`` 和 ``1.0``），則集合中只能包含其中一"
"個。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:463
msgid "There are currently two intrinsic set types:"
msgstr "目前有兩種固有的集合型別："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:466
msgid "Sets"
msgstr "Set（集合）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:469
msgid ""
"These represent a mutable set. They are created by the built-in :func:`set` "
"constructor and can be modified afterwards by several methods, such as :meth:"
"`~set.add`."
msgstr ""
"這些代表可變的集合。它們由內建的 :func:`set` 建構函式建立，之後可以透過數個方"
"法修改，例如 :meth:`~set.add`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:474
msgid "Frozen sets"
msgstr "Frozen set（凍結集合）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:477
msgid ""
"These represent an immutable set.  They are created by the built-in :func:"
"`frozenset` constructor.  As a frozenset is immutable and :term:`hashable`, "
"it can be used again as an element of another set, or as a dictionary key."
msgstr ""
"這些代表不可變的集合。它們由內建的 :func:`frozenset` 建構函式建立。由於 "
"frozenset 是不可變且\\ :term:`可雜湊的 <hashable>`，它可以再作為另一個集合的"
"元素，或作為字典的鍵。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:486
msgid "Mappings"
msgstr "對映"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:493
msgid ""
"These represent finite sets of objects indexed by arbitrary index sets. The "
"subscript notation ``a[k]`` selects the item indexed by ``k`` from the "
"mapping ``a``; this can be used in expressions and as the target of "
"assignments or :keyword:`del` statements. The built-in function :func:`len` "
"returns the number of items in a mapping."
msgstr ""
"這些代表以任意索引集合作為索引的有限物件集合。下標標示法 ``a[k]`` 會從對映 "
"``a`` 中選取以 ``k`` 為索引的項目；這可以用在運算式中，也可以作為賦值或 :"
"keyword:`del` 陳述式的目標。內建函式 :func:`len` 會回傳對映中的項目數量。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:499
msgid "There are two intrinsic mapping types:"
msgstr "有兩種固有的對映型別："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:503
msgid "Dictionaries"
msgstr "字典"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:507
msgid ""
"These represent finite sets of objects indexed by nearly arbitrary values.  "
"The only types of values not acceptable as keys are values containing lists "
"or dictionaries or other mutable types that are compared by value rather "
"than by object identity, the reason being that the efficient implementation "
"of dictionaries requires a key's hash value to remain constant. Numeric "
"types used for keys obey the normal rules for numeric comparison: if two "
"numbers compare equal (e.g., ``1`` and ``1.0``) then they can be used "
"interchangeably to index the same dictionary entry."
msgstr ""
"這些代表以幾乎任意的值作為索引的有限物件集合。唯一不能作為鍵的值型別，是包含"
"串列、字典或其他以值而非物件識別性進行比較的可變型別的值，原因是字典的高效實"
"作需要鍵的雜湊值保持不變。用作鍵的數值型別遵循一般的數值比較規則：如果兩個數"
"字比較結果相等（例如 ``1`` 和 ``1.0``），則它們可以互換使用來索引同一個字典條"
"目。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:516
msgid ""
"Dictionaries preserve insertion order, meaning that keys will be produced in "
"the same order they were added sequentially over the dictionary. Replacing "
"an existing key does not change the order, however removing a key and re-"
"inserting it will add it to the end instead of keeping its old place."
msgstr ""
"字典會保留插入順序，也就是說，鍵產生的順序會與它們依序加入字典的順序相同。取"
"代既有的鍵不會改變順序，但移除一個鍵後再重新插入，會將它加到最後，而不是保留"
"原本的位置。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:521
msgid ""
"Dictionaries are mutable; they can be created by the ``{}`` notation (see "
"section :ref:`dict`)."
msgstr ""
"字典是可變的；它們可以用 ``{}`` 標示法建立（請見\\ :ref:`dict`\\ 章節）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:528
msgid ""
"The extension modules :mod:`dbm.ndbm` and :mod:`dbm.gnu` provide additional "
"examples of mapping types, as does the :mod:`collections` module."
msgstr ""
"擴充模組 :mod:`dbm.ndbm` 與 :mod:`dbm.gnu` 提供了更多對映型別的範例，:mod:"
"`collections` 模組也是如此。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:532
msgid ""
"Dictionaries did not preserve insertion order in versions of Python before "
"3.6. In CPython 3.6, insertion order was preserved, but it was considered an "
"implementation detail at that time rather than a language guarantee."
msgstr ""
"在 Python 3.6 之前的版本中，字典不會保留插入順序。在 CPython 3.6 中，插入順序"
"會被保留，但當時這被視為實作細節，而非語言層面的保證。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:539
msgid "Frozen dictionaries"
msgstr "凍結字典"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:543
msgid ""
"These represent an immutable dictionary.  They are created by the built-in :"
"func:`frozendict` constructor.  A frozendict is :term:`hashable` if all of "
"its keys and values are hashable, in which case it can be used as an element "
"of a set, or as a key in another mapping.  :class:`!frozendict` is not a "
"subclass of :class:`dict`; it inherits directly from :class:`object`."
msgstr ""
"這些代表不可變的字典。它們由內建的 :func:`frozendict` 建構函式建立。如果 "
"frozendict 的所有鍵與值都是可雜湊的，它就是\\ :term:`可雜湊的 <hashable>`，在"
"這種情況下它可以作為集合的元素，或作為另一個對映中的鍵。:class:`!frozendict` "
"不是 :class:`dict` 的子類別；它直接繼承自 :class:`object`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:553
msgid "Callable types"
msgstr "可呼叫型別"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:561
msgid ""
"These are the types to which the function call operation (see section :ref:"
"`calls`) can be applied:"
msgstr "以下是可套用函式呼叫操作（請見\\ :ref:`calls`\\ 章節）的型別："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:568
msgid "User-defined functions"
msgstr "使用者定義函式"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:575
msgid ""
"A user-defined function object is created by a function definition (see "
"section :ref:`function`).  It should be called with an argument list "
"containing the same number of items as the function's formal parameter list."
msgstr ""
"使用者定義函式物件由函式定義建立（請見\\ :ref:`function`\\ 章節）。呼叫它時所"
"用的引數列表，項目數量應與該函式的形式參數列表相同。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:581 ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1499
#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1702
msgid "Special read-only attributes"
msgstr "特殊唯讀屬性"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:592 ../../reference/datamodel.rst:634
#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1232
msgid "Attribute"
msgstr "屬性"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:593 ../../reference/datamodel.rst:635
#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1233
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr "含義"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:596
msgid ""
"A reference to the :class:`dictionary <dict>` that holds the function's "
"builtins namespace."
msgstr ""
"一個對\\ :class:`字典 <dict>`\\ 的參照，該字典保存了函式的內建命名空間。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:602
msgid ""
"A reference to the :class:`dictionary <dict>` that holds the function's :ref:"
"`global variables <naming>` -- the global namespace of the module in which "
"the function was defined."
msgstr ""
"一個對\\ :class:`字典 <dict>`\\ 的參照，該字典保存了函式的\\ :ref:`全域變數 "
"<naming>` -- 也就是定義該函式之模組的全域命名空間。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:607
msgid ""
"``None`` or a :class:`tuple` of cells that contain bindings for the names "
"specified in the :attr:`~codeobject.co_freevars` attribute of the "
"function's :attr:`code object <function.__code__>`."
msgstr ""
"``None`` 或一個由 cell 組成的 :class:`tuple`，這些 cell 包含了在函式\\ :attr:"
"`程式碼物件 <function.__code__>`\\ 的 :attr:`~codeobject.co_freevars` 屬性中"
"所指定之名稱的繫結。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:611
msgid ""
"A cell object has the attribute ``cell_contents``. This can be used to get "
"the value of the cell, as well as set the value."
msgstr ""
"cell 物件具有 ``cell_contents`` 屬性。它可以用來取得 cell 的值，也可以設定該"
"值。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:615 ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1750
msgid "Special writable attributes"
msgstr "特殊可寫入屬性"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:629
msgid "Most of these attributes check the type of the assigned value:"
msgstr "這些屬性大多會檢查所指派之值的型別："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:638
msgid "The function's documentation string, or ``None`` if unavailable."
msgstr "函式的文件字串，若不可用則為 ``None``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:641
msgid ""
"The function's name. See also: :attr:`__name__ attributes <definition."
"__name__>`."
msgstr "函式的名稱。另請參閱：:attr:`__name__ 屬性 <definition.__name__>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:645
msgid ""
"The function's :term:`qualified name`. See also: :attr:`__qualname__ "
"attributes <definition.__qualname__>`."
msgstr ""
"函式的\\ :term:`限定名稱 <qualified name>`。另請參閱：:attr:`__qualname__ 屬"
"性 <definition.__qualname__>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:651
msgid ""
"The name of the module the function was defined in, or ``None`` if "
"unavailable."
msgstr "定義該函式的模組名稱，若不可用則為 ``None``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:655
msgid ""
"A :class:`tuple` containing default :term:`parameter` values for those "
"parameters that have defaults, or ``None`` if no parameters have a default "
"value."
msgstr ""
"一個 :class:`tuple`，包含具有預設值之\\ :term:`參數 <parameter>`\\ 的預設值；"
"若沒有參數具有預設值則為 ``None``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:660
msgid ""
"The :ref:`code object <code-objects>` representing the compiled function "
"body."
msgstr "代表編譯函式主體的\\ :ref:`程式碼物件 <code-objects>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:664
msgid ""
"The namespace supporting arbitrary function attributes. See also: :attr:"
"`__dict__ attributes <object.__dict__>`."
msgstr ""
"支援任意函式屬性的命名空間。另請參閱：:attr:`__dict__ 屬性 <object."
"__dict__>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:668
msgid ""
"A :class:`dictionary <dict>` containing annotations of :term:`parameters "
"<parameter>`. The keys of the dictionary are the parameter names, and "
"``'return'`` for the return annotation, if provided. See also: :attr:`object."
"__annotations__`."
msgstr ""
"一個包含\\ :term:`參數 <parameter>`\\ 註釋的\\ :class:`字典 <dict>`。字典的鍵"
"為參數名稱，若有提供回傳註釋，則還有代表回傳註釋的 ``'return'``。另請參閱：:"
"attr:`object.__annotations__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:674 ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1124
#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1290
msgid ""
"Annotations are now :ref:`lazily evaluated <lazy-evaluation>`. See :pep:"
"`649`."
msgstr "註釋現在會\\ :ref:`惰性求值 <lazy-evaluation>`。請見 :pep:`649`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:679
msgid ""
"The :term:`annotate function` for this function, or ``None`` if the function "
"has no annotations. See :attr:`object.__annotate__`."
msgstr ""
"此函式的\\ :term:`註釋函式 <annotate function>`，若函式沒有註釋則為 "
"``None``。請見 :attr:`object.__annotate__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:685
msgid ""
"A :class:`dictionary <dict>` containing defaults for keyword-only :term:"
"`parameters <parameter>`."
msgstr ""
"一個包含僅限關鍵字\\ :term:`參數 <parameter>`\\ 之預設值的\\ :class:`字典 "
"<dict>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:689
msgid ""
"A :class:`tuple` containing the :ref:`type parameters <type-params>` of a :"
"ref:`generic function <generic-functions>`."
msgstr ""
"一個 :class:`tuple`，包含\\ :ref:`泛型函式 <generic-functions>`\\ 的\\ :ref:`"
"型別參數 <type-params>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:694
msgid ""
"Function objects also support getting and setting arbitrary attributes, "
"which can be used, for example, to attach metadata to functions.  Regular "
"attribute dot-notation is used to get and set such attributes."
msgstr ""
"函式物件也支援取得與設定任意屬性，例如可以用來將詮釋資料附加到函式上。取得與"
"設定這類屬性時使用一般的屬性點標示法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:700
msgid ""
"CPython's current implementation only supports function attributes on user-"
"defined functions. Function attributes on :ref:`built-in functions <builtin-"
"functions>` may be supported in the future."
msgstr ""
"CPython 目前的實作只支援在使用者定義函式上設定函式屬性。未來可能會支援在\\ :"
"ref:`內建函式 <builtin-functions>`\\ 上設定函式屬性。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:705
msgid ""
"Additional information about a function's definition can be retrieved from "
"its :ref:`code object <code-objects>` (accessible via the :attr:`~function."
"__code__` attribute)."
msgstr ""
"關於函式定義的其他資訊可以從其\\ :ref:`程式碼物件 <code-objects>`\\ 取得（可"
"透過 :attr:`~function.__code__` 屬性存取）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:713
msgid "Instance methods"
msgstr "實例方法"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:720
msgid ""
"An instance method object combines a class, a class instance and any "
"callable object (normally a user-defined function)."
msgstr ""
"實例方法物件結合了一個類別、一個類別實例與任意可呼叫物件（通常是使用者定義函"
"式）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:730 ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1846
msgid "Special read-only attributes:"
msgstr "特殊唯讀屬性："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:735
msgid ""
"Refers to the class instance object to which the method is :ref:`bound "
"<method-binding>`"
msgstr "指向該方法所\\ :ref:`繫結 <method-binding>`\\ 的類別實例物件"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:739
msgid "Refers to the original :ref:`function object <user-defined-funcs>`"
msgstr "指向原始的\\ :ref:`函式物件 <user-defined-funcs>`"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:742
msgid ""
"The method's documentation (same as :attr:`method.__func__.__doc__ <function."
"__doc__>`). A :class:`string <str>` if the original function had a "
"docstring, else ``None``."
msgstr ""
"方法的說明文件（同 :attr:`method.__func__.__doc__ <function.__doc__>`）。若原"
"始函式有說明字串則為一個\\ :class:`字串 <str>`，否則為 ``None``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:748
msgid ""
"The name of the method (same as :attr:`method.__func__.__name__ <function."
"__name__>`)"
msgstr "方法的名稱（同 :attr:`method.__func__.__name__ <function.__name__>`）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:752
msgid ""
"The name of the module the method was defined in, or ``None`` if unavailable."
msgstr "定義該方法的模組名稱，若不可用則為 ``None``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:755
msgid ""
"Methods also support accessing (but not setting) the arbitrary function "
"attributes on the underlying :ref:`function object <user-defined-funcs>`."
msgstr ""
"方法也支援存取（但不支援設定）底層\\ :ref:`函式物件 <user-defined-funcs>`\\ "
"上的任意函式屬性。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:758
msgid ""
"User-defined method objects may be created when getting an attribute of a "
"class (perhaps via an instance of that class), if that attribute is a user-"
"defined :ref:`function object <user-defined-funcs>` or a :class:"
"`classmethod` object."
msgstr ""
"在取得類別的屬性時（可能是透過該類別的實例），如果該屬性是使用者定義的\\ :"
"ref:`函式物件 <user-defined-funcs>`\\ 或 :class:`classmethod` 物件，則可能會"
"建立使用者定義方法物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:765
msgid ""
"When an instance method object is created by retrieving a user-defined :ref:"
"`function object <user-defined-funcs>` from a class via one of its "
"instances, its :attr:`~method.__self__` attribute is the instance, and the "
"method object is said to be *bound*.  The new method's :attr:`~method."
"__func__` attribute is the original function object."
msgstr ""
"當實例方法物件是透過類別的某個實例，從類別中取得使用者定義的\\ :ref:`函式物"
"件 <user-defined-funcs>`\\ 而建立時，其 :attr:`~method.__self__` 屬性即為該實"
"例，而該方法物件被稱為\\ *已繫結* (bound)。新方法的 :attr:`~method.__func__` "
"屬性是原始的函式物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:771
msgid ""
"When an instance method object is created by retrieving a :class:"
"`classmethod` object from a class or instance, its :attr:`~method.__self__` "
"attribute is the class itself, and its :attr:`~method.__func__` attribute is "
"the function object underlying the class method."
msgstr ""
"當實例方法物件是透過從類別或實例取得 :class:`classmethod` 物件而建立時，其 :"
"attr:`~method.__self__` 屬性為類別本身，而其 :attr:`~method.__func__` 屬性則"
"是該類別方法底層的函式物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:776
msgid ""
"When an instance method object is called, the underlying function (:attr:"
"`~method.__func__`) is called, inserting the class instance (:attr:`~method."
"__self__`) in front of the argument list.  For instance, when :class:`!C` is "
"a class which contains a definition for a function :meth:`!f`, and ``x`` is "
"an instance of :class:`!C`, calling ``x.f(1)`` is equivalent to calling ``C."
"f(x, 1)``."
msgstr ""
"呼叫實例方法物件時，會呼叫底層函式 (:attr:`~method.__func__`)，並將類別實例 "
"(:attr:`~method.__self__`) 插入到引數列表的最前面。舉例來說，當 :class:`!C` "
"是一個包含函式 :meth:`!f` 定義的類別，且 ``x`` 是 :class:`!C` 的實例時，呼叫 "
"``x.f(1)`` 等同於呼叫 ``C.f(x, 1)``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:783
msgid ""
"When an instance method object is derived from a :class:`classmethod` "
"object, the \"class instance\" stored in :attr:`~method.__self__` will "
"actually be the class itself, so that calling either ``x.f(1)`` or ``C."
"f(1)`` is equivalent to calling ``f(C,1)`` where ``f`` is the underlying "
"function."
msgstr ""
"當實例方法物件衍生自 :class:`classmethod` 物件時，儲存在 :attr:`~method."
"__self__` 中的「類別實例」實際上會是類別本身，因此呼叫 ``x.f(1)`` 或 ``C."
"f(1)`` 都等同於呼叫 ``f(C,1)``，其中 ``f`` 是底層函式。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:788
msgid ""
"It is important to note that user-defined functions which are attributes of "
"a class instance are not converted to bound methods; this *only* happens "
"when the function is an attribute of the class."
msgstr ""
"需要特別注意的是，作為類別實例屬性的使用者定義函式不會被轉換為已繫結方法；這"
"\\ *只*\\ 會在函式是類別的屬性時發生。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:795
msgid "Generator functions"
msgstr "產生器函式"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:801
msgid ""
"A function or method which contains a :keyword:`yield` expression (see "
"section :ref:`yieldexpr`) is called a :dfn:`generator function`.  Such a "
"function, when called, always returns an :term:`iterator` object which can "
"be used to execute the body of the function:  calling the iterator's :meth:"
"`iterator.__next__` method will cause the function to execute until it "
"provides a value using the :keyword:`!yield` expression.  When the function "
"executes a :keyword:`return` statement or falls off the end, a :exc:"
"`StopIteration` exception is raised and the iterator will have reached the "
"end of the set of values to be returned."
msgstr ""
"包含 :keyword:`yield` 運算式（請見 :ref:`yieldexpr`\\ 章節）的函式或方法稱為"
"\\ :dfn:`產生器函式`。這樣的函式在被呼叫時，總是會回傳一個可用來執行函式主體"
"的\\ :term:`疊代器 <iterator>`\\ 物件：呼叫該疊代器的 :meth:`iterator."
"__next__` 方法會使函式執行，直到它使用 :keyword:`!yield` 運算式提供一個值為"
"止。當函式執行 :keyword:`return` 陳述式或執行到結尾時，會引發 :exc:"
"`StopIteration` 例外，且該疊代器將會到達要回傳之值集合的結尾。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:813
msgid "Coroutine functions"
msgstr "Coroutine（協程）函式"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:818
msgid ""
"A function or method which is defined using :keyword:`async def` is called "
"a :dfn:`coroutine function`.  Such a function, when called, returns a :term:"
"`coroutine` object.  It may contain :keyword:`await` expressions, as well "
"as :keyword:`async with` and :keyword:`async for` statements. See also the :"
"ref:`coroutine-objects` section."
msgstr ""
"使用 :keyword:`async def` 定義的函式或方法稱為\\ :dfn:`協程函式`。這樣的函式"
"在被呼叫時會回傳一個\\ :term:`協程 <coroutine>`\\ 物件。它可以包含 :keyword:"
"`await` 運算式，以及 :keyword:`async with` 和 :keyword:`async for` 陳述式。另"
"請參閱\\ :ref:`coroutine-objects`\\ 章節。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:826
msgid "Asynchronous generator functions"
msgstr "非同步產生器函式"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:832
msgid ""
"A function or method which is defined using :keyword:`async def` and which "
"contains a :keyword:`yield` expression is called a :dfn:`asynchronous "
"generator function`.  Such a function, when called, returns an :term:"
"`asynchronous iterator` object which can be used in an :keyword:`async for` "
"statement to execute the body of the function."
msgstr ""
"使用 :keyword:`async def` 定義且包含 :keyword:`yield` 運算式的函式或方法稱為"
"\\ :dfn:`非同步產生器函式`。這樣的函式在被呼叫時會回傳一個\\ :term:`非同步疊"
"代器 <asynchronous iterator>`\\ 物件，可在 :keyword:`async for` 陳述式中用來"
"執行函式主體。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:838
msgid ""
"Calling the asynchronous iterator's :meth:`aiterator.__anext__ <object."
"__anext__>` method will return an :term:`awaitable` which when awaited will "
"execute until it provides a value using the :keyword:`yield` expression.  "
"When the function executes an empty :keyword:`return` statement or falls off "
"the end, a :exc:`StopAsyncIteration` exception is raised and the "
"asynchronous iterator will have reached the end of the set of values to be "
"yielded."
msgstr ""
"呼叫非同步疊代器的 :meth:`aiterator.__anext__ <object.__anext__>` 方法會回傳"
"一個\\ :term:`可等待物件 <awaitable>`，該物件在被等待時會執行到使用 :keyword:"
"`yield` 運算式提供一個值為止。當函式執行空的 :keyword:`return` 陳述式或執行到"
"結尾時，會引發 :exc:`StopAsyncIteration` 例外，且該非同步疊代器將會到達要產生"
"之值集合的結尾。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:851
msgid "Built-in functions"
msgstr "內建函式"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:858
msgid ""
"A built-in function object is a wrapper around a C function.  Examples of "
"built-in functions are :func:`len` and :func:`math.sin` (:mod:`math` is a "
"standard built-in module). The number and type of the arguments are "
"determined by the C function. Special read-only attributes:"
msgstr ""
"一個內建函式物件是一個 C 函式的 wrapper。內建函式的範例有 :func:`len` 和 :"
"func:`math.sin`\\ （\\ :mod:`math` 是一個標準的內建模組）。內建函式的引數數量"
"與其型別由其包裝的 C 函式所決定。特殊唯讀屬性："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:863
msgid ""
":attr:`!__doc__` is the function's documentation string, or ``None`` if "
"unavailable. See :attr:`function.__doc__`."
msgstr ""
":attr:`!__doc__` 是函式的文件字串，若不可用則為 ``None``。請見 :attr:"
"`function.__doc__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:865
msgid ""
":attr:`!__name__` is the function's name. See :attr:`function.__name__`."
msgstr ":attr:`!__name__` 是函式的名稱。請見 :attr:`function.__name__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:866
msgid ""
":attr:`!__self__` is the module object the function was defined in or "
"``None`` if unavailable."
msgstr ":attr:`!__self__` 是定義該函式的模組物件，若不可用則為 ``None``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:868
msgid ""
":attr:`!__module__` is the name of the module the function was defined in or "
"``None`` if unavailable. See :attr:`function.__module__`."
msgstr ""
":attr:`!__module__` 是定義該函式的模組名稱，若不可用則為 ``None``。請見 :"
"attr:`function.__module__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:876
msgid "Built-in methods"
msgstr "內建方法"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:883
msgid ""
"This is really a different disguise of a built-in function, this time "
"containing an object passed to the C function as an implicit extra "
"argument.  An example of a built-in method is ``alist.append()``, assuming "
"*alist* is a list object. In this case, the special read-only attribute :"
"attr:`!__self__` is set to the object denoted by *alist*. (The attribute has "
"the same semantics as it does with :attr:`other instance methods <method."
"__self__>`.)"
msgstr ""
"這實際上是內建函式的另一種偽裝形式，只是這次包含了一個作為隱含額外引數傳給 C "
"函式的物件。內建方法的一個例子是 ``alist.append()``，假設 *alist* 是一個串列"
"物件。在這種情況下，特殊唯讀屬性 :attr:`!__self__` 會被設為 *alist* 所指的物"
"件。（該屬性的語意與它在\\ :attr:`其他實例方法 <method.__self__>`\\ 中相"
"同。）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:893
msgid "Classes"
msgstr "類別"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:895
msgid ""
"Classes are callable.  These objects normally act as factories for new "
"instances of themselves, but variations are possible for class types that "
"override :meth:`~object.__new__`.  The arguments of the call are passed to :"
"meth:`!__new__` and, in the typical case, to :meth:`~object.__init__` to "
"initialize the new instance."
msgstr ""
"類別是可呼叫的。這些物件通常作為建立自身新實例的工廠，但覆寫了 :meth:"
"`~object.__new__` 的類別型別可能會有不同的變化。呼叫時的引數會被傳給 :meth:`!"
"__new__`，並在典型情況下傳給 :meth:`~object.__init__` 以初始化新的實例。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:903
msgid "Class Instances"
msgstr "類別實例"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:905
msgid ""
"Instances of arbitrary classes can be made callable by defining a :meth:"
"`~object.__call__` method in their class."
msgstr ""
"任意類別的實例都可以透過在其類別中定義 :meth:`~object.__call__` 方法而成為可"
"呼叫的。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:912
msgid "Modules"
msgstr "模組"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:918
msgid ""
"Modules are a basic organizational unit of Python code, and are created by "
"the :ref:`import system <importsystem>` as invoked either by the :keyword:"
"`import` statement, or by calling functions such as :func:`importlib."
"import_module` and built-in :func:`__import__`.  A module object has a "
"namespace implemented by a :class:`dictionary <dict>` object (this is the "
"dictionary referenced by the :attr:`~function.__globals__` attribute of "
"functions defined in the module).  Attribute references are translated to "
"lookups in this dictionary, e.g., ``m.x`` is equivalent to ``m."
"__dict__[\"x\"]``. A module object does not contain the code object used to "
"initialize the module (since it isn't needed once the initialization is "
"done)."
msgstr ""
"模組是 Python 程式碼的基本組織單位，由\\ :ref:`引入系統 <importsystem>`\\ 建"
"立，而引入系統可以透過 :keyword:`import` 陳述式叫用，或透過呼叫 :func:"
"`importlib.import_module` 與內建的 :func:`__import__` 等函式叫用。模組物件有"
"一個以\\ :class:`字典 <dict>`\\ 物件實作的命名空間（這就是在該模組中定義之函"
"式的 :attr:`~function.__globals__` 屬性所參照的字典）。屬性參照會被轉譯為在此"
"字典中的查找，例如 ``m.x`` 等同於 ``m.__dict__[\"x\"]``。模組物件不包含用來初"
"始化模組的程式碼物件（因為初始化完成後就不再需要它）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:931
msgid ""
"Attribute assignment updates the module's namespace dictionary, e.g., ``m.x "
"= 1`` is equivalent to ``m.__dict__[\"x\"] = 1``."
msgstr ""
"屬性賦值會更新模組的命名空間字典，例如 ``m.x = 1`` 等同於 ``m."
"__dict__[\"x\"] = 1``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:950
msgid "Import-related attributes on module objects"
msgstr "模組物件上與引入相關的屬性"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:952
msgid ""
"Module objects have the following attributes that relate to the :ref:`import "
"system <importsystem>`. When a module is created using the machinery "
"associated with the import system, these attributes are filled in based on "
"the module's :term:`spec <module spec>`, before the :term:`loader` executes "
"and loads the module."
msgstr ""
"模組物件具有以下與\\ :ref:`引入系統 <importsystem>`\\ 相關的屬性。當模組是使"
"用與引入系統相關的機制建立時，這些屬性會在\\ :term:`載入器 <loader>`\\ 執行並"
"載入模組之前，根據模組的\\ :term:`規格 <module spec>`\\ 填入。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:958
msgid ""
"To create a module dynamically rather than using the import system, it's "
"recommended to use :func:`importlib.util.module_from_spec`, which will set "
"the various import-controlled attributes to appropriate values. It's also "
"possible to use the :class:`types.ModuleType` constructor to create modules "
"directly, but this technique is more error-prone, as most attributes must be "
"manually set on the module object after it has been created when using this "
"approach."
msgstr ""
"若要動態建立模組而非使用引入系統，建議使用 :func:`importlib.util."
"module_from_spec`，它會將各種由引入控制的屬性設為適當的值。也可以使用 :class:"
"`types.ModuleType` 建構函式直接建立模組，但這種技巧較容易出錯，因為使用這種方"
"式時，大部分屬性都必須在模組物件建立後手動設定。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:968
msgid ""
"With the exception of :attr:`~module.__name__`, it is **strongly** "
"recommended that you rely on :attr:`~module.__spec__` and its attributes "
"instead of any of the other individual attributes listed in this subsection. "
"Note that updating an attribute on :attr:`!__spec__` will not update the "
"corresponding attribute on the module itself:"
msgstr ""
"除了 :attr:`~module.__name__` 之外，**強烈**\\ 建議你依賴 :attr:`~module."
"__spec__` 及其屬性，而不是本小節列出的其他任何個別屬性。請注意，更新 :attr:`!"
"__spec__` 上的屬性並不會更新模組本身對應的屬性："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:974
msgid ""
">>> import typing\n"
">>> typing.__name__, typing.__spec__.name\n"
"('typing', 'typing')\n"
">>> typing.__spec__.name = 'spelling'\n"
">>> typing.__name__, typing.__spec__.name\n"
"('typing', 'spelling')\n"
">>> typing.__name__ = 'keyboard_smashing'\n"
">>> typing.__name__, typing.__spec__.name\n"
"('keyboard_smashing', 'spelling')"
msgstr ""
">>> import typing\n"
">>> typing.__name__, typing.__spec__.name\n"
"('typing', 'typing')\n"
">>> typing.__spec__.name = 'spelling'\n"
">>> typing.__name__, typing.__spec__.name\n"
"('typing', 'spelling')\n"
">>> typing.__name__ = 'keyboard_smashing'\n"
">>> typing.__name__, typing.__spec__.name\n"
"('keyboard_smashing', 'spelling')"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:988
msgid ""
"The name used to uniquely identify the module in the import system. For a "
"directly executed module, this will be set to ``\"__main__\"``."
msgstr ""
"在引入系統中用來唯一識別該模組的名稱。對於直接執行的模組，這會被設為 "
"``\"__main__\"``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:991
msgid ""
"This attribute must be set to the fully qualified name of the module. It is "
"expected to match the value of :attr:`module.__spec__.name <importlib."
"machinery.ModuleSpec.name>`."
msgstr ""
"此屬性必須設為模組的完整限定名稱，且其值應與 :attr:`module.__spec__.name "
"<importlib.machinery.ModuleSpec.name>` 相符。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:997
msgid "A record of the module's import-system-related state."
msgstr "模組與引入系統相關之狀態的紀錄。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:999
msgid ""
"Set to the :class:`module spec <importlib.machinery.ModuleSpec>` that was "
"used when importing the module. See :ref:`module-specs` for more details."
msgstr ""
"設為引入該模組時所使用的\\ :class:`模組規格 <importlib.machinery."
"ModuleSpec>`。更多細節請見\\ :ref:`module-specs`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1006
msgid "The :term:`package` a module belongs to."
msgstr "模組所屬的\\ :term:`套件 <package>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1008
msgid ""
"If the module is top-level (that is, not a part of any specific package) "
"then the attribute should be set to ``''`` (the empty string). Otherwise, it "
"should be set to the name of the module's package (which can be equal to :"
"attr:`module.__name__` if the module itself is a package). See :pep:`366` "
"for further details."
msgstr ""
"如果模組是頂層的（也就是不屬於任何特定套件），則此屬性應設為 ``''``\\ （空字"
"串）。否則應設為模組所屬套件的名稱（如果模組本身就是套件，則可以等於 :attr:"
"`module.__name__`）。更多細節請見 :pep:`366`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1014
msgid ""
"This attribute is used instead of :attr:`~module.__name__` to calculate "
"explicit relative imports for main modules. It defaults to ``None`` for "
"modules created dynamically using the :class:`types.ModuleType` constructor; "
"use :func:`importlib.util.module_from_spec` instead to ensure the attribute "
"is set to a :class:`str`."
msgstr ""
"此屬性用來取代 :attr:`~module.__name__`，為主模組計算明確的相對引入。對於使"
"用 :class:`types.ModuleType` 建構函式動態建立的模組，此屬性預設為 ``None``；"
"請改用 :func:`importlib.util.module_from_spec` 以確保此屬性被設為 :class:"
"`str`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1020
msgid ""
"It is **strongly** recommended that you use :attr:`module.__spec__.parent "
"<importlib.machinery.ModuleSpec.parent>` instead of :attr:`!module."
"__package__`. :attr:`__package__` is now only used as a fallback if :attr:`!"
"__spec__.parent` is not set, and this fallback path is deprecated."
msgstr ""
"**強烈**\\ 建議你使用 :attr:`module.__spec__.parent <importlib.machinery."
"ModuleSpec.parent>` 而非 :attr:`!module.__package__`。:attr:`__package__` 現"
"在只會在 :attr:`!__spec__.parent` 未設定時作為後備使用，且此後備路徑已被棄"
"用。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1026 ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1067
msgid ""
"This attribute now defaults to ``None`` for modules created dynamically "
"using the :class:`types.ModuleType` constructor. Previously the attribute "
"was optional."
msgstr ""
"對於使用 :class:`types.ModuleType` 建構函式動態建立的模組，此屬性現在預設為 "
"``None``。先前此屬性是可選的。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1031
msgid ""
"The value of :attr:`!__package__` is expected to be the same as :attr:"
"`__spec__.parent <importlib.machinery.ModuleSpec.parent>`. :attr:"
"`__package__` is now only used as a fallback during import resolution if :"
"attr:`!__spec__.parent` is not defined."
msgstr ""
":attr:`!__package__` 的值預期會與 :attr:`__spec__.parent <importlib."
"machinery.ModuleSpec.parent>` 相同。:attr:`__package__` 現在只會在 :attr:`!"
"__spec__.parent` 未定義時，於引入解析期間作為後備使用。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1037
msgid ""
":exc:`ImportWarning` is raised if an import resolution falls back to :attr:`!"
"__package__` instead of :attr:`__spec__.parent <importlib.machinery."
"ModuleSpec.parent>`."
msgstr ""
"如果引入解析退回使用 :attr:`!__package__` 而非 :attr:`__spec__.parent "
"<importlib.machinery.ModuleSpec.parent>`，則會引發 :exc:`ImportWarning`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1042
msgid ""
"Raise :exc:`DeprecationWarning` instead of :exc:`ImportWarning` when falling "
"back to :attr:`!__package__` during import resolution."
msgstr ""
"在引入解析期間退回使用 :attr:`!__package__` 時，改為引發 :exc:"
"`DeprecationWarning` 而非 :exc:`ImportWarning`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1046
msgid ""
":attr:`!__package__` will cease to be set or taken into consideration by the "
"import system or standard library."
msgstr "引入系統或標準函式庫將不再設定或納入考量 :attr:`!__package__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1052
msgid ""
"The :term:`loader` object that the import machinery used to load the module."
msgstr "引入機制用來載入該模組的\\ :term:`載入器 <loader>`\\ 物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1054
msgid ""
"This attribute is mostly useful for introspection, but can be used for "
"additional loader-specific functionality, for example getting data "
"associated with a loader."
msgstr ""
"此屬性主要用於內省 (introspection)，但也可用於特定於載入器的額外功能，例如取"
"得與載入器相關聯的資料。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1058
msgid ""
":attr:`!__loader__` defaults to ``None`` for modules created dynamically "
"using the :class:`types.ModuleType` constructor; use :func:`importlib.util."
"module_from_spec` instead to ensure the attribute is set to a :term:`loader` "
"object."
msgstr ""
"對於使用 :class:`types.ModuleType` 建構函式動態建立的模組，:attr:`!"
"__loader__` 預設為 ``None``；請改用 :func:`importlib.util.module_from_spec` "
"以確保此屬性被設為\\ :term:`載入器 <loader>`\\ 物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1063
msgid ""
"It is **strongly** recommended that you use :attr:`module.__spec__.loader "
"<importlib.machinery.ModuleSpec.loader>` instead of :attr:`!module."
"__loader__`."
msgstr ""
"**強烈**\\ 建議你使用 :attr:`module.__spec__.loader <importlib.machinery."
"ModuleSpec.loader>` 而非 :attr:`!module.__loader__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1072
msgid ""
"Setting :attr:`!__loader__` on a module while failing to set :attr:`!"
"__spec__.loader` is deprecated. In Python 3.16, :attr:`!__loader__` will "
"cease to be set or taken into consideration by the import system or the "
"standard library."
msgstr ""
"在模組上設定 :attr:`!__loader__` 而沒有設定 :attr:`!__spec__.loader` 的做法已"
"被棄用。在 Python 3.16 中，引入系統或標準函式庫將不再設定或納入考量 :attr:`!"
"__loader__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1080
msgid ""
"A (possibly empty) :term:`sequence` of strings enumerating the locations "
"where the package's submodules will be found. Non-package modules should not "
"have a :attr:`!__path__` attribute. See :ref:`package-path-rules` for more "
"details."
msgstr ""
"一個（可能為空的）字串\\ :term:`序列 <sequence>`，列舉可以找到該套件子模組的"
"位置。非套件模組不應具有 :attr:`!__path__` 屬性。更多細節請見\\ :ref:"
"`package-path-rules`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1085
msgid ""
"It is **strongly** recommended that you use :attr:`module.__spec__."
"submodule_search_locations <importlib.machinery.ModuleSpec."
"submodule_search_locations>` instead of :attr:`!module.__path__`."
msgstr ""
"**強烈**\\ 建議你使用 :attr:`module.__spec__.submodule_search_locations "
"<importlib.machinery.ModuleSpec.submodule_search_locations>` 而非 :attr:`!"
"module.__path__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1091
msgid ""
":attr:`!__file__` is an optional attribute that may or may not be set. Both "
"attributes should be a :class:`str` when they are available."
msgstr ""
":attr:`!__file__` 是一個可選屬性，可能有設定也可能沒有。兩個屬性在可用時都應"
"該是 :class:`str`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1095
msgid ""
"An optional attribute, :attr:`!__file__` indicates the pathname of the file "
"from which the module was loaded (if loaded from a file), or the pathname of "
"the shared library file for extension modules loaded dynamically from a "
"shared library. It might be missing for certain types of modules, such as C "
"modules that are statically linked into the interpreter, and the :ref:"
"`import system <importsystem>` may opt to leave it unset if it has no "
"semantic meaning (for example, a module loaded from a database)."
msgstr ""
"作為可選屬性，:attr:`!__file__` 表示載入該模組的檔案路徑名稱（如果是從檔案載"
"入），或者對於從共享函式庫動態載入的擴充模組而言，則是該共享函式庫檔案的路徑"
"名稱。某些種類的模組可能沒有此屬性，例如靜態連結到直譯器中的 C 模組；而若此屬"
"性沒有語意上的意義（例如從資料庫載入的模組），:ref:`引入系統 "
"<importsystem>`\\ 也可以選擇不設定它。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1103
msgid ""
"The ``__cached__`` attribute is no longer set on modules or taken into "
"consideration by the import system or standard library."
msgstr ""
"模組上不再設定 ``__cached__`` 屬性，引入系統或標準函式庫也不再將其納入考量。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1108
msgid "Other writable attributes on module objects"
msgstr "模組物件的其他可寫入屬性"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1110
msgid ""
"As well as the import-related attributes listed above, module objects also "
"have the following writable attributes:"
msgstr "除了上述與引入相關的屬性之外，模組物件還具有以下可寫入屬性："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1115
msgid ""
"The module's documentation string, or ``None`` if unavailable. See also: :"
"attr:`__doc__ attributes <definition.__doc__>`."
msgstr ""
"模組的文件字串，若不可用則為 ``None``。另請參閱：:attr:`__doc__ 屬性 "
"<definition.__doc__>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1120
msgid ""
"A dictionary containing :term:`variable annotations <variable annotation>` "
"collected during module body execution.  For best practices on working with :"
"attr:`!__annotations__`, see :mod:`annotationlib`."
msgstr ""
"一個包含在模組主體執行期間所收集之\\ :term:`變數註釋 <variable "
"annotation>`\\ 的字典。關於使用 :attr:`!__annotations__` 的最佳實踐，請參閱 :"
"mod:`annotationlib`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1130
msgid ""
"The :term:`annotate function` for this module, or ``None`` if the module has "
"no annotations. See also: :attr:`~object.__annotate__` attributes."
msgstr ""
"此模組的\\ :term:`註釋函式 <annotate function>`，若模組沒有註釋則為 "
"``None``。另請參閱：:attr:`~object.__annotate__` 屬性。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1137
msgid ""
"A container (an object implementing :meth:`~object.__contains__`) of fully "
"qualified module name strings.  When defined at module scope, any regular :"
"keyword:`import` statement in that module whose target module name appears "
"in this container is treated as a :ref:`lazy import <lazy-imports>`, as if "
"the :keyword:`lazy` keyword had been used.  Imports inside functions, class "
"bodies, or :keyword:`try`/:keyword:`except`/:keyword:`finally` blocks are "
"unaffected."
msgstr ""
"一個由完整限定模組名稱字串所組成的容器（實作了 :meth:`~object.__contains__` "
"的物件）。在模組作用域中定義時，該模組中任何目標模組名稱出現在此容器內的一"
"般 :keyword:`import` 陳述式，都會被視為\\ :ref:`惰性引入 (lazy import) <lazy-"
"imports>`，就如同使用了 :keyword:`lazy` 關鍵字一樣。函式、類別主體或 :"
"keyword:`try`/:keyword:`except`/:keyword:`finally` 區塊內的引入則不受影響。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1145
msgid "See :ref:`lazy-modules-compat` for details and examples."
msgstr "細節與範例請見 :ref:`lazy-modules-compat`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1150
msgid "Module dictionaries"
msgstr "模組字典"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1152
msgid "Module objects also have the following special read-only attribute:"
msgstr "模組物件還具有以下特殊唯讀屬性："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1157
msgid ""
"The module's namespace as a dictionary object. Uniquely among the attributes "
"listed here, :attr:`!__dict__` cannot be accessed as a global variable from "
"within a module; it can only be accessed as an attribute on module objects."
msgstr ""
"以字典物件表示的模組命名空間。在此列出的屬性中，:attr:`!__dict__` 是唯一無法"
"在模組內部作為全域變數存取的屬性；它只能作為模組物件上的屬性來存取。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1163
msgid ""
"Because of the way CPython clears module dictionaries, the module dictionary "
"will be cleared when the module falls out of scope even if the dictionary "
"still has live references.  To avoid this, copy the dictionary or keep the "
"module around while using its dictionary directly."
msgstr ""
"由於 CPython 清除模組字典的方式，當模組離開作用域時，即使模組字典仍有存活的參"
"照，它也會被清除。為了避免這種情況，請複製該字典，或在直接使用模組字典的期間"
"保持該模組存活。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1172
msgid "Custom classes"
msgstr "自訂類別"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1174
msgid ""
"Custom class types are typically created by class definitions (see section :"
"ref:`class`).  A class has a namespace implemented by a dictionary object. "
"Class attribute references are translated to lookups in this dictionary, e."
"g., ``C.x`` is translated to ``C.__dict__[\"x\"]`` (although there are a "
"number of hooks which allow for other means of locating attributes). When "
"the attribute name is not found there, the attribute search continues in the "
"base classes. This search of the base classes uses the C3 method resolution "
"order which behaves correctly even in the presence of 'diamond' inheritance "
"structures where there are multiple inheritance paths leading back to a "
"common ancestor. Additional details on the C3 MRO used by Python can be "
"found at :ref:`python_2.3_mro`."
msgstr ""
"自訂類別型別通常由類別定義建立（請見\\ :ref:`class`\\ 章節）。類別有一個以字"
"典物件實作的命名空間。類別屬性參照會被轉譯為在此字典中的查找，例如 ``C.x`` 會"
"被轉譯為 ``C.__dict__[\"x\"]``\\ （不過有許多掛鉤 (hook) 允許以其他方式來定位"
"屬性）。當在該處找不到屬性名稱時，屬性搜尋會繼續在基底類別中進行。這種對基底"
"類別的搜尋使用 C3 方法解析順序，即使存在「菱形」繼承結構（有多條繼承路徑通往"
"同一個共同祖先），它的行為也是正確的。關於 Python 所使用之 C3 MRO 的更多細"
"節，請參閱 :ref:`python_2.3_mro`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1195
msgid ""
"When a class attribute reference (for class :class:`!C`, say) would yield a "
"class method object, it is transformed into an instance method object whose :"
"attr:`~method.__self__` attribute is :class:`!C`. When it would yield a :"
"class:`staticmethod` object, it is transformed into the object wrapped by "
"the static method object. See section :ref:`descriptors` for another way in "
"which attributes retrieved from a class may differ from those actually "
"contained in its :attr:`~object.__dict__`."
msgstr ""
"當類別屬性參照（例如對於類別 :class:`!C`）會產生一個類別方法物件時，它會被轉"
"換為一個 :attr:`~method.__self__` 屬性為 :class:`!C` 的實例方法物件。當它會產"
"生一個 :class:`staticmethod` 物件時，它會被轉換為由該靜態方法物件所包裝的物"
"件。關於從類別取得的屬性可能與實際包含在其 :attr:`~object.__dict__` 中的屬性"
"有所不同的另一種情況，請見\\ :ref:`descriptors`\\ 章節。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1206
msgid ""
"Class attribute assignments update the class's dictionary, never the "
"dictionary of a base class."
msgstr "類別屬性賦值會更新該類別的字典，而絕不會更新基底類別的字典。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1211
msgid ""
"A class object can be called (see above) to yield a class instance (see "
"below)."
msgstr "類別物件可以被呼叫（見上文）以產生一個類別實例（見下文）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1214 ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1390
msgid "Special attributes"
msgstr "特殊屬性"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1236
msgid ""
"The class's name. See also: :attr:`__name__ attributes <definition."
"__name__>`."
msgstr "類別的名稱。另請參閱：:attr:`__name__ 屬性 <definition.__name__>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1240
msgid ""
"The class's :term:`qualified name`. See also: :attr:`__qualname__ attributes "
"<definition.__qualname__>`."
msgstr ""
"類別的\\ :term:`限定名稱 <qualified name>`。另請參閱：:attr:`__qualname__ 屬"
"性 <definition.__qualname__>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1244
msgid "The name of the module in which the class was defined."
msgstr "定義該類別的模組名稱。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1247
msgid ""
"A :class:`mapping proxy <types.MappingProxyType>` providing a read-only view "
"of the class's namespace. See also: :attr:`__dict__ attributes <object."
"__dict__>`."
msgstr ""
"一個提供類別命名空間唯讀檢視的\\ :class:`對映代理 <types.MappingProxyType>`。"
"另請參閱：:attr:`__dict__ 屬性 <object.__dict__>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1252
msgid ""
"A :class:`tuple` containing the class's bases. In most cases, for a class "
"defined as ``class X(A, B, C)``, ``X.__bases__`` will be exactly equal to "
"``(A, B, C)``."
msgstr ""
"一個包含類別之基底類別的 :class:`tuple`。在大多數情況下，對於定義為 ``class "
"X(A, B, C)`` 的類別，``X.__bases__`` 會完全等於 ``(A, B, C)``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1259
msgid ""
"The single base class in the inheritance chain that is responsible for the "
"memory layout of instances. This attribute corresponds to :c:member:"
"`~PyTypeObject.tp_base` at the C level."
msgstr ""
"繼承鏈中負責實例記憶體佈局的單一基底類別。此屬性對應於 C 層級的 :c:member:"
"`~PyTypeObject.tp_base`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1264
msgid ""
"The class's documentation string, or ``None`` if undefined. Not inherited by "
"subclasses."
msgstr "類別的文件字串，若未定義則為 ``None``。不會被子類別繼承。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1268
msgid ""
"A dictionary containing :term:`variable annotations <variable annotation>` "
"collected during class body execution. See also: :attr:`__annotations__ "
"attributes <object.__annotations__>`."
msgstr ""
"一個包含在類別主體執行期間所收集之\\ :term:`變數註釋 <variable "
"annotation>`\\ 的字典。另請參閱：:attr:`__annotations__ 屬性 <object."
"__annotations__>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1273
msgid ""
"For best practices on working with :attr:`~object.__annotations__`, please "
"see :mod:`annotationlib`. Use :func:`annotationlib.get_annotations` instead "
"of accessing this attribute directly."
msgstr ""
"關於使用 :attr:`~object.__annotations__` 的最佳實踐，請參閱 :mod:"
"`annotationlib`。請使用 :func:`annotationlib.get_annotations`，而不要直接存取"
"此屬性。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1280
msgid ""
"Accessing the :attr:`!__annotations__` attribute directly on a class object "
"may return annotations for the wrong class, specifically in certain cases "
"where the class, its base class, or a metaclass is defined under ``from "
"__future__ import annotations``. See :pep:`749 <749#pep749-metaclasses>` for "
"details."
msgstr ""
"直接在類別物件上存取 :attr:`!__annotations__` 屬性可能會回傳錯誤類別的註釋，"
"特別是在類別、其基底類別或元類別是在 ``from __future__ import annotations`` "
"下定義的某些情況中。詳情請見 :pep:`749 <749#pep749-metaclasses>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1286
msgid ""
"This attribute does not exist on certain builtin classes. On user-defined "
"classes without ``__annotations__``, it is an empty dictionary."
msgstr ""
"此屬性在某些內建類別上不存在。在沒有 ``__annotations__`` 的使用者定義類別上，"
"它是一個空字典。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1295
msgid ""
"The :term:`annotate function` for this class, or ``None`` if the class has "
"no annotations. See also: :attr:`__annotate__ attributes <object."
"__annotate__>`."
msgstr ""
"此類別的\\ :term:`註釋函式 <annotate function>`，若類別沒有註釋則為 "
"``None``。另請參閱：:attr:`__annotate__ 屬性 <object.__annotate__>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1302
msgid ""
"A :class:`tuple` containing the :ref:`type parameters <type-params>` of a :"
"ref:`generic class <generic-classes>`."
msgstr ""
"一個 :class:`tuple`，包含\\ :ref:`泛型類別 <generic-classes>`\\ 的\\ :ref:`型"
"別參數 <type-params>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1308
msgid ""
"A :class:`tuple` containing names of attributes of this class which are "
"assigned through ``self.X`` from any function in its body."
msgstr ""
"一個 :class:`tuple`，包含此類別主體中任何函式透過 ``self.X`` 所指派之屬性的名"
"稱。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1314
msgid ""
"The line number of the first line of the class definition, including "
"decorators. Setting the :attr:`~type.__module__` attribute removes the :attr:"
"`!__firstlineno__` item from the type's dictionary."
msgstr ""
"類別定義第一列的列號，包含裝飾器。設定 :attr:`~type.__module__` 屬性會從型別"
"的字典中移除 :attr:`!__firstlineno__` 項目。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1322
msgid ""
"The :class:`tuple` of classes that are considered when looking for base "
"classes during method resolution."
msgstr "在方法解析期間尋找基底類別時所考慮之類別的 :class:`tuple`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1327
msgid "Special methods"
msgstr "特殊方法"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1329
msgid ""
"In addition to the special attributes described above, all Python classes "
"also have the following two methods available:"
msgstr "除了上述特殊屬性之外，所有 Python 類別還具有以下兩個可用的方法："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1334
msgid ""
"This method can be overridden by a metaclass to customize the method "
"resolution order for its instances.  It is called at class instantiation, "
"and its result is stored in :attr:`~type.__mro__`."
msgstr ""
"此方法可以被元類別覆寫，以自訂其實例的方法解析順序。它會在類別實例化時被呼"
"叫，其結果會儲存在 :attr:`~type.__mro__` 中。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1340
msgid ""
"Each class keeps a list of weak references to its immediate subclasses. This "
"method returns a list of all those references still alive. The list is in "
"definition order. Example:"
msgstr ""
"每個類別都會保存一個由指向其直接子類別之弱參照所組成的串列。此方法會回傳所有"
"仍然存活之參照所組成的串列。該串列依定義順序排列。範例："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1344
msgid ""
">>> class A: pass\n"
">>> class B(A): pass\n"
">>> A.__subclasses__()\n"
"[<class 'B'>]"
msgstr ""
">>> class A: pass\n"
">>> class B(A): pass\n"
">>> A.__subclasses__()\n"
"[<class 'B'>]"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1352
msgid "Class instances"
msgstr "類別實例"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1360
msgid ""
"A class instance is created by calling a class object (see above).  A class "
"instance has a namespace implemented as a dictionary which is the first "
"place in which attribute references are searched.  When an attribute is not "
"found there, and the instance's class has an attribute by that name, the "
"search continues with the class attributes.  If a class attribute is found "
"that is a user-defined function object, it is transformed into an instance "
"method object whose :attr:`~method.__self__` attribute is the instance.  "
"Static method and class method objects are also transformed; see above under "
"\"Classes\".  See section :ref:`descriptors` for another way in which "
"attributes of a class retrieved via its instances may differ from the "
"objects actually stored in the class's :attr:`~object.__dict__`.  If no "
"class attribute is found, and the object's class has a :meth:`~object."
"__getattr__` method, that is called to satisfy the lookup."
msgstr ""
"類別實例是透過呼叫類別物件（見上文）建立的。類別實例有一個以字典實作的命名空"
"間，這是搜尋屬性參照的第一個地方。當在該處找不到屬性，且實例的類別具有該名稱"
"的屬性時，搜尋會繼續在類別屬性中進行。如果找到的類別屬性是使用者定義函式物"
"件，它會被轉換為一個 :attr:`~method.__self__` 屬性為該實例的實例方法物件。靜"
"態方法與類別方法物件也會被轉換；請見上文「類別」中的說明。關於透過實例取得的"
"類別屬性可能與實際儲存在類別 :attr:`~object.__dict__` 中的物件有所不同的另一"
"種情況，請見\\ :ref:`descriptors`\\ 章節。如果找不到類別屬性，且物件的類別具"
"有 :meth:`~object.__getattr__` 方法，則會呼叫該方法來完成查找。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1376
msgid ""
"Attribute assignments and deletions update the instance's dictionary, never "
"a class's dictionary.  If the class has a :meth:`~object.__setattr__` or :"
"meth:`~object.__delattr__` method, this is called instead of updating the "
"instance dictionary directly."
msgstr ""
"屬性賦值與刪除會更新實例的字典，而絕不會更新類別的字典。如果類別具有 :meth:"
"`~object.__setattr__` 或 :meth:`~object.__delattr__` 方法，則會呼叫該方法，而"
"不是直接更新實例字典。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1386
msgid ""
"Class instances can pretend to be numbers, sequences, or mappings if they "
"have methods with certain special names.  See section :ref:`specialnames`."
msgstr ""
"如果類別實例具有某些特殊名稱的方法，它們就可以偽裝成數字、序列或對映。請見"
"\\ :ref:`specialnames`\\ 章節。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1398
msgid "The class to which a class instance belongs."
msgstr "類別實例所屬的類別。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1402
msgid ""
"A dictionary or other mapping object used to store an object's (writable) "
"attributes. Not all instances have a :attr:`!__dict__` attribute; see the "
"section on :ref:`slots` for more details."
msgstr ""
"用來儲存物件（可寫入）屬性的字典或其他對映物件。並非所有實例都有 :attr:`!"
"__dict__` 屬性；更多細節請見 :ref:`slots` 章節。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1408
msgid "I/O objects (also known as file objects)"
msgstr "I/O 物件（也稱為檔案物件）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1423
msgid ""
"A :term:`file object` represents an open file.  Various shortcuts are "
"available to create file objects: the :func:`open` built-in function, and "
"also :func:`os.popen`, :func:`os.fdopen`, and the :meth:`~socket.socket."
"makefile` method of socket objects (and perhaps by other functions or "
"methods provided by extension modules)."
msgstr ""
":term:`檔案物件 <file object>`\\ 代表一個開啟的檔案。有多種捷徑可以建立檔案物"
"件：內建函式 :func:`open`，以及 :func:`os.popen`、:func:`os.fdopen` 與 "
"socket 物件的 :meth:`~socket.socket.makefile` 方法（也可能是擴充模組所提供的"
"其他函式或方法）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1429
msgid ""
"File objects implement common methods, listed below, to simplify usage in "
"generic code. They are expected to be :ref:`context-managers`."
msgstr ""
"檔案物件實作了下列常見方法，以簡化在泛用程式碼中的使用。它們應為 :ref:"
"`context-managers`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1432
msgid ""
"The objects ``sys.stdin``, ``sys.stdout`` and ``sys.stderr`` are initialized "
"to file objects corresponding to the interpreter's standard input, output "
"and error streams; they are all open in text mode and therefore follow the "
"interface defined by the :class:`io.TextIOBase` abstract class."
msgstr ""
"物件 ``sys.stdin``、``sys.stdout`` 與 ``sys.stderr`` 會被初始化為對應直譯器標"
"準輸入、輸出與錯誤串流的檔案物件；它們都以文字模式開啟，因此遵循 :class:`io."
"TextIOBase` 抽象類別所定義的介面。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1440
msgid ""
"Retrieve up to *size* data from the file. As a convenience if *size* is "
"unspecified or -1 retrieve all data available."
msgstr ""
"從檔案中取得最多 *size* 的資料。為了方便起見，如果未指定 *size* 或其為 -1，則"
"取得所有可用的資料。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1445
msgid "Store *data* to the file."
msgstr "將 *data* 儲存到檔案中。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1449
msgid "Flush any buffers and close the underlying file."
msgstr "排清 (flush) 所有緩衝區並關閉底層檔案。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1453
msgid "Internal types"
msgstr "內部型別"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1459
msgid ""
"A few types used internally by the interpreter are exposed to the user. "
"Their definitions may change with future versions of the interpreter, but "
"they are mentioned here for completeness."
msgstr ""
"直譯器內部使用的少數型別會公開給使用者。它們的定義可能會隨著未來的直譯器版本"
"而改變，但為了完整起見，在此仍會提及。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1467
msgid "Code objects"
msgstr "程式碼物件"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1471
msgid ""
"Code objects represent *byte-compiled* executable Python code, or :term:"
"`bytecode`. The difference between a code object and a function object is "
"that the function object contains an explicit reference to the function's "
"globals (the module in which it was defined), while a code object contains "
"no context; also the default argument values are stored in the function "
"object, not in the code object (because they represent values calculated at "
"run-time).  Unlike function objects, code objects are immutable and contain "
"no references (directly or indirectly) to mutable objects."
msgstr ""
"程式碼物件代表\\ *位元組編譯* (byte-compiled) 的可執行 Python 程式碼，或稱"
"\\ :term:`位元組碼 <bytecode>`。程式碼物件與函式物件之間的差異在於，函式物件"
"包含對函式全域變數（即定義該函式的模組）的明確參照，而程式碼物件不包含任何情"
"境；此外，預設引數值是儲存在函式物件中，而不是程式碼物件中（因為它們代表在 "
"runtime 計算的值）。與函式物件不同，程式碼物件是不可變的，且不包含（直接或間"
"接）對可變物件的參照。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1504
msgid "The function name"
msgstr "函式名稱"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1507
msgid "The fully qualified function name"
msgstr "完整限定函式名稱"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1512
msgid ""
"The total number of positional :term:`parameters <parameter>` (including "
"positional-only parameters and parameters with default values) that the "
"function has"
msgstr ""
"函式所具有的位置\\ :term:`參數 <parameter>`\\ 總數（包括僅限位置參數與具有預"
"設值的參數）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1517
msgid ""
"The number of positional-only :term:`parameters <parameter>` (including "
"arguments with default values) that the function has"
msgstr ""
"函式所具有的僅限位置\\ :term:`參數 <parameter>`\\ 數量（包括具有預設值的引"
"數）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1521
msgid ""
"The number of keyword-only :term:`parameters <parameter>` (including "
"arguments with default values) that the function has"
msgstr ""
"函式所具有的僅限關鍵字\\ :term:`參數 <parameter>`\\ 數量（包括具有預設值的引"
"數）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1525
msgid ""
"The number of :ref:`local variables <naming>` used by the function "
"(including parameters)"
msgstr "函式所使用的\\ :ref:`區域變數 <naming>`\\ 數量（包括參數）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1529
msgid ""
"A :class:`tuple` containing the names of the local variables in the function "
"(starting with the parameter names)"
msgstr "一個包含函式中區域變數名稱的 :class:`tuple`\\ （以參數名稱開頭）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1533
msgid ""
"A :class:`tuple` containing the names of :ref:`local variables <naming>` "
"that are referenced from at least one :term:`nested scope` inside the "
"function"
msgstr ""
"一個 :class:`tuple`，包含函式內至少一個\\ :term:`巢狀作用域 <nested "
"scope>`\\ 所參照之\\ :ref:`區域變數 <naming>`\\ 的名稱"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1537
msgid ""
"A :class:`tuple` containing the names of :term:`free (closure) variables "
"<closure variable>` that a :term:`nested scope` references in an outer "
"scope. See also :attr:`function.__closure__`."
msgstr ""
"一個 :class:`tuple`，包含\\ :term:`巢狀作用域 <nested scope>`\\ 在外層作用域"
"中所參照之\\ :term:`自由（閉包）變數 <closure variable>`\\ 的名稱。另請參閱 :"
"attr:`function.__closure__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1541
msgid "Note: references to global and builtin names are *not* included."
msgstr "注意：對全域與內建名稱的參照\\ *不會*\\ 被包含在內。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1544
msgid ""
"A string representing the sequence of :term:`bytecode` instructions in the "
"function"
msgstr "一個表示函式中\\ :term:`位元組碼 <bytecode>`\\ 指令序列的字串"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1548
msgid ""
"A :class:`tuple` containing the literals used by the :term:`bytecode` in the "
"function"
msgstr ""
"一個包含函式中\\ :term:`位元組碼 <bytecode>`\\ 所使用之字面值的 :class:"
"`tuple`"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1552
msgid ""
"A :class:`tuple` containing the names used by the :term:`bytecode` in the "
"function"
msgstr ""
"一個包含函式中\\ :term:`位元組碼 <bytecode>`\\ 所使用之名稱的 :class:`tuple`"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1556
msgid "The name of the file from which the code was compiled"
msgstr "編譯出該程式碼的檔案名稱"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1559
msgid "The line number of the first line of the function"
msgstr "函式第一列的列號"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1562
msgid ""
"A :class:`bytes` object containing encoded source location information. The "
"exact format is an implementation detail and may change between Python "
"versions. Use :meth:`~codeobject.co_lines` and :meth:`~codeobject."
"co_positions` for supported access to line and position information. To "
"create a modified copy of a code object, use :meth:`~codeobject.replace`."
msgstr ""
"一個包含編碼後原始碼位置資訊的 :class:`bytes` 物件。確切的格式屬於實作細節，"
"可能會在不同 Python 版本之間改變。若要以受支援的方式存取列與位置資訊，請使"
"用 :meth:`~codeobject.co_lines` 與 :meth:`~codeobject.co_positions`。若要建立"
"程式碼物件的修改副本，請使用 :meth:`~codeobject.replace`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1572
msgid "The required stack size of the code object"
msgstr "程式碼物件所需的堆疊大小"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1575
msgid ""
"An :class:`integer <int>` encoding a number of flags for the interpreter."
msgstr "一個為直譯器編碼了數個旗標的\\ :class:`整數 <int>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1580
msgid ""
"The following flag bits are defined for :attr:`~codeobject.co_flags`: bit "
"``0x04`` is set if the function uses the ``*arguments`` syntax to accept an "
"arbitrary number of positional arguments; bit ``0x08`` is set if the "
"function uses the ``**keywords`` syntax to accept arbitrary keyword "
"arguments; bit ``0x20`` is set if the function is a generator. See :ref:"
"`inspect-module-co-flags` for details on the semantics of each flags that "
"might be present."
msgstr ""
":attr:`~codeobject.co_flags` 定義了以下旗標位元：如果函式使用 ``*arguments`` "
"語法來接受任意數量的位置引數，則會設定位元 ``0x04``；如果函式使用 "
"``**keywords`` 語法來接受任意關鍵字引數，則會設定位元 ``0x08``；如果函式是產"
"生器，則會設定位元 ``0x20``。關於可能出現的各個旗標之語意的細節，請參閱 :ref:"
"`inspect-module-co-flags`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1588
msgid ""
"Future feature declarations (for example, ``from __future__ import "
"division``) also use bits in :attr:`~codeobject.co_flags` to indicate "
"whether a code object was compiled with a particular feature enabled. See :"
"attr:`~__future__._Feature.compiler_flag`."
msgstr ""
"Future 功能宣告（例如 ``from __future__ import division``）也會使用 :attr:"
"`~codeobject.co_flags` 中的位元，來表示程式碼物件在編譯時是否啟用了特定功能。"
"請參閱 :attr:`~__future__._Feature.compiler_flag`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1592
msgid ""
"Other bits in :attr:`~codeobject.co_flags` are reserved for internal use."
msgstr ":attr:`~codeobject.co_flags` 中的其他位元保留供內部使用。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1596
msgid ""
"If a code object represents a function and has a docstring, the :data:"
"`~inspect.CO_HAS_DOCSTRING` bit is set in :attr:`~codeobject.co_flags` and "
"the first item in :attr:`~codeobject.co_consts` is the docstring of the "
"function."
msgstr ""
"如果程式碼物件代表一個函式且具有說明字串，則 :attr:`~codeobject.co_flags` 中"
"會設定 :data:`~inspect.CO_HAS_DOCSTRING` 位元，且 :attr:`~codeobject."
"co_consts` 中的第一個項目就是該函式的說明字串。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1602
msgid "Methods on code objects"
msgstr "用於程式碼物件的方法"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1606
msgid ""
"Returns an iterable over the source code positions of each :term:`bytecode` "
"instruction in the code object."
msgstr ""
"回傳一個涵蓋程式碼物件中每個\\ :term:`位元組碼 <bytecode>`\\ 指令之原始碼位置"
"的可疊代物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1609
msgid ""
"The iterator returns :class:`tuple`\\s containing the ``(start_line, "
"end_line, start_column, end_column)``. The *i-th* tuple corresponds to the "
"position of the source code that compiled to the *i-th* code unit. Column "
"information is 0-indexed utf-8 byte offsets on the given source line."
msgstr ""
"該疊代器會回傳包含 ``(start_line, end_line, start_column, end_column)`` 的 :"
"class:`tuple`。第 *i* 個 tuple 對應於編譯為第 *i* 個程式碼單元的原始碼位置。"
"欄資訊是給定原始碼列上以 0 起始的 utf-8 位元組偏移量。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1615
msgid ""
"This positional information can be missing. A non-exhaustive lists of cases "
"where this may happen:"
msgstr "此位置資訊可能會缺少。以下是可能發生這種情況的非詳盡列表："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1618
msgid "Running the interpreter with :option:`-X` ``no_debug_ranges``."
msgstr "使用 :option:`-X` ``no_debug_ranges`` 執行直譯器。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1619
msgid ""
"Loading a pyc file compiled while using :option:`-X` ``no_debug_ranges``."
msgstr "載入在使用 :option:`-X` ``no_debug_ranges`` 時編譯的 pyc 檔案。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1620
msgid "Position tuples corresponding to artificial instructions."
msgstr "對應於編譯器合成之指令 (artificial instruction) 的位置 tuple。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1621
msgid ""
"Line and column numbers that can't be represented due to implementation "
"specific limitations."
msgstr "由於實作特定的限制而無法表示的列號與欄號。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1624
msgid ""
"When this occurs, some or all of the tuple elements can be :const:`None`."
msgstr "發生這種情況時，tuple 的部分或全部元素可能為 :const:`None`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1630
msgid ""
"This feature requires storing column positions in code objects which may "
"result in a small increase of disk usage of compiled Python files or "
"interpreter memory usage. To avoid storing the extra information and/or "
"deactivate printing the extra traceback information, the :option:`-X` "
"``no_debug_ranges`` command line flag or the :envvar:`PYTHONNODEBUGRANGES` "
"environment variable can be used."
msgstr ""
"此功能需要在程式碼物件中儲存欄位置，這可能會使編譯後 Python 檔案的磁碟用量或"
"直譯器的記憶體用量略為增加。若要避免儲存額外資訊和/或停用印出額外的 "
"traceback 資訊，可以使用 :option:`-X` ``no_debug_ranges`` 命令列旗標或 :"
"envvar:`PYTHONNODEBUGRANGES` 環境變數。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1639
msgid ""
"Returns an iterator that yields information about successive ranges of :term:"
"`bytecode`\\s. Each item yielded is a ``(start, end, lineno)`` :class:"
"`tuple`:"
msgstr ""
"回傳一個疊代器，該疊代器會產生關於連續\\ :term:`位元組碼 <bytecode>`\\ 範圍的"
"資訊。每個產生的項目都是一個 ``(start, end, lineno)`` :class:`tuple`："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1643
msgid ""
"``start`` (an :class:`int`) represents the offset (inclusive) of the start "
"of the :term:`bytecode` range"
msgstr ""
"``start``\\ （一個 :class:`int`）表示\\ :term:`位元組碼 <bytecode>`\\ 範圍起"
"始處的偏移量（包含）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1645
msgid ""
"``end`` (an :class:`int`) represents the offset (exclusive) of the end of "
"the :term:`bytecode` range"
msgstr ""
"``end``\\ （一個 :class:`int`）表示\\ :term:`位元組碼 <bytecode>`\\ 範圍結尾"
"處的偏移量（不包含）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1647
msgid ""
"``lineno`` is an :class:`int` representing the line number of the :term:"
"`bytecode` range, or ``None`` if the bytecodes in the given range have no "
"line number"
msgstr ""
"``lineno`` 是一個 :class:`int`，表示\\ :term:`位元組碼 <bytecode>`\\ 範圍的列"
"號；如果給定範圍內的位元組碼沒有列號，則為 ``None``"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1651
msgid "The items yielded will have the following properties:"
msgstr "產生的項目具有以下特性："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1653
msgid "The first range yielded will have a ``start`` of 0."
msgstr "產生的第一個範圍的 ``start`` 為 0。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1654
msgid ""
"The ``(start, end)`` ranges will be non-decreasing and consecutive. That is, "
"for any pair of :class:`tuple`\\s, the ``start`` of the second will be equal "
"to the ``end`` of the first."
msgstr ""
"``(start, end)`` 範圍會是非遞減且連續的。也就是說，對於任何一對 :class:"
"`tuple`，第二個的 ``start`` 會等於第一個的 ``end``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1657
msgid "No range will be backwards: ``end >= start`` for all triples."
msgstr "沒有任何範圍是反向的：對於所有三元組，``end >= start``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1658
msgid ""
"The last :class:`tuple` yielded will have ``end`` equal to the size of the :"
"term:`bytecode`."
msgstr ""
"最後產生的 :class:`tuple` 的 ``end`` 會等於\\ :term:`位元組碼 <bytecode>`\\ "
"的大小。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1661
msgid ""
"Zero-width ranges, where ``start == end``, are allowed. Zero-width ranges "
"are used for lines that are present in the source code, but have been "
"eliminated by the :term:`bytecode` compiler."
msgstr ""
"允許零寬度的範圍，也就是 ``start == end``。零寬度範圍用於存在於原始碼中、但已"
"被\\ :term:`位元組碼 <bytecode>`\\ 編譯器消除的列。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1669
msgid ":pep:`626` - Precise line numbers for debugging and other tools."
msgstr ":pep:`626` - 用於除錯及其他工具的精確列號。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1670
msgid "The PEP that introduced the :meth:`!co_lines` method."
msgstr "引入 :meth:`!co_lines` 方法的 PEP。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1674
msgid ""
"Return a copy of the code object with new values for the specified fields."
msgstr "回傳程式碼物件的副本，並為指定的欄位設定新值。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1676
msgid ""
"Code objects are also supported by the generic function :func:`copy.replace`."
msgstr "泛型函式 :func:`copy.replace` 也支援程式碼物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1684
msgid "Frame objects"
msgstr "Frame 物件"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1688
msgid ""
"Frame objects represent execution frames.  They may occur in :ref:`traceback "
"objects <traceback-objects>`, and are also passed to registered trace "
"functions."
msgstr ""
"Frame 物件代表執行框 (execution frame)。它們可能出現在 :ref:`traceback 物件 "
"<traceback-objects>`\\ 中，也會被傳給已註冊的追蹤函式。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1707
msgid ""
"Points to the previous stack frame (towards the caller), or ``None`` if this "
"is the bottom stack frame"
msgstr ""
"指向前一個（朝向呼叫者的）堆疊框 (stack frame)，如果這是最底層的堆疊框則為 "
"``None``"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1711
msgid ""
"The :ref:`code object <code-objects>` being executed in this frame. "
"Accessing this attribute raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``object."
"__getattr__`` with arguments ``obj`` and ``\"f_code\"``."
msgstr ""
"在這個 frame 中執行的\\ :ref:`程式碼物件 <code-objects>`。存取這個屬性會引發"
"一個附帶引數 ``obj`` 與 ``\"f_code\"`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` "
"``object.__getattr__``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1716
msgid ""
"The mapping used by the frame to look up :ref:`local variables <naming>`. If "
"the frame refers to an :term:`optimized scope`, this may return a write-"
"through proxy object."
msgstr ""
"frame 用來查找\\ :ref:`區域變數 <naming>`\\ 的對映。如果該 frame 參照的是\\ :"
"term:`最佳化作用域 <optimized scope>`，則可能會回傳一個直寫 (write-through) "
"代理物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1721
msgid "Return a proxy for optimized scopes."
msgstr "為最佳化作用域回傳一個代理。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1725
msgid ""
"The dictionary used by the frame to look up :ref:`global variables <naming>`"
msgstr "frame 用來查找\\ :ref:`全域變數 <naming>`\\ 的字典"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1729
msgid ""
"The dictionary used by the frame to look up :ref:`built-in (intrinsic) names "
"<naming>`"
msgstr "frame 用來查找\\ :ref:`內建（固有）名稱 <naming>`\\ 的字典"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1733
msgid ""
"The \"precise instruction\" of the frame object (this is an index into the :"
"term:`bytecode` string of the :ref:`code object <code-objects>`)"
msgstr ""
"frame 物件的「精確指令」（這是\\ :ref:`程式碼物件 <code-objects>`\\ 之\\ :"
"term:`位元組碼 <bytecode>`\\ 字串中的索引）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1738
msgid ""
"The :term:`generator` or :term:`coroutine` object that owns this frame, or "
"``None`` if the frame is a normal function."
msgstr ""
"擁有此 frame 的\\ :term:`產生器 <generator>`\\ 或\\ :term:`協程 "
"<coroutine>`\\ 物件，如果該 frame 是一般函式則為 ``None``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1755
msgid ""
"If not ``None``, this is a function called for various events during code "
"execution (this is used by debuggers). Normally an event is triggered for "
"each new source line (see :attr:`~frame.f_trace_lines`)."
msgstr ""
"如果不是 ``None``，這是一個在程式碼執行期間針對各種事件所呼叫的函式（除錯器會"
"使用它）。通常每一個新的原始碼列都會觸發一個事件（請見 :attr:`~frame."
"f_trace_lines`）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1760
msgid ""
"Set this attribute to :const:`False` to disable triggering a tracing event "
"for each source line."
msgstr "將此屬性設為 :const:`False` 可停用針對每一個原始碼列觸發追蹤事件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1764
msgid ""
"Set this attribute to :const:`True` to allow per-opcode events to be "
"requested. Note that this may lead to undefined interpreter behaviour if "
"exceptions raised by the trace function escape to the function being traced."
msgstr ""
"將此屬性設為 :const:`True` 可允許請求每個操作碼 (per-opcode) 的事件。請注意，"
"如果追蹤函式所引發的例外傳播到被追蹤的函式，這可能會導致未定義的直譯器行為。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1770
msgid ""
"The current line number of the frame -- writing to this from within a trace "
"function jumps to the given line (only for the bottom-most frame).  A "
"debugger can implement a Jump command (aka Set Next Statement) by writing to "
"this attribute."
msgstr ""
"frame 目前的列號 -- 在追蹤函式中寫入此屬性會跳到指定的列（僅適用於最底層的 "
"frame）。除錯器可以透過寫入此屬性來實作 Jump 命令（也稱為 Set Next "
"Statement）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1776
msgid "Frame object methods"
msgstr "Frame 物件方法"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1778
msgid "Frame objects support one method:"
msgstr "Frame 物件支援一個方法："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1782
msgid ""
"This method clears all references to :ref:`local variables <naming>` held by "
"the frame.  Also, if the frame belonged to a :term:`generator`, the "
"generator is finalized.  This helps break reference cycles involving frame "
"objects (for example when catching an :ref:`exception <bltin-exceptions>` "
"and storing its :ref:`traceback <traceback-objects>` for later use)."
msgstr ""
"此方法會清除 frame 所持有之所有對\\ :ref:`區域變數 <naming>`\\ 的參照。此外，"
"如果該 frame 屬於一個\\ :term:`產生器 <generator>`，該產生器會被最終化。這有"
"助於打破涉及 frame 物件的參照循環 (reference cycle)，例如在捕捉\\ :ref:`例外 "
"<bltin-exceptions>`\\ 並儲存其 :ref:`traceback <traceback-objects>` 供之後使"
"用時。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1788
msgid ""
":exc:`RuntimeError` is raised if the frame is currently executing or "
"suspended."
msgstr "如果該 frame 目前正在執行或已暫停，則會引發 :exc:`RuntimeError`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1793
msgid ""
"Attempting to clear a suspended frame raises :exc:`RuntimeError` (as has "
"always been the case for executing frames)."
msgstr ""
"嘗試清除已暫停的 frame 會引發 :exc:`RuntimeError`\\ （如同對正在執行的 frame "
"一直以來的行為）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1801
msgid "Traceback objects"
msgstr "Traceback 物件"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1814
msgid ""
"Traceback objects represent the stack trace of an :ref:`exception <tut-"
"errors>`. A traceback object is implicitly created when an exception occurs, "
"and may also be explicitly created by calling :class:`types.TracebackType`."
msgstr ""
"Traceback 物件代表一個\\ :ref:`例外 <tut-errors>`\\ 的堆疊追蹤。traceback 物"
"件會在例外發生時隱式建立，也可以透過呼叫 :class:`types.TracebackType` 明確建"
"立。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1819
msgid "Traceback objects can now be explicitly instantiated from Python code."
msgstr "Traceback 物件現在可以從 Python 程式碼中明確地實例化。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1822
msgid ""
"For implicitly created tracebacks, when the search for an exception handler "
"unwinds the execution stack, at each unwound level a traceback object is "
"inserted in front of the current traceback.  When an exception handler is "
"entered, the stack trace is made available to the program. (See section :ref:"
"`try`.) It is accessible as the third item of the tuple returned by :func:"
"`sys.exc_info`, and as the :attr:`~BaseException.__traceback__` attribute of "
"the caught exception."
msgstr ""
"對於隱式建立的 traceback，當搜尋例外處理器的過程展開 (unwind) 執行堆疊時，每"
"展開一層，就會在目前的 traceback 前面插入一個 traceback 物件。當進入例外處理"
"器時，堆疊追蹤就可供程式使用。（請見 :ref:`try`\\ 章節。）它可以作為 :func:"
"`sys.exc_info` 所回傳之 tuple 的第三個項目來存取，也可以作為所捕捉例外的 :"
"attr:`~BaseException.__traceback__` 屬性來存取。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1831
msgid ""
"When the program contains no suitable handler, the stack trace is written "
"(nicely formatted) to the standard error stream; if the interpreter is "
"interactive, it is also made available to the user as :data:`sys."
"last_traceback`."
msgstr ""
"當程式不包含合適的處理器時，堆疊追蹤會以良好的格式寫入標準錯誤串流；如果直譯"
"器是互動式的，它也會作為 :data:`sys.last_traceback` 提供給使用者。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1836
msgid ""
"For explicitly created tracebacks, it is up to the creator of the traceback "
"to determine how the :attr:`~traceback.tb_next` attributes should be linked "
"to form a full stack trace."
msgstr ""
"對於明確建立的 traceback，由 traceback 的建立者決定應如何連結 :attr:"
"`~traceback.tb_next` 屬性以形成完整的堆疊追蹤。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1851
msgid ""
"Points to the execution :ref:`frame <frame-objects>` of the current level."
msgstr "指向目前層級的\\ :ref:`執行框 <frame-objects>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1854
msgid ""
"Accessing this attribute raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``object."
"__getattr__`` with arguments ``obj`` and ``\"tb_frame\"``."
msgstr ""
"存取此屬性會引發一個附帶引數 ``obj`` 與 ``\"tb_frame\"`` 的\\ :ref:`稽核事件 "
"<auditing>` ``object.__getattr__``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1859
msgid "Gives the line number where the exception occurred"
msgstr "提供發生例外的列號"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1862
msgid "Indicates the \"precise instruction\"."
msgstr "表示「精確指令」。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1864
msgid ""
"The line number and last instruction in the traceback may differ from the "
"line number of its :ref:`frame object <frame-objects>` if the exception "
"occurred in a :keyword:`try` statement with no matching except clause or "
"with a :keyword:`finally` clause."
msgstr ""
"如果例外發生在沒有相符 except 子句或帶有 :keyword:`finally` 子句的 :keyword:"
"`try` 陳述式中，traceback 中的列號與最後指令可能會與其 :ref:`frame 物件 "
"<frame-objects>`\\ 的列號不同。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1875
msgid ""
"The special writable attribute :attr:`!tb_next` is the next level in the "
"stack trace (towards the frame where the exception occurred), or ``None`` if "
"there is no next level."
msgstr ""
"特殊可寫入屬性 :attr:`!tb_next` 是堆疊追蹤中的下一層（朝向發生例外的 "
"frame），如果沒有下一層則為 ``None``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1879
msgid "This attribute is now writable"
msgstr "此屬性現在可寫入"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1884
msgid "Slice objects"
msgstr "切片物件"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1888
msgid ""
"Slice objects are used to represent slices for :meth:`~object.__getitem__` "
"methods.  They are also created by the built-in :func:`slice` function."
msgstr ""
"切片物件用來表示 :meth:`~object.__getitem__` 方法的切片。它們也可以由內建的 :"
"func:`slice` 函式建立。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1894
msgid ""
"The :func:`slice` type now supports :ref:`subscription <subscriptions>`. For "
"example, ``slice[float]`` may be used in type annotations to indicate a "
"slice containing :type:`float` objects."
msgstr ""
":func:`slice` 型別現在支援\\ :ref:`下標 <subscriptions>`。例如，"
"``slice[float]`` 可以在型別註釋中用來表示包含 :type:`float` 物件的切片。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1903
msgid ""
"Special read-only attributes: :attr:`~slice.start` is the lower bound; :attr:"
"`~slice.stop` is the upper bound; :attr:`~slice.step` is the step value; "
"each is ``None`` if omitted.  These attributes can have any type."
msgstr ""
"特殊唯讀屬性：:attr:`~slice.start` 是下界；:attr:`~slice.stop` 是上界；:attr:"
"`~slice.step` 是步長值；若省略則各為 ``None``。這些屬性可以是任何型別。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1907
msgid "Slice objects support one method:"
msgstr "切片物件支援一個方法："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1911
msgid ""
"This method takes a single integer argument *length* and computes "
"information about the slice that the slice object would describe if applied "
"to a sequence of *length* items.  It returns a tuple of three integers; "
"respectively these are the *start* and *stop* indices and the *step* or "
"stride length of the slice. Missing or out-of-bounds indices are handled in "
"a manner consistent with regular slices."
msgstr ""
"這個方法接受單一整數引數 *length*，並計算當切片物件套用到一個包含 *length* 個"
"項目的序列時，該切片物件所描述的切片資訊。它會回傳一個由三個整數組成的 "
"tuple，依序是切片的 *start* 和 *stop* 索引，以及 *step*\\ （即步長）。缺少或"
"超出範圍的索引會以與一般切片一致的方式處理。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1920
msgid "Static method objects"
msgstr "靜態方法物件"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1922
msgid ""
"Static method objects provide a way of defeating the transformation of "
"function objects to method objects described above. A static method object "
"is a wrapper around any other object, usually a user-defined method object. "
"When a static method object is retrieved from a class or a class instance, "
"the object actually returned is the wrapped object, which is not subject to "
"any further transformation. Static method objects are also callable. Static "
"method objects are created by the built-in :func:`staticmethod` constructor."
msgstr ""
"靜態方法物件提供了一種方式，可以阻止上述將函式物件轉換為方法物件的過程。靜態"
"方法物件是包裝任何其他物件的 wrapper，被包裝的通常是使用者定義的方法物件。當"
"從類別或類別實例取得靜態方法物件時，實際回傳的是被包裝的物件，它不會再經過任"
"何進一步的轉換。靜態方法物件也是可呼叫的。靜態方法物件由內建的 :func:"
"`staticmethod` 建構函式建立。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1932
msgid "Class method objects"
msgstr "類別方法物件"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1934
msgid ""
"A class method object, like a static method object, is a wrapper around "
"another object that alters the way in which that object is retrieved from "
"classes and class instances. The behaviour of class method objects upon such "
"retrieval is described above, under :ref:`\"instance methods\" <instance-"
"methods>`. Class method objects are created by the built-in :func:"
"`classmethod` constructor."
msgstr ""
"類別方法物件和靜態方法物件一樣，是包裝另一個物件的 wrapper，會改變從類別和類"
"別實例取得該物件的方式。類別方法物件在這種取得情況下的行為，已在上方的\\ :"
"ref:`「實例方法」 <instance-methods>`\\ 中描述。類別方法物件由內建的 :func:"
"`classmethod` 建構函式建立。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1944
msgid "Special method names"
msgstr "特殊方法名稱"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1950
msgid ""
"A class can implement certain operations that are invoked by special syntax "
"(such as arithmetic operations or subscripting and slicing) by defining "
"methods with special names. This is Python's approach to :dfn:`operator "
"overloading`, allowing classes to define their own behavior with respect to "
"language operators.  For instance, if a class defines a method named :meth:"
"`~object.__getitem__`, and ``x`` is an instance of this class, then ``x[i]`` "
"is roughly equivalent to ``type(x).__getitem__(x, i)``.  Except where "
"mentioned, attempts to execute an operation raise an exception when no "
"appropriate method is defined (typically :exc:`AttributeError` or :exc:"
"`TypeError`)."
msgstr ""
"一個類別可以透過定義具有特殊名稱的方法，來實作由特殊語法（例如算術運算或下標"
"與切片）所呼叫的特定操作。這是 Python 處理\\ :dfn:`運算子多載 (operator "
"overloading)` 的方式，讓類別能夠針對語言的運算子定義自己的行為。舉例來說，如"
"果一個類別定義了名為 :meth:`~object.__getitem__` 的方法，且 ``x`` 是該類別的"
"實例，那麼 ``x[i]`` 大致等同於 ``type(x).__getitem__(x, i)``。除非另有說明，"
"當沒有定義適當的方法時，嘗試執行該操作會引發例外（通常是 :exc:"
"`AttributeError` 或 :exc:`TypeError`）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1961
msgid ""
"Setting a special method to ``None`` indicates that the corresponding "
"operation is not available.  For example, if a class sets :meth:`~object."
"__iter__` to ``None``, the class is not iterable, so calling :func:`iter` on "
"its instances will raise a :exc:`TypeError` (without falling back to :meth:"
"`~object.__getitem__`). [#]_"
msgstr ""
"將特殊方法設為 ``None`` 表示對應的操作無法使用。例如，如果一個類別將 :meth:"
"`~object.__iter__` 設為 ``None``，該類別就不是可疊代的，因此對其實例呼叫 :"
"func:`iter` 會引發 :exc:`TypeError`\\ （而不會退回使用 :meth:`~object."
"__getitem__`）。\\ [#]_"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1967
msgid ""
"When implementing a class that emulates any built-in type, it is important "
"that the emulation only be implemented to the degree that it makes sense for "
"the object being modelled.  For example, some sequences may work well with "
"retrieval of individual elements, but extracting a slice may not make sense. "
"(One example of this is the :ref:`NodeList <dom-nodelist-objects>` interface "
"in the W3C's Document Object Model.)"
msgstr ""
"在實作一個模擬任何內建型別的類別時，重要的是只在對所建模物件有意義的範圍內實"
"作該模擬。例如，某些序列可能很適合取得個別元素，但擷取切片可能就沒有意義。"
"（W3C 文件物件模型 (Document Object Model) 中的 :ref:`NodeList <dom-nodelist-"
"objects>` 介面就是一個例子。）"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1978
msgid "Basic customization"
msgstr "基本自訂"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1984
msgid ""
"Called to create a new instance of class *cls*.  :meth:`__new__` is a static "
"method (special-cased so you need not declare it as such) that takes the "
"class of which an instance was requested as its first argument.  The "
"remaining arguments are those passed to the object constructor expression "
"(the call to the class).  The return value of :meth:`__new__` should be the "
"new object instance (usually an instance of *cls*)."
msgstr ""
"呼叫以建立類別 *cls* 的新實例。:meth:`__new__` 是一個靜態方法（已特別處理，因"
"此你不需要將它宣告為靜態方法），它接受被請求建立實例的那個類別作為第一個引"
"數。其餘引數則是傳給物件建構運算式（即對類別的呼叫）的引數。:meth:`__new__` "
"的回傳值應為新的物件實例（通常是 *cls* 的實例）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1991
msgid ""
"Typical implementations create a new instance of the class by invoking the "
"superclass's :meth:`__new__` method using ``super().__new__(cls[, ...])`` "
"with appropriate arguments and then modifying the newly created instance as "
"necessary before returning it."
msgstr ""
"典型的實作會使用 ``super().__new__(cls[, ...])`` 並搭配適當的引數來呼叫超類別"
"的 :meth:`__new__` 方法，以建立該類別的新實例，接著在回傳之前視需要修改這個新"
"建立的實例。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:1996
msgid ""
"If :meth:`__new__` is invoked during object construction and it returns an "
"instance of *cls*, then the new instance’s :meth:`__init__` method will be "
"invoked like ``__init__(self[, ...])``, where *self* is the new instance and "
"the remaining arguments are the same as were passed to the object "
"constructor."
msgstr ""
"如果 :meth:`__new__` 在物件建構期間被呼叫，並且回傳了 *cls* 的實例，那麼新實"
"例的 :meth:`__init__` 方法將會以 ``__init__(self[, ...])`` 的形式被呼叫，其"
"中 *self* 是新實例，其餘引數則與傳給物件建構函式的引數相同。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2001
msgid ""
"If :meth:`__new__` does not return an instance of *cls*, then the new "
"instance's :meth:`__init__` method will not be invoked."
msgstr ""
"如果 :meth:`__new__` 沒有回傳 *cls* 的實例，則新實例的 :meth:`__init__` 方法"
"將不會被呼叫。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2004
msgid ""
":meth:`__new__` is intended mainly to allow subclasses of immutable types "
"(like int, str, or tuple) to customize instance creation.  It is also "
"commonly overridden in custom metaclasses in order to customize class "
"creation."
msgstr ""
":meth:`__new__` 主要是用來讓不可變型別（例如 int、str 或 tuple）的子類別能夠"
"自訂實例的建立。它也經常在自訂元類別中被覆寫，以自訂類別的建立。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2013
msgid ""
"Called after the instance has been created (by :meth:`__new__`), but before "
"it is returned to the caller.  The arguments are those passed to the class "
"constructor expression.  If a base class has an :meth:`__init__` method, the "
"derived class's :meth:`__init__` method, if any, must explicitly call it to "
"ensure proper initialization of the base class part of the instance; for "
"example: ``super().__init__([args...])``."
msgstr ""
"在實例（由 :meth:`__new__`）建立之後、回傳給呼叫者之前呼叫。引數為傳給類別建"
"構運算式的引數。如果基底類別有 :meth:`__init__` 方法，衍生類別的 :meth:"
"`__init__` 方法（如果有的話）必須明確呼叫它，以確保實例中屬於基底類別的部分能"
"被正確初始化；例如：``super().__init__([args...])``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2020
msgid ""
"Because :meth:`__new__` and :meth:`__init__` work together in constructing "
"objects (:meth:`__new__` to create it, and :meth:`__init__` to customize "
"it), no non-``None`` value may be returned by :meth:`__init__`; doing so "
"will cause a :exc:`TypeError` to be raised at runtime."
msgstr ""
"因為 :meth:`__new__` 和 :meth:`__init__` 在建構物件時協同運作（:meth:"
"`__new__` 負責建立，:meth:`__init__` 負責自訂），所以 :meth:`__init__` 不得回"
"傳任何非 ``None`` 的值；這樣做會導致在 runtime 時引發 :exc:`TypeError`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2033
msgid ""
"Called when the instance is about to be destroyed.  This is also called a "
"finalizer or (improperly) a destructor.  If a base class has a :meth:"
"`__del__` method, the derived class's :meth:`__del__` method, if any, must "
"explicitly call it to ensure proper deletion of the base class part of the "
"instance."
msgstr ""
"在實例即將被摧毀時呼叫。這也被稱為終結函式 (finalizer) 或（不恰當地）稱為解構"
"函式 (destructor)。如果基底類別有 :meth:`__del__` 方法，衍生類別的 :meth:"
"`__del__` 方法（如果有的話）必須明確呼叫它，以確保實例中屬於基底類別的部分能"
"被正確刪除。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2039
msgid ""
"It is possible (though not recommended!) for the :meth:`__del__` method to "
"postpone destruction of the instance by creating a new reference to it.  "
"This is called object *resurrection*.  It is implementation-dependent "
"whether :meth:`__del__` is called a second time when a resurrected object is "
"about to be destroyed; the current :term:`CPython` implementation only calls "
"it once."
msgstr ""
":meth:`__del__` 方法有可能（雖然不建議！）透過建立對實例的新參照來延後該實例"
"的摧毀。這被稱為物件\\ *復活 (resurrection)*。當復活的物件即將被摧毀時，:"
"meth:`__del__` 是否會被第二次呼叫取決於實作；目前的 :term:`CPython` 實作只會"
"呼叫一次。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2046
msgid ""
"It is not guaranteed that :meth:`__del__` methods are called for objects "
"that still exist when the interpreter exits. :class:`weakref.finalize` "
"provides a straightforward way to register a cleanup function to be called "
"when an object is garbage collected."
msgstr ""
"對於直譯器結束時仍存在的物件，不保證會呼叫其 :meth:`__del__` 方法。:class:"
"`weakref.finalize` 提供了一種直接的方式來註冊清理函式，讓它在物件被垃圾回收時"
"被呼叫。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2053
msgid ""
"``del x`` doesn't directly call ``x.__del__()`` --- the former decrements "
"the reference count for ``x`` by one, and the latter is only called when "
"``x``'s reference count reaches zero."
msgstr ""
"``del x`` 不會直接呼叫 ``x.__del__()`` --- 前者會將 ``x`` 的參照計數減一，而"
"後者只會在 ``x`` 的參照計數歸零時被呼叫。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2058
msgid ""
"It is possible for a reference cycle to prevent the reference count of an "
"object from going to zero.  In this case, the cycle will be later detected "
"and deleted by the :term:`cyclic garbage collector <garbage collection>`.  A "
"common cause of reference cycles is when an exception has been caught in a "
"local variable.  The frame's locals then reference the exception, which "
"references its own traceback, which references the locals of all frames "
"caught in the traceback."
msgstr ""
"參照循環有可能使物件的參照計數無法歸零。在這種情況下，該循環稍後會被\\ :term:"
"`循環垃圾回收器 <garbage collection>`\\ 偵測並刪除。參照循環的一個常見成因是"
"在區域變數中捕捉到例外。此時 frame 的區域變數會參照該例外，而例外又參照它自己"
"的 traceback，traceback 則參照了其中捕捉到的所有 frame 的區域變數。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2068
msgid "Documentation for the :mod:`gc` module."
msgstr ":mod:`gc` 模組的文件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2072
msgid ""
"Due to the precarious circumstances under which :meth:`__del__` methods are "
"invoked, exceptions that occur during their execution are ignored, and a "
"warning is printed to ``sys.stderr`` instead.  In particular:"
msgstr ""
"由於 :meth:`__del__` 方法被呼叫時所處的情況並不穩定，在其執行期間發生的例外會"
"被忽略，並改為在 ``sys.stderr`` 印出警告。特別是："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2076
msgid ""
":meth:`__del__` can be invoked when arbitrary code is being executed, "
"including from any arbitrary thread.  If :meth:`__del__` needs to take a "
"lock or invoke any other blocking resource, it may deadlock as the resource "
"may already be taken by the code that gets interrupted to execute :meth:"
"`__del__`."
msgstr ""
":meth:`__del__` 可能在任意程式碼正在執行時被呼叫，包括從任意執行緒中呼叫。如"
"果 :meth:`__del__` 需要取得鎖或使用任何其他會阻塞的資源，它可能會發生死鎖，因"
"為該資源可能已經被那段為了執行 :meth:`__del__` 而被中斷的程式碼所占用。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2082
msgid ""
":meth:`__del__` can be executed during interpreter shutdown.  As a "
"consequence, the global variables it needs to access (including other "
"modules) may already have been deleted or set to ``None``. Python guarantees "
"that globals whose name begins with a single underscore are deleted from "
"their module before other globals are deleted; if no other references to "
"such globals exist, this may help in assuring that imported modules are "
"still available at the time when the :meth:`__del__` method is called."
msgstr ""
":meth:`__del__` 可能在直譯器關閉期間被執行。因此，它需要存取的全域變數（包括"
"其他模組）可能已經被刪除或被設為 ``None``。Python 保證名稱以單一底線開頭的全"
"域變數，會先於其他全域變數從其模組中刪除；如果沒有其他對這類全域變數的參照存"
"在，這可能有助於確保在呼叫 :meth:`__del__` 方法時，被引入的模組仍然可用。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2097
msgid ""
"Called by the :func:`repr` built-in function to compute the \"official\" "
"string representation of an object.  If at all possible, this should look "
"like a valid Python expression that could be used to recreate an object with "
"the same value (given an appropriate environment).  If this is not possible, "
"a string of the form ``<...some useful description...>`` should be returned. "
"The return value must be a string object. If a class defines :meth:"
"`__repr__` but not :meth:`__str__`, then :meth:`__repr__` is also used when "
"an \"informal\" string representation of instances of that class is required."
msgstr ""
"由內建函式 :func:`repr` 呼叫，以計算物件的「正式」字串表示法。如果可能的話，"
"它應該看起來像是一個有效的 Python 運算式，可以用來（在適當的環境下）重新建立"
"具有相同值的物件。如果做不到，則應回傳形如 ``<...some useful description..."
">`` 的字串。回傳值必須是字串物件。如果類別定義了 :meth:`__repr__` 但沒有定"
"義 :meth:`__str__`，那麼當需要該類別實例的「非正式」字串表示法時，也會使用 :"
"meth:`__repr__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2106
msgid ""
"This is typically used for debugging, so it is important that the "
"representation is information-rich and unambiguous. A default implementation "
"is provided by the :class:`object` class itself."
msgstr ""
"這通常用於除錯，因此表示法必須資訊豐富且沒有歧義。:class:`object` 類別本身提"
"供了預設實作。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2118
msgid ""
"Called by :func:`str(object) <str>`, the default :meth:`__format__` "
"implementation, and the built-in function :func:`print`, to compute the "
"\"informal\" or nicely printable string representation of an object.  The "
"return value must be a :ref:`str <textseq>` object."
msgstr ""
"由 :func:`str(object) <str>`、預設的 :meth:`__format__` 實作以及內建函式 :"
"func:`print` 呼叫，以計算物件的「非正式」或適合印出的字串表示法。回傳值必須"
"是 :ref:`str <textseq>` 物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2123
msgid ""
"This method differs from :meth:`object.__repr__` in that there is no "
"expectation that :meth:`__str__` return a valid Python expression: a more "
"convenient or concise representation can be used."
msgstr ""
"此方法與 :meth:`object.__repr__` 的不同之處在於，並不預期 :meth:`__str__` 回"
"傳有效的 Python 運算式：可以使用更方便或更簡潔的表示法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2127
msgid ""
"The default implementation defined by the built-in type :class:`object` "
"calls :meth:`object.__repr__`."
msgstr ""
"內建型別 :class:`object` 所定義的預設實作會呼叫 :meth:`object.__repr__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2137
msgid ""
"Called by :ref:`bytes <func-bytes>` to compute a byte-string representation "
"of an object. This should return a :class:`bytes` object. The :class:"
"`object` class itself does not provide this method."
msgstr ""
"由 :ref:`bytes <func-bytes>` 呼叫，以計算物件的位元組字串表示法。這應該回傳一"
"個 :class:`bytes` 物件。:class:`object` 類別本身不提供此方法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2149
msgid ""
"Called by the :func:`format` built-in function, and by extension, evaluation "
"of :ref:`formatted string literals <f-strings>` and the :meth:`str.format` "
"method, to produce a \"formatted\" string representation of an object. The "
"*format_spec* argument is a string that contains a description of the "
"formatting options desired. The interpretation of the *format_spec* argument "
"is up to the type implementing :meth:`__format__`, however most classes will "
"either delegate formatting to one of the built-in types, or use a similar "
"formatting option syntax."
msgstr ""
"由內建函式 :func:`format` 呼叫，延伸而言也在對\\ :ref:`格式化的字串字面值 <f-"
"strings>`\\ 求值時和 :meth:`str.format` 方法中呼叫，以產生物件的「格式化」字"
"串表示法。*format_spec* 引數是一個字串，包含所需格式化選項的描述。"
"*format_spec* 引數如何解讀由實作 :meth:`__format__` 的型別決定，不過大多數類"
"別會將格式化委派給某個內建型別，或使用類似的格式化選項語法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2159
msgid ""
"See :ref:`formatspec` for a description of the standard formatting syntax."
msgstr "標準格式化語法的描述請見\\ :ref:`formatspec`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2161
msgid "The return value must be a string object."
msgstr "回傳值必須是個字串物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2163
msgid ""
"The default implementation by the :class:`object` class should be given an "
"empty *format_spec* string. It delegates to :meth:`__str__`."
msgstr ""
"呼叫 :class:`object` 類別的預設實作時，應傳入空的 *format_spec* 字串。它會委"
"派給 :meth:`__str__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2166
msgid ""
"The __format__ method of ``object`` itself raises a :exc:`TypeError` if "
"passed any non-empty string."
msgstr ""
"``object`` 本身的 __format__ 方法在傳入任何非空字串時會引發 :exc:"
"`TypeError`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2170
msgid ""
"``object.__format__(x, '')`` is now equivalent to ``str(x)`` rather than "
"``format(str(x), '')``."
msgstr ""
"``object.__format__(x, '')`` 現在等同於 ``str(x)``，而不是 ``format(str(x), "
"'')``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2186
msgid ""
"These are the so-called \"rich comparison\" methods. The correspondence "
"between operator symbols and method names is as follows: ``x<y`` calls ``x."
"__lt__(y)``, ``x<=y`` calls ``x.__le__(y)``, ``x==y`` calls ``x.__eq__(y)``, "
"``x!=y`` calls ``x.__ne__(y)``, ``x>y`` calls ``x.__gt__(y)``, and ``x>=y`` "
"calls ``x.__ge__(y)``."
msgstr ""
"這些是所謂的「rich comparison」方法。運算子符號與方法名稱之間的對應關係如下："
"``x<y`` 會呼叫 ``x.__lt__(y)``、``x<=y`` 會呼叫 ``x.__le__(y)``、``x==y`` 會"
"呼叫 ``x.__eq__(y)``、``x!=y`` 會呼叫 ``x.__ne__(y)``、``x>y`` 會呼叫 ``x."
"__gt__(y)``，而 ``x>=y`` 會呼叫 ``x.__ge__(y)``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2192
msgid ""
"A rich comparison method may return the singleton :data:`NotImplemented` if "
"it does not implement the operation for a given pair of arguments. By "
"convention, ``False`` and ``True`` are returned for a successful comparison. "
"However, these methods can return any value, so if the comparison operator "
"is used in a Boolean context (e.g., in the condition of an ``if`` "
"statement), Python will call :func:`bool` on the value to determine if the "
"result is true or false."
msgstr ""
"如果 rich comparison 方法沒有為給定的一對引數實作該操作，它可以回傳單例 :"
"data:`NotImplemented`。按照慣例，成功的比較會回傳 ``False`` 或 ``True``。然"
"而，這些方法可以回傳任何值，因此如果比較運算子用在預期布林值的情境中（例如在 "
"``if`` 陳述式的條件中），Python 會對該值呼叫 :func:`bool` 來判斷結果為真或為"
"假。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2199
msgid ""
"By default, ``object`` implements :meth:`__eq__` by using ``is``, returning :"
"data:`NotImplemented` in the case of a false comparison: ``True if x is y "
"else NotImplemented``. For :meth:`__ne__`, by default it delegates to :meth:"
"`__eq__` and inverts the result unless it is :data:`!NotImplemented`.  There "
"are no other implied relationships among the comparison operators or default "
"implementations; for example, the truth of ``(x<y or x==y)`` does not imply "
"``x<=y``. To automatically generate ordering operations from a single root "
"operation, see :deco:`functools.total_ordering`."
msgstr ""
"預設情況下，``object`` 會使用 ``is`` 來實作 :meth:`__eq__`，並在比較結果為假"
"時回傳 :data:`NotImplemented`：``True if x is y else NotImplemented``。對於 :"
"meth:`__ne__`，預設會委派給 :meth:`__eq__` 並將結果反轉，除非結果是 :data:`!"
"NotImplemented`。比較運算子或預設實作之間沒有其他隱含的關係；例如，``(x<y or "
"x==y)`` 為真並不代表 ``x<=y``。若要從單一根操作自動產生排序操作，請參閱 :"
"deco:`functools.total_ordering`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2208
msgid ""
"By default, the :class:`object` class provides implementations consistent "
"with :ref:`expressions-value-comparisons`: equality compares according to "
"object identity, and order comparisons raise :exc:`TypeError`. Each default "
"method may generate these results directly, but may also return :data:"
"`NotImplemented`."
msgstr ""
"預設情況下，:class:`object` 類別提供的實作與\\ :ref:`expressions-value-"
"comparisons`\\ 一致：相等性依據物件識別性進行比較，而順序比較則會引發 :exc:"
"`TypeError`。每個預設方法可以直接產生這些結果，但也可能回傳 :data:"
"`NotImplemented`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2214
msgid ""
"See the paragraph on :meth:`__hash__` for some important notes on creating :"
"term:`hashable` objects which support custom comparison operations and are "
"usable as dictionary keys."
msgstr ""
"關於建立支援自訂比較操作、並可用作字典鍵的\\ :term:`可雜湊的 <hashable>`\\ 物"
"件，請參閱 :meth:`__hash__` 段落中的一些重要說明。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2218
msgid ""
"There are no swapped-argument versions of these methods (to be used when the "
"left argument does not support the operation but the right argument does); "
"rather, :meth:`__lt__` and :meth:`__gt__` are each other's reflection, :meth:"
"`__le__` and :meth:`__ge__` are each other's reflection, and :meth:`__eq__` "
"and :meth:`__ne__` are their own reflection. If the operands are of "
"different types, and the right operand's type is a direct or indirect "
"subclass of the left operand's type, the reflected method of the right "
"operand has priority, otherwise the left operand's method has priority.  "
"Virtual subclassing is not considered."
msgstr ""
"這些方法沒有引數對調的版本（用於左引數不支援該操作、但右引數支援的情況）；相"
"反地，:meth:`__lt__` 和 :meth:`__gt__` 互為對方的反轉，:meth:`__le__` 和 :"
"meth:`__ge__` 互為對方的反轉，而 :meth:`__eq__` 和 :meth:`__ne__` 則是自己的"
"反轉。如果運算元的型別不同，且右運算元的型別是左運算元型別的直接或間接子類"
"別，則右運算元的反轉方法具有優先權，否則左運算元的方法具有優先權。虛擬子類別"
"化不列入考慮。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2229
msgid ""
"When no appropriate method returns any value other than :data:"
"`NotImplemented`, the ``==`` and ``!=`` operators will fall back to ``is`` "
"and ``is not``, respectively."
msgstr ""
"當沒有任何適當的方法回傳 :data:`NotImplemented` 以外的值時，``==`` 和 ``!=`` "
"運算子將分別退回使用 ``is`` 和 ``is not``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2238
msgid ""
"Called by built-in function :func:`hash` and for operations on members of "
"hashed collections including :class:`set`, :class:`frozenset`, :class:"
"`dict`, and :class:`frozendict`. The ``__hash__()`` method should return an "
"integer. The only required property is that objects which compare equal have "
"the same hash value; it is advised to mix together the hash values of the "
"components of the object that also play a part in comparison of objects by "
"packing them into a tuple and hashing the tuple. Example::"
msgstr ""
"由內建函式 :func:`hash` 呼叫，也用於雜湊集合（包括 :class:`set`、:class:"
"`frozenset`、:class:`dict` 與 :class:`frozendict`）成員的操作。"
"``__hash__()`` 方法應回傳一個整數。唯一要求的特性是比較結果相等的物件具有相同"
"的雜湊值；建議的做法是把物件中同樣參與物件比較的各個組成部分打包成一個 "
"tuple，再對該 tuple 進行雜湊，藉此將這些組成部分的雜湊值混合在一起。範例： ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2246
msgid ""
"def __hash__(self):\n"
"    return hash((self.name, self.nick, self.color))"
msgstr ""
"def __hash__(self):\n"
"    return hash((self.name, self.nick, self.color))"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2251
msgid ""
":func:`hash` truncates the value returned from an object's custom :meth:"
"`__hash__` method to the size of a :c:type:`Py_ssize_t`.  This is typically "
"8 bytes on 64-bit builds and 4 bytes on 32-bit builds.  If an object's   :"
"meth:`__hash__` must interoperate on builds of different bit sizes, be sure "
"to check the width on all supported builds.  An easy way to do this is with "
"``python -c \"import sys; print(sys.hash_info.width)\"``."
msgstr ""
":func:`hash` 會將物件自訂的 :meth:`__hash__` 方法所回傳的值截斷為 :c:type:"
"`Py_ssize_t` 的大小。在 64 位元建置上通常為 8 個位元組，在 32 位元建置上則為 "
"4 個位元組。如果物件的 :meth:`__hash__` 必須在不同位元大小的建置之間互通，請"
"務必檢查所有支援的建置上的寬度。一個簡單的做法是使用 ``python -c \"import "
"sys; print(sys.hash_info.width)\"``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2259
msgid ""
"If a class does not define an :meth:`__eq__` method it should not define a :"
"meth:`__hash__` operation either; if it defines :meth:`__eq__` but not :meth:"
"`__hash__`, its instances will not be usable as items in hashable "
"collections.  If a class defines mutable objects and implements an :meth:"
"`__eq__` method, it should not implement :meth:`__hash__`, since the "
"implementation of :term:`hashable` collections requires that a key's hash "
"value is immutable (if the object's hash value changes, it will be in the "
"wrong hash bucket)."
msgstr ""
"如果類別沒有定義 :meth:`__eq__` 方法，它也不應該定義 :meth:`__hash__` 操作；"
"如果它定義了 :meth:`__eq__` 但沒有定義 :meth:`__hash__`，它的實例將無法作為可"
"雜湊集合中的項目使用。如果類別定義的是可變物件並實作了 :meth:`__eq__` 方法，"
"它就不應該實作 :meth:`__hash__`，因為\\ :term:`可雜湊的 <hashable>`\\ 集合的"
"實作要求鍵的雜湊值是不可變的（如果物件的雜湊值改變了，它會位於錯誤的雜湊桶 "
"(hash bucket) 中）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2268
msgid ""
"User-defined classes have :meth:`__eq__` and :meth:`__hash__` methods by "
"default (inherited from the :class:`object` class); with them, all objects "
"compare unequal (except with themselves) and ``x.__hash__()`` returns an "
"appropriate value such that ``x == y`` implies both that ``x is y`` and "
"``hash(x) == hash(y)``."
msgstr ""
"使用者定義的類別預設具有 :meth:`__eq__` 和 :meth:`__hash__` 方法（繼承自 :"
"class:`object` 類別）；有了這些方法，所有物件之間比較皆不相等（與自身比較除"
"外），且 ``x.__hash__()`` 會回傳適當的值，使得 ``x == y`` 同時意味著 ``x is "
"y`` 和 ``hash(x) == hash(y)``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2273
msgid ""
"A class that overrides :meth:`__eq__` and does not define :meth:`__hash__` "
"will have its :meth:`__hash__` implicitly set to ``None``.  When the :meth:"
"`__hash__` method of a class is ``None``, instances of the class will raise "
"an appropriate :exc:`TypeError` when a program attempts to retrieve their "
"hash value, and will also be correctly identified as unhashable when "
"checking ``isinstance(obj, collections.abc.Hashable)``."
msgstr ""
"覆寫了 :meth:`__eq__` 而沒有定義 :meth:`__hash__` 的類別，其 :meth:"
"`__hash__` 會被隱式地設為 ``None``。當類別的 :meth:`__hash__` 方法為 "
"``None`` 時，若程式嘗試取得該類別實例的雜湊值，實例將會引發適當的 :exc:"
"`TypeError`，而且在檢查 ``isinstance(obj, collections.abc.Hashable)`` 時也會"
"被正確地識別為不可雜湊。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2280
msgid ""
"If a class that overrides :meth:`__eq__` needs to retain the implementation "
"of :meth:`__hash__` from a parent class, the interpreter must be told this "
"explicitly by setting ``__hash__ = <ParentClass>.__hash__``."
msgstr ""
"如果覆寫了 :meth:`__eq__` 的類別需要保留父類別的 :meth:`__hash__` 實作，必須"
"透過設定 ``__hash__ = <ParentClass>.__hash__`` 來明確告知直譯器。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2284
msgid ""
"If a class that does not override :meth:`__eq__` wishes to suppress hash "
"support, it should include ``__hash__ = None`` in the class definition. A "
"class which defines its own :meth:`__hash__` that explicitly raises a :exc:"
"`TypeError` would be incorrectly identified as hashable by an "
"``isinstance(obj, collections.abc.Hashable)`` call."
msgstr ""
"如果沒有覆寫 :meth:`__eq__` 的類別希望停用雜湊支援，應該在類別定義中加入 "
"``__hash__ = None``。如果類別定義了自己的 :meth:`__hash__` 並明確引發 :exc:"
"`TypeError`，則會被 ``isinstance(obj, collections.abc.Hashable)`` 呼叫錯誤地"
"識別為可雜湊。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2293
msgid ""
"By default, the :meth:`__hash__` values of str and bytes objects are "
"\"salted\" with an unpredictable random value.  Although they remain "
"constant within an individual Python process, they are not predictable "
"between repeated invocations of Python."
msgstr ""
"預設情況下，str 和 bytes 物件的 :meth:`__hash__` 值會以一個無法預測的隨機值"
"「加鹽」(salted)。雖然在單一 Python 行程中它們會保持不變，但在多次執行 "
"Python 之間則無法預測。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2298
msgid ""
"This is intended to provide protection against a denial-of-service caused by "
"carefully chosen inputs that exploit the worst case performance of a dict "
"insertion, *O*\\ (*n*\\ :sup:`2`) complexity.  See https://ocert.org/"
"advisories/ocert-2011-003.html for details."
msgstr ""
"這是為了防範因精心挑選的輸入而造成的阻斷服務攻擊 (denial-of-service)，這些輸"
"入會利用 dict 插入操作的最壞情況效能，也就是 *O*\\ (*n*\\ :sup:`2`) 複雜度。"
"詳情請見 https://ocert.org/advisories/ocert-2011-003.html 。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2303
msgid ""
"Changing hash values affects the iteration order of sets. Python has never "
"made guarantees about this ordering (and it typically varies between 32-bit "
"and 64-bit builds)."
msgstr ""
"改變雜湊值會影響集合的疊代順序。Python 從未對此順序做出任何保證（而且它通常"
"在 32 位元和 64 位元建置之間有所不同）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2307
msgid "See also :envvar:`PYTHONHASHSEED`."
msgstr "另請參閱 :envvar:`PYTHONHASHSEED`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2309
msgid "Hash randomization is enabled by default."
msgstr "雜湊隨機化預設為啟用。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2317
msgid ""
"Called to implement truth value testing and the built-in operation "
"``bool()``; should return ``False`` or ``True``.  When this method is not "
"defined, :meth:`~object.__len__` is called, if it is defined, and the object "
"is considered true if its result is nonzero.  If a class defines neither :"
"meth:`!__len__` nor :meth:`!__bool__` (which is true of the :class:`object` "
"class itself), all its instances are considered true."
msgstr ""
"用來實作真值測試和內建操作 ``bool()``；應回傳 ``False`` 或 ``True``。當此方法"
"未定義時，如果有定義 :meth:`~object.__len__`，則會呼叫它，且當其結果不為零"
"時，該物件被視為真。如果類別既沒有定義 :meth:`!__len__` 也沒有定義 :meth:`!"
"__bool__`\\ （:class:`object` 類別本身即是如此），則其所有實例都被視為真。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2328
msgid "Customizing attribute access"
msgstr "自訂屬性存取"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2330
msgid ""
"The following methods can be defined to customize the meaning of attribute "
"access (use of, assignment to, or deletion of ``x.name``) for class "
"instances."
msgstr ""
"可以定義以下方法來自訂類別實例的屬性存取（使用、賦值或刪除 ``x.name``）的意"
"義。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2338
msgid ""
"Called when the default attribute access fails with an :exc:`AttributeError` "
"(either :meth:`__getattribute__` raises an :exc:`AttributeError` because "
"*name* is not an instance attribute or an attribute in the class tree for "
"``self``; or :meth:`__get__` of a *name* property raises :exc:"
"`AttributeError`).  This method should either return the (computed) "
"attribute value or raise an :exc:`AttributeError` exception. The :class:"
"`object` class itself does not provide this method."
msgstr ""
"當預設的屬性存取因 :exc:`AttributeError` 而失敗時呼叫（可能是 :meth:"
"`__getattribute__` 因為 *name* 既不是實例屬性、也不是 ``self`` 類別樹中的屬性"
"而引發 :exc:`AttributeError`；或者是 *name* property 的 :meth:`__get__` 引發"
"了 :exc:`AttributeError`）。此方法應該回傳（計算後的）屬性值，或是引發 :exc:"
"`AttributeError` 例外。:class:`object` 類別本身不提供此方法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2346
msgid ""
"Note that if the attribute is found through the normal mechanism, :meth:"
"`__getattr__` is not called.  (This is an intentional asymmetry between :"
"meth:`__getattr__` and :meth:`__setattr__`.) This is done both for "
"efficiency reasons and because otherwise :meth:`__getattr__` would have no "
"way to access other attributes of the instance.  Note that at least for "
"instance variables, you can take total control by not inserting any values "
"in the instance attribute dictionary (but instead inserting them in another "
"object).  See the :meth:`__getattribute__` method below for a way to "
"actually get total control over attribute access."
msgstr ""
"請注意，如果透過正常機制找到了該屬性，就不會呼叫 :meth:`__getattr__`。（這"
"是 :meth:`__getattr__` 和 :meth:`__setattr__` 之間刻意設計的不對稱。）這麼做"
"既是出於效率考量，也是因為若非如此，:meth:`__getattr__` 將無法存取實例的其他"
"屬性。請注意，至少對於實例變數來說，你可以透過不在實例屬性字典中插入任何值"
"（而是將它們插入另一個物件中）來取得完全的控制權。關於如何真正取得屬性存取的"
"完全控制權，請參閱下方的 :meth:`__getattribute__` 方法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2359
msgid ""
"Called unconditionally to implement attribute accesses for instances of the "
"class. If the class also defines :meth:`__getattr__`, the latter will not be "
"called unless :meth:`__getattribute__` either calls it explicitly or raises "
"an :exc:`AttributeError`. This method should return the (computed) attribute "
"value or raise an :exc:`AttributeError` exception. In order to avoid "
"infinite recursion in this method, its implementation should always call the "
"base class method with the same name to access any attributes it needs, for "
"example, ``object.__getattribute__(self, name)``."
msgstr ""
"無條件地被呼叫，用來實作類別實例的屬性存取。如果類別也定義了 :meth:"
"`__getattr__`，除非 :meth:`__getattribute__` 明確呼叫它或引發 :exc:"
"`AttributeError`，否則後者不會被呼叫。此方法應該回傳（計算後的）屬性值，或是"
"引發 :exc:`AttributeError` 例外。為了避免此方法中發生無限遞迴，其實作應該總是"
"呼叫同名的基底類別方法來存取它需要的任何屬性，例如 ``object."
"__getattribute__(self, name)``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2370
msgid ""
"This method may still be bypassed when looking up special methods as the "
"result of implicit invocation via language syntax or :ref:`built-in "
"functions <builtin-functions>`. See :ref:`special-lookup`."
msgstr ""
"當透過語言語法或\\ :ref:`內建函式 <builtin-functions>`\\ 隱式呼叫而查找特殊方"
"法時，仍可能略過此方法。請參閱\\ :ref:`special-lookup`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2375 ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2377
msgid ""
"For certain sensitive attribute accesses, raises an :ref:`auditing event "
"<auditing>` ``object.__getattr__`` with arguments ``obj`` and ``name``."
msgstr ""
"對於某些敏感的屬性存取，會引發一個附帶引數 ``obj`` 與 ``name`` 的\\ :ref:`稽"
"核事件 <auditing>` ``object.__getattr__``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2384
msgid ""
"Called when an attribute assignment is attempted.  This is called instead of "
"the normal mechanism (i.e. store the value in the instance dictionary). "
"*name* is the attribute name, *value* is the value to be assigned to it."
msgstr ""
"在嘗試進行屬性賦值時呼叫。此方法會取代正常機制（即將值儲存在實例字典中）。"
"*name* 是屬性名稱，*value* 是要指派給它的值。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2388
msgid ""
"If :meth:`__setattr__` wants to assign to an instance attribute, it should "
"call the base class method with the same name, for example, ``object."
"__setattr__(self, name, value)``."
msgstr ""
"如果 :meth:`__setattr__` 想要對實例屬性賦值，它應該呼叫同名的基底類別方法，例"
"如 ``object.__setattr__(self, name, value)``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2392 ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2394
msgid ""
"For certain sensitive attribute assignments, raises an :ref:`auditing event "
"<auditing>` ``object.__setattr__`` with arguments ``obj``, ``name``, "
"``value``."
msgstr ""
"對於某些敏感的屬性賦值，會引發一個附帶引數 ``obj``、``name``、``value`` 的"
"\\ :ref:`稽核事件 <auditing>` ``object.__setattr__``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2401
msgid ""
"Like :meth:`__setattr__` but for attribute deletion instead of assignment.  "
"This should only be implemented if ``del obj.name`` is meaningful for the "
"object."
msgstr ""
"與 :meth:`__setattr__` 類似，但用於屬性刪除而非賦值。只有在 ``del obj.name`` "
"對該物件有意義時才應實作此方法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2404 ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2406
msgid ""
"For certain sensitive attribute deletions, raises an :ref:`auditing event "
"<auditing>` ``object.__delattr__`` with arguments ``obj`` and ``name``."
msgstr ""
"對於某些敏感的屬性刪除，會引發一個附帶引數 ``obj`` 與 ``name`` 的\\ :ref:`稽"
"核事件 <auditing>` ``object.__delattr__``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2413
msgid ""
"Called when :func:`dir` is called on the object. An iterable must be "
"returned. :func:`dir` converts the returned iterable to a list and sorts it."
msgstr ""
"在對物件呼叫 :func:`dir` 時呼叫。必須回傳一個可疊代物件。:func:`dir` 會將回傳"
"的可疊代物件轉換為串列並加以排序。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2418
msgid "Customizing module attribute access"
msgstr "自訂模組屬性存取"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2428
msgid ""
"Special names ``__getattr__`` and ``__dir__`` can be also used to customize "
"access to module attributes. The ``__getattr__`` function at the module "
"level should accept one argument which is the name of an attribute and "
"return the computed value or raise an :exc:`AttributeError`. If an attribute "
"is not found on a module object through the normal lookup, i.e. :meth:"
"`object.__getattribute__`, then ``__getattr__`` is searched in the module "
"``__dict__`` before raising an :exc:`AttributeError`. If found, it is called "
"with the attribute name and the result is returned."
msgstr ""
"特殊名稱 ``__getattr__`` 和 ``__dir__`` 也可以用來自訂對模組屬性的存取。模組"
"層級的 ``__getattr__`` 函式應接受一個引數，即屬性名稱，並回傳計算後的值或引"
"發 :exc:`AttributeError`。如果透過正常查找（即 :meth:`object."
"__getattribute__`）在模組物件上找不到某個屬性，則在引發 :exc:"
"`AttributeError` 之前，會先在模組的 ``__dict__`` 中搜尋 ``__getattr__``。如果"
"找到了，就會以屬性名稱呼叫它並回傳其結果。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2437
msgid ""
"The ``__dir__`` function should accept no arguments, and return an iterable "
"of strings that represents the names accessible on module. If present, this "
"function overrides the standard :func:`dir` search on a module."
msgstr ""
"``__dir__`` 函式不應接受任何引數，並應回傳一個字串的可疊代物件，代表模組上可"
"存取的名稱。如果存在，此函式會覆寫模組上的標準 :func:`dir` 搜尋。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2443
msgid ""
"For a more fine grained customization of the module behavior (setting "
"attributes, properties, etc.), one can set the ``__class__`` attribute of a "
"module object to a subclass of :class:`types.ModuleType`. For example::"
msgstr ""
"若要對模組行為進行更細緻的自訂（設定屬性、property 等），可以將模組物件的 "
"``__class__`` 屬性設為 :class:`types.ModuleType` 的子類別。例如： ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2447
msgid ""
"import sys\n"
"from types import ModuleType\n"
"\n"
"class VerboseModule(ModuleType):\n"
"    def __repr__(self):\n"
"        return f'Verbose {self.__name__}'\n"
"\n"
"    def __setattr__(self, attr, value):\n"
"        print(f'Setting {attr}...')\n"
"        super().__setattr__(attr, value)\n"
"\n"
"sys.modules[__name__].__class__ = VerboseModule"
msgstr ""
"import sys\n"
"from types import ModuleType\n"
"\n"
"class VerboseModule(ModuleType):\n"
"    def __repr__(self):\n"
"        return f'Verbose {self.__name__}'\n"
"\n"
"    def __setattr__(self, attr, value):\n"
"        print(f'Setting {attr}...')\n"
"        super().__setattr__(attr, value)\n"
"\n"
"sys.modules[__name__].__class__ = VerboseModule"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2461
msgid ""
"Defining module ``__getattr__`` and setting module ``__class__`` only affect "
"lookups made using the attribute access syntax -- directly accessing the "
"module globals (whether by code within the module, or via a reference to the "
"module's globals dictionary) is unaffected."
msgstr ""
"定義模組的 ``__getattr__`` 和設定模組的 ``__class__`` 只會影響使用屬性存取語"
"法進行的查找 -- 直接存取模組的全域變數（無論是透過模組內的程式碼，還是透過對"
"模組全域變數字典的參照）則不受影響。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2466
msgid "``__class__`` module attribute is now writable."
msgstr "``__class__`` 模組屬性現在是可寫入的。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2469
msgid "``__getattr__`` and ``__dir__`` module attributes."
msgstr "``__getattr__`` 和 ``__dir__`` 模組屬性。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2474
msgid ":pep:`562` - Module __getattr__ and __dir__"
msgstr ":pep:`562` - 模組 __getattr__ 和 __dir__"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2475
msgid "Describes the ``__getattr__`` and ``__dir__`` functions on modules."
msgstr "描述模組上的 ``__getattr__`` 和 ``__dir__`` 函式。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2481
msgid "Implementing Descriptors"
msgstr "實作描述器"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2483
msgid ""
"The following methods only apply when an instance of the class containing "
"the method (a so-called *descriptor* class) appears in an *owner* class (the "
"descriptor must be in either the owner's class dictionary or in the class "
"dictionary for one of its parents).  In the examples below, \"the "
"attribute\" refers to the attribute whose name is the key of the property in "
"the owner class' :attr:`~object.__dict__`.  The :class:`object` class itself "
"does not implement any of these protocols."
msgstr ""
"以下方法只在包含該方法的類別（所謂的\\ *描述器*\\ 類別）的實例出現在\\ *擁有"
"者* (owner) 類別中時才適用（描述器必須位於擁有者的類別字典中，或位於其某個父"
"類別的類別字典中）。在以下範例中，「該屬性」指的是名稱為擁有者類別 :attr:"
"`~object.__dict__` 中該項目之鍵的那個屬性。:class:`object` 類別本身沒有實作任"
"何這些協定。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2493
msgid ""
"Called to get the attribute of the owner class (class attribute access) or "
"of an instance of that class (instance attribute access). The optional "
"*owner* argument is the owner class, while *instance* is the instance that "
"the attribute was accessed through, or ``None`` when the attribute is "
"accessed through the *owner*."
msgstr ""
"用來取得擁有者類別的屬性（類別屬性存取）或該類別實例的屬性（實例屬性存取）。"
"可選的 *owner* 引數是擁有者類別，而 *instance* 是用來存取該屬性的實例，若屬性"
"是透過 *owner* 存取的則為 ``None``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2499
msgid ""
"This method should return the computed attribute value or raise an :exc:"
"`AttributeError` exception."
msgstr "此方法應該回傳計算後的屬性值，或引發 :exc:`AttributeError` 例外。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2502
msgid ""
":PEP:`252` specifies that :meth:`__get__` is callable with one or two "
"arguments.  Python's own built-in descriptors support this specification; "
"however, it is likely that some third-party tools have descriptors that "
"require both arguments.  Python's own :meth:`__getattribute__` "
"implementation always passes in both arguments whether they are required or "
"not."
msgstr ""
":PEP:`252` 規定 :meth:`__get__` 可以用一個或兩個引數呼叫。Python 自身的內建描"
"述器支援此規格；然而，某些第三方工具很可能有需要兩個引數的描述器。Python 自身"
"的 :meth:`__getattribute__` 實作無論是否需要，總是會傳入兩個引數。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2511
msgid ""
"Called to set the attribute on an instance *instance* of the owner class to "
"a new value, *value*."
msgstr "用來將擁有者類別的實例 *instance* 上的屬性設為新值 *value*。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2514
msgid ""
"Note, adding :meth:`__set__` or :meth:`__delete__` changes the kind of "
"descriptor to a \"data descriptor\".  See :ref:`descriptor-invocation` for "
"more details."
msgstr ""
"請注意，新增 :meth:`__set__` 或 :meth:`__delete__` 會將描述器的種類變更為「資"
"料描述器」。詳情請參閱\\ :ref:`descriptor-invocation`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2520
msgid ""
"Called to delete the attribute on an instance *instance* of the owner class."
msgstr "用來刪除擁有者類別的實例 *instance* 上的屬性。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2522
msgid ""
"Instances of descriptors may also have the :attr:`!__objclass__` attribute "
"present:"
msgstr "描述器的實例也可能具有 :attr:`!__objclass__` 屬性："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2527
msgid ""
"The attribute :attr:`!__objclass__` is interpreted by the :mod:`inspect` "
"module as specifying the class where this object was defined (setting this "
"appropriately can assist in runtime introspection of dynamic class "
"attributes). For callables, it may indicate that an instance of the given "
"type (or a subclass) is expected or required as the first positional "
"argument (for example, CPython sets this attribute for unbound methods that "
"are implemented in C)."
msgstr ""
":mod:`inspect` 模組會將 :attr:`!__objclass__` 屬性解讀為指定此物件被定義於哪"
"個類別（適當地設定此屬性有助於動態類別屬性的 runtime 內省）。對於可呼叫物件，"
"它可能表示第一個位置引數預期或必須是給定型別（或其子類別）的實例（例如，"
"CPython 會為以 C 實作的未繫結方法設定此屬性）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2538
msgid "Invoking Descriptors"
msgstr "呼叫描述器"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2540
msgid ""
"In general, a descriptor is an object attribute with \"binding behavior\", "
"one whose attribute access has been overridden by methods in the descriptor "
"protocol:  :meth:`~object.__get__`, :meth:`~object.__set__`, and :meth:"
"`~object.__delete__`. If any of those methods are defined for an object, it "
"is said to be a descriptor."
msgstr ""
"一般來說，描述器是具有「繫結行為 (binding behavior)」的物件屬性，其屬性存取已"
"被描述器協定中的方法所覆寫：:meth:`~object.__get__`、:meth:`~object.__set__` "
"和 :meth:`~object.__delete__`。如果一個物件定義了其中任何一個方法，它就被稱為"
"描述器。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2546
msgid ""
"The default behavior for attribute access is to get, set, or delete the "
"attribute from an object's dictionary. For instance, ``a.x`` has a lookup "
"chain starting with ``a.__dict__['x']``, then ``type(a).__dict__['x']``, and "
"continuing through the base classes of ``type(a)`` excluding metaclasses."
msgstr ""
"屬性存取的預設行為是從物件的字典中取得、設定或刪除屬性。例如，``a.x`` 有一個"
"查找鏈，從 ``a.__dict__['x']`` 開始，然後是 ``type(a).__dict__['x']``，並沿"
"著 ``type(a)`` 的基底類別（不包括元類別）繼續查找。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2551
msgid ""
"However, if the looked-up value is an object defining one of the descriptor "
"methods, then Python may override the default behavior and invoke the "
"descriptor method instead.  Where this occurs in the precedence chain "
"depends on which descriptor methods were defined and how they were called."
msgstr ""
"然而，如果查找到的值是定義了其中一個描述器方法的物件，那麼 Python 可能會覆寫"
"預設行為並改為呼叫描述器方法。這在優先順序鏈中發生的位置，取決於定義了哪些描"
"述器方法以及它們是如何被呼叫的。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2556
msgid ""
"The starting point for descriptor invocation is a binding, ``a.x``. How the "
"arguments are assembled depends on ``a``:"
msgstr "描述器呼叫的起點是一個繫結 ``a.x``。引數如何組合取決於 ``a``："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2559
msgid "Direct Call"
msgstr "直接呼叫"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2560
msgid ""
"The simplest and least common call is when user code directly invokes a "
"descriptor method:    ``x.__get__(a)``."
msgstr ""
"最簡單但也最不常見的呼叫，是使用者程式碼直接呼叫描述器方法：``x."
"__get__(a)``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2563
msgid "Instance Binding"
msgstr "實例繫結"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2564
msgid ""
"If binding to an object instance, ``a.x`` is transformed into the call: "
"``type(a).__dict__['x'].__get__(a, type(a))``."
msgstr ""
"如果繫結到物件實例，``a.x`` 會被轉換為呼叫：``type(a).__dict__['x']."
"__get__(a, type(a))``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2567
msgid "Class Binding"
msgstr "類別繫結"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2568
msgid ""
"If binding to a class, ``A.x`` is transformed into the call: ``A."
"__dict__['x'].__get__(None, A)``."
msgstr ""
"如果繫結到類別，``A.x`` 會被轉換為呼叫：``A.__dict__['x'].__get__(None, "
"A)``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2571
msgid "Super Binding"
msgstr "super 繫結"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2572
msgid ""
"A dotted lookup such as ``super(A, a).x`` searches ``a.__class__.__mro__`` "
"for a base class ``B`` following ``A`` and then returns ``B.__dict__['x']."
"__get__(a, A)``.  If not a descriptor, ``x`` is returned unchanged."
msgstr ""
"像 ``super(A, a).x`` 這樣的點號查找，會在 ``a.__class__.__mro__`` 中搜尋位於 "
"``A`` 之後的基底類別 ``B``，然後回傳 ``B.__dict__['x'].__get__(a, A)``。如果"
"不是描述器，則 ``x`` 會原封不動地回傳。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2609
msgid ""
"For instance bindings, the precedence of descriptor invocation depends on "
"which descriptor methods are defined.  A descriptor can define any "
"combination of :meth:`~object.__get__`, :meth:`~object.__set__` and :meth:"
"`~object.__delete__`.  If it does not define :meth:`!__get__`, then "
"accessing the attribute will return the descriptor object itself unless "
"there is a value in the object's instance dictionary.  If the descriptor "
"defines :meth:`!__set__` and/or :meth:`!__delete__`, it is a data "
"descriptor; if it defines neither, it is a non-data descriptor.  Normally, "
"data descriptors define both :meth:`!__get__` and :meth:`!__set__`, while "
"non-data descriptors have just the :meth:`!__get__` method.  Data "
"descriptors with :meth:`!__get__` and :meth:`!__set__` (and/or :meth:`!"
"__delete__`) defined always override a redefinition in an instance "
"dictionary.  In contrast, non-data descriptors can be overridden by "
"instances."
msgstr ""
"對於實例繫結，描述器呼叫的優先順序取決於定義了哪些描述器方法。描述器可以定"
"義 :meth:`~object.__get__`、:meth:`~object.__set__` 和 :meth:`~object."
"__delete__` 的任意組合。如果它沒有定義 :meth:`!__get__`，那麼存取該屬性將回傳"
"描述器物件本身，除非物件的實例字典中有一個值。如果描述器定義了 :meth:`!"
"__set__` 和/或 :meth:`!__delete__`，它就是資料描述器；如果兩者都沒有定義，它"
"就是非資料描述器。通常資料描述器會同時定義 :meth:`!__get__` 和 :meth:`!"
"__set__`，而非資料描述器只有 :meth:`!__get__` 方法。定義了 :meth:`!__get__` "
"和 :meth:`!__set__`\\ （和/或 :meth:`!__delete__`）的資料描述器，總是會覆寫實"
"例字典中的重新定義。相反地，非資料描述器可以被實例覆寫。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2624
msgid ""
"Python methods (including those decorated with :deco:`staticmethod` and :"
"deco:`classmethod`) are implemented as non-data descriptors.  Accordingly, "
"instances can redefine and override methods.  This allows individual "
"instances to acquire behaviors that differ from other instances of the same "
"class."
msgstr ""
"Python 方法（包括以 :deco:`staticmethod` 和 :deco:`classmethod` 裝飾的方法）"
"是以非資料描述器實作的。因此，實例可以重新定義和覆寫方法。這讓個別實例能夠擁"
"有與同一類別其他實例不同的行為。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2630
msgid ""
"The :deco:`property` decorator is implemented as a data descriptor. "
"Accordingly, instances cannot override the behavior of a property."
msgstr ""
":deco:`property` 裝飾器是以資料描述器實作的。因此，實例無法覆寫 property 的行"
"為。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2637
msgid "__slots__"
msgstr "__slots__"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2639
msgid ""
"*__slots__* allow us to explicitly declare data members (like properties) "
"and deny the creation of :attr:`~object.__dict__` and *__weakref__* (unless "
"explicitly declared in *__slots__* or available in a parent.)"
msgstr ""
"*__slots__* 可以明確宣告資料成員（類似 property），並拒絕建立 :attr:`~object."
"__dict__` 和 *__weakref__*\\ （除非在 *__slots__* 中明確宣告，或在父類別中可"
"用）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2643
msgid ""
"The space saved over using :attr:`~object.__dict__` can be significant. "
"Attribute lookup speed can be significantly improved as well."
msgstr ""
"相較於使用 :attr:`~object.__dict__`，所節省的空間可能相當可觀。屬性查找速度也"
"能大幅提升。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2648
msgid ""
"This class variable can be assigned a string, iterable, or sequence of "
"strings with variable names used by instances.  *__slots__* reserves space "
"for the declared variables and prevents the automatic creation of :attr:"
"`~object.__dict__` and *__weakref__* for each instance."
msgstr ""
"這個類別變數可以被指派為一個字串、可疊代物件，或是由實例所使用的變數名稱組成"
"的字串序列。*__slots__* 會為宣告的變數保留空間，並防止為每個實例自動建立 :"
"attr:`~object.__dict__` 和 *__weakref__*。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2657
msgid "Notes on using *__slots__*:"
msgstr "使用 *__slots__* 的注意事項："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2659
msgid ""
"When inheriting from a class without *__slots__*, the :attr:`~object."
"__dict__` and *__weakref__* attribute of the instances will always be "
"accessible."
msgstr ""
"當繼承自沒有 *__slots__* 的類別時，實例的 :attr:`~object.__dict__` 和 "
"*__weakref__* 屬性一定可以存取。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2663
msgid ""
"Without a :attr:`~object.__dict__` variable, instances cannot be assigned "
"new variables not listed in the *__slots__* definition.  Attempts to assign "
"to an unlisted variable name raises :exc:`AttributeError`. If dynamic "
"assignment of new variables is desired, then add ``'__dict__'`` to the "
"sequence of strings in the *__slots__* declaration."
msgstr ""
"沒有 :attr:`~object.__dict__` 變數時，實例無法被指派未列在 *__slots__* 定義中"
"的新變數。嘗試對未列出的變數名稱賦值會引發 :exc:`AttributeError`。如果需要動"
"態指派新變數，請將 ``'__dict__'`` 加入 *__slots__* 宣告中的字串序列。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2670
msgid ""
"Without a *__weakref__* variable for each instance, classes defining "
"*__slots__* do not support :mod:`weak references <weakref>` to its "
"instances. If weak reference support is needed, then add ``'__weakref__'`` "
"to the sequence of strings in the *__slots__* declaration."
msgstr ""
"若每個實例沒有 *__weakref__* 變數，定義了 *__slots__* 的類別就不支援對其實例"
"的\\ :mod:`弱參照 <weakref>`。如果需要弱參照支援，請將 ``'__weakref__'`` 加"
"入 *__slots__* 宣告中的字串序列。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2676
msgid ""
"*__slots__* are implemented at the class level by creating :ref:`descriptors "
"<descriptors>` for each variable name.  As a result, class attributes cannot "
"be used to set default values for instance variables defined by *__slots__*; "
"otherwise, the class attribute would overwrite the descriptor assignment."
msgstr ""
"*__slots__* 是在類別層級透過為每個變數名稱建立\\ :ref:`描述器 "
"<descriptors>`\\ 來實作的。因此，類別屬性不能用來為 *__slots__* 所定義的實例"
"變數設定預設值；否則類別屬性會覆蓋描述器的指派。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2682
msgid ""
"The action of a *__slots__* declaration is not limited to the class where it "
"is defined.  *__slots__* declared in parents are available in child classes. "
"However, instances of a child subclass will get a :attr:`~object.__dict__` "
"and *__weakref__* unless the subclass also defines *__slots__* (which should "
"only contain names of any *additional* slots)."
msgstr ""
"*__slots__* 宣告的作用不僅限於定義它的類別。在父類別中宣告的 *__slots__* 在子"
"類別中也可以使用。然而，子類別的實例會得到 :attr:`~object.__dict__` 和 "
"*__weakref__*，除非子類別也定義了 *__slots__*\\ （其中應該只包含任何\\ *額外"
"* slot 的名稱）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2688
msgid ""
"If a class defines a slot also defined in a base class, the instance "
"variable defined by the base class slot is inaccessible (except by "
"retrieving its descriptor directly from the base class). This renders the "
"meaning of the program undefined.  In the future, a check may be added to "
"prevent this."
msgstr ""
"如果類別定義了一個在基底類別中也有定義的 slot，則由基底類別 slot 所定義的實例"
"變數將無法存取（除非直接從基底類別取得其描述器）。這會使程式的意義變得未定"
"義。未來可能會加入檢查來防止這種情況。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2693
msgid ""
":exc:`TypeError` will be raised if *__slots__* other than *__dict__* and "
"*__weakref__* are defined for a class derived from a :c:member:`\"variable-"
"length\" built-in type <PyTypeObject.tp_itemsize>` such as :class:`int`, :"
"class:`bytes`, and :class:`type`, except :class:`tuple`."
msgstr ""
"如果為衍生自\\ :c:member:`「可變長度」內建型別 <PyTypeObject.tp_itemsize>`\\ "
"（例如 :class:`int`、:class:`bytes` 與 :class:`type`，但 :class:`tuple` 除"
"外）的類別定義了 *__dict__* 和 *__weakref__* 以外的 *__slots__*，則會引發 :"
"exc:`TypeError`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2698
msgid "Any non-string :term:`iterable` may be assigned to *__slots__*."
msgstr ""
"任何非字串的\\ :term:`可疊代物件 <iterable>`\\ 都可以被指派給 *__slots__*。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2700
msgid ""
"If a :class:`dictionary <dict>` is used to assign *__slots__*, the "
"dictionary keys will be used as the slot names. The values of the dictionary "
"can be used to provide per-attribute docstrings that will be recognised by :"
"func:`inspect.getdoc` and displayed in the output of :func:`help`."
msgstr ""
"如果使用\\ :class:`字典 <dict>`\\ 來指派 *__slots__*，字典的鍵將被用作 slot "
"名稱。字典的值可以用來為每個屬性提供說明字串，這些說明字串會被 :func:"
"`inspect.getdoc` 識別，並顯示在 :func:`help` 的輸出中。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2705
msgid ""
":attr:`~object.__class__` assignment works only if both classes have the "
"same *__slots__*."
msgstr ""
"只有當兩個類別具有相同的 *__slots__* 時，:attr:`~object.__class__` 賦值才有"
"效。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2708
msgid ""
":ref:`Multiple inheritance <multiple-inheritance>` with multiple slotted "
"parent classes can be used, but only one parent is allowed to have "
"attributes created by slots (the other bases must have empty slot layouts) - "
"violations raise :exc:`TypeError`."
msgstr ""
"可以使用具有多個帶有 slot 之父類別的\\ :ref:`多重繼承 <multiple-"
"inheritance>`，但只允許其中一個父類別擁有由 slot 建立的屬性（其他基底必須具有"
"空的 slot 佈局）；違反此規則會引發 :exc:`TypeError`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2714
msgid ""
"If an :term:`iterator` is used for *__slots__* then a :term:`descriptor` is "
"created for each of the iterator's values. However, the *__slots__* "
"attribute will be an empty iterator."
msgstr ""
"如果將\\ :term:`疊代器 <iterator>`\\ 用於 *__slots__*，則會為疊代器的每個值建"
"立一個\\ :term:`描述器 <descriptor>`。然而，*__slots__* 屬性將會是一個空的疊"
"代器。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2719
msgid ""
"Allowed defining the *__dict__* and *__weakref__* *__slots__* for any class. "
"Allowed defining any *__slots__* for a class derived from :class:`tuple`."
msgstr ""
"允許為任何類別定義 *__dict__* 和 *__weakref__* 的 *__slots__*。允許為衍生自 :"
"class:`tuple` 的類別定義任何 *__slots__*。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2727
msgid "Customizing class creation"
msgstr "自訂類別建立"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2729
msgid ""
"Whenever a class inherits from another class, :meth:`~object."
"__init_subclass__` is called on the parent class. This way, it is possible "
"to write classes which change the behavior of subclasses. This is closely "
"related to class decorators, but where class decorators only affect the "
"specific class they're applied to, ``__init_subclass__`` solely applies to "
"future subclasses of the class defining the method."
msgstr ""
"每當一個類別繼承自另一個類別時，就會在父類別上呼叫 :meth:`~object."
"__init_subclass__`。如此一來，就可以撰寫能改變子類別行為的類別。這與類別裝飾"
"器密切相關，但類別裝飾器只會影響它們所套用的特定類別，而 "
"``__init_subclass__`` 只適用於定義此方法之類別的未來子類別。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2738
msgid ""
"This method is called whenever the containing class is subclassed. *cls* is "
"then the new subclass. If defined as a normal instance method, this method "
"is implicitly converted to a class method."
msgstr ""
"每當包含此方法的類別被子類別化時，就會呼叫此方法。此時 *cls* 是新的子類別。如"
"果它被定義為一般的實例方法，則此方法會被隱式地轉換為類別方法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2742
msgid ""
"Keyword arguments which are given to a new class are passed to the parent "
"class's ``__init_subclass__``. For compatibility with other classes using "
"``__init_subclass__``, one should take out the needed keyword arguments and "
"pass the others over to the base class, as in::"
msgstr ""
"傳給新類別的關鍵字引數會被傳遞給父類別的 ``__init_subclass__``。為了與其他使"
"用 ``__init_subclass__`` 的類別相容，應該取出所需的關鍵字引數，並將其餘的傳遞"
"給基底類別，如下所示： ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2748
msgid ""
"class Philosopher:\n"
"    def __init_subclass__(cls, /, default_name, **kwargs):\n"
"        super().__init_subclass__(**kwargs)\n"
"        cls.default_name = default_name\n"
"\n"
"class AustralianPhilosopher(Philosopher, default_name=\"Bruce\"):\n"
"    pass"
msgstr ""
"class Philosopher:\n"
"    def __init_subclass__(cls, /, default_name, **kwargs):\n"
"        super().__init_subclass__(**kwargs)\n"
"        cls.default_name = default_name\n"
"\n"
"class AustralianPhilosopher(Philosopher, default_name=\"Bruce\"):\n"
"    pass"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2756
msgid ""
"The default implementation ``object.__init_subclass__`` does nothing, but "
"raises an error if it is called with any arguments."
msgstr ""
"預設實作 ``object.__init_subclass__`` 不做任何事，但如果在呼叫時帶有任何引"
"數，則會引發錯誤。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2761
msgid ""
"The metaclass hint ``metaclass`` is consumed by the rest of the type "
"machinery, and is never passed to ``__init_subclass__`` implementations. The "
"actual metaclass (rather than the explicit hint) can be accessed as "
"``type(cls)``."
msgstr ""
"元類別提示 ``metaclass`` 會被型別機制的其餘部分取用，且永遠不會被傳遞給 "
"``__init_subclass__`` 的實作。實際的元類別（而非明確的提示）可以透過 "
"``type(cls)`` 存取。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2769
msgid ""
"When a class is created, :meth:`!type.__new__` scans the class variables and "
"makes callbacks to those with a :meth:`~object.__set_name__` hook."
msgstr ""
"當類別被建立時，:meth:`!type.__new__` 會掃描類別變數，並對具有 :meth:"
"`~object.__set_name__` 掛鉤的變數進行回呼。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2774
msgid ""
"Automatically called at the time the owning class *owner* is created. The "
"object has been assigned to *name* in that class::"
msgstr ""
"在擁有者類別 *owner* 被建立時自動呼叫。該物件已在該類別中被指派給 *name*： ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2777
msgid ""
"class A:\n"
"    x = C()  # Automatically calls: x.__set_name__(A, 'x')"
msgstr ""
"class A:\n"
"    x = C()  # 自動呼叫：x.__set_name__(A, 'x')"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2780
msgid ""
"If the class variable is assigned after the class is created, :meth:"
"`__set_name__` will not be called automatically. If needed, :meth:"
"`__set_name__` can be called directly::"
msgstr ""
"如果類別變數是在類別建立之後才被指派，則不會自動呼叫 :meth:`__set_name__`。如"
"有需要，可以直接呼叫 :meth:`__set_name__`： ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2784
msgid ""
"class A:\n"
"   pass\n"
"\n"
"c = C()\n"
"A.x = c                  # The hook is not called\n"
"c.__set_name__(A, 'x')   # Manually invoke the hook"
msgstr ""
"class A:\n"
"   pass\n"
"\n"
"c = C()\n"
"A.x = c                  # 掛鉤不會被呼叫\n"
"c.__set_name__(A, 'x')   # 手動呼叫掛鉤"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2791
msgid "See :ref:`class-object-creation` for more details."
msgstr "更多細節請見\\ :ref:`class-object-creation`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2799
msgid "Metaclasses"
msgstr "元類別"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2806
msgid ""
"By default, classes are constructed using :func:`type`. The class body is "
"executed in a new namespace and the class name is bound locally to the "
"result of ``type(name, bases, namespace)``."
msgstr ""
"預設情況下，類別是使用 :func:`type` 來建構的。類別主體會在一個新的命名空間中"
"執行，而類別名稱會在區域命名空間中被繫結到 ``type(name, bases, namespace)`` "
"的結果。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2810
msgid ""
"The class creation process can be customized by passing the ``metaclass`` "
"keyword argument in the class definition line, or by inheriting from an "
"existing class that included such an argument. In the following example, "
"both ``MyClass`` and ``MySubclass`` are instances of ``Meta``::"
msgstr ""
"類別建立的過程可以透過在類別定義的那一列傳入 ``metaclass`` 關鍵字引數，或繼承"
"自包含此類引數的現有類別來自訂。在以下範例中，``MyClass`` 和 ``MySubclass`` "
"都是 ``Meta`` 的實例： ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2815
msgid ""
"class Meta(type):\n"
"    pass\n"
"\n"
"class MyClass(metaclass=Meta):\n"
"    pass\n"
"\n"
"class MySubclass(MyClass):\n"
"    pass"
msgstr ""
"class Meta(type):\n"
"    pass\n"
"\n"
"class MyClass(metaclass=Meta):\n"
"    pass\n"
"\n"
"class MySubclass(MyClass):\n"
"    pass"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2824
msgid ""
"Any other keyword arguments that are specified in the class definition are "
"passed through to all metaclass operations described below."
msgstr ""
"在類別定義中指定的任何其他關鍵字引數，都會被傳遞給下面描述的所有元類別操作。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2827
msgid "When a class definition is executed, the following steps occur:"
msgstr "當執行類別定義時，會發生以下步驟："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2829
msgid "MRO entries are resolved;"
msgstr "解析 MRO 項目；"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2830
msgid "the appropriate metaclass is determined;"
msgstr "決定適當的元類別；"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2831
msgid "the class namespace is prepared;"
msgstr "準備類別命名空間；"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2832
msgid "the class body is executed;"
msgstr "執行類別主體；"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2833
msgid "the class object is created."
msgstr "建立類別物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2837
msgid "Resolving MRO entries"
msgstr "解析 MRO 項目"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2841
msgid ""
"If a base that appears in a class definition is not an instance of :class:"
"`type`, then an :meth:`!__mro_entries__` method is searched on the base. If "
"an :meth:`!__mro_entries__` method is found, the base is substituted with "
"the result of a call to :meth:`!__mro_entries__` when creating the class. "
"The method is called with the original bases tuple passed to the *bases* "
"parameter, and must return a tuple of classes that will be used instead of "
"the base. The returned tuple may be empty: in these cases, the original base "
"is ignored."
msgstr ""
"如果出現在類別定義中的基底不是 :class:`type` 的實例，則會在該基底上搜尋 :"
"meth:`!__mro_entries__` 方法。如果找到了 :meth:`!__mro_entries__` 方法，則在"
"建立類別時，該基底會被替換為呼叫 :meth:`!__mro_entries__` 的結果。呼叫此方法"
"時，原始的基底 tuple 會被傳給 *bases* 參數，且此方法必須回傳一個由類別組成的 "
"tuple，用來取代該基底。回傳的 tuple 可以是空的：在這種情況下，原始的基底會被"
"忽略。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2852
msgid ":func:`types.resolve_bases`"
msgstr ":func:`types.resolve_bases`"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2853
msgid "Dynamically resolve bases that are not instances of :class:`type`."
msgstr "動態解析不是 :class:`type` 實例的基底。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2855
msgid ":func:`types.get_original_bases`"
msgstr ":func:`types.get_original_bases`"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2856
msgid ""
"Retrieve a class's \"original bases\" prior to modifications by :meth:"
"`~object.__mro_entries__`."
msgstr "取得類別在被 :meth:`~object.__mro_entries__` 修改之前的「原始基底」。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2859
msgid ":pep:`560`"
msgstr ":pep:`560`"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2860
msgid "Core support for typing module and generic types."
msgstr "typing 模組與泛型型別的核心支援。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2866
msgid "Determining the appropriate metaclass"
msgstr "決定適當的元類別"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2870
msgid ""
"The appropriate metaclass for a class definition is determined as follows:"
msgstr "類別定義的適當元類別依照以下方式決定："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2872
msgid ""
"if no bases and no explicit metaclass are given, then :func:`type` is used;"
msgstr "如果沒有給定基底也沒有明確的元類別，則使用 :func:`type`；"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2873
msgid ""
"if an explicit metaclass is given and it is *not* an instance of :func:"
"`type`, then it is used directly as the metaclass;"
msgstr ""
"如果給定了明確的元類別，且它\\ *不是* :func:`type` 的實例，則直接將它用作元類"
"別；"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2875
msgid ""
"if an instance of :func:`type` is given as the explicit metaclass, or bases "
"are defined, then the most derived metaclass is used."
msgstr ""
"如果給定 :func:`type` 的實例作為明確的元類別，或是有定義基底，則使用最衍生的"
"元類別。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2878
msgid ""
"The most derived metaclass is selected from the explicitly specified "
"metaclass (if any) and the metaclasses (i.e. ``type(cls)``) of all specified "
"base classes. The most derived metaclass is one which is a subtype of *all* "
"of these candidate metaclasses. If none of the candidate metaclasses meets "
"that criterion, then the class definition will fail with ``TypeError``."
msgstr ""
"最衍生的元類別是從明確指定的元類別（如果有的話）和所有指定基底類別的元類別"
"（即 ``type(cls)``）中選出的。最衍生的元類別是同時為\\ *所有*\\ 候選元類別之"
"子型別的那一個。如果沒有任何候選元類別符合該條件，則類別定義將會失敗並引發 "
"``TypeError``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2888
msgid "Preparing the class namespace"
msgstr "準備類別命名空間"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2893
msgid ""
"Once the appropriate metaclass has been identified, then the class namespace "
"is prepared. If the metaclass has a ``__prepare__`` attribute, it is called "
"as ``namespace = metaclass.__prepare__(name, bases, **kwds)`` (where the "
"additional keyword arguments, if any, come from the class definition). The "
"``__prepare__`` method should be implemented as a :func:`classmethod "
"<classmethod>`. The namespace returned by ``__prepare__`` is passed in to "
"``__new__``, but when the final class object is created the namespace is "
"copied into a new ``dict``."
msgstr ""
"一旦確定了適當的元類別，就會準備類別命名空間。如果元類別有 ``__prepare__`` 屬"
"性，則會以 ``namespace = metaclass.__prepare__(name, bases, **kwds)`` 的形式"
"呼叫它（其中額外的關鍵字引數，如果有的話，來自類別定義）。``__prepare__`` 方"
"法應該被實作為 :func:`classmethod <classmethod>`。``__prepare__`` 所回傳的命"
"名空間會被傳入 ``__new__``，但在建立最終的類別物件時，該命名空間會被複製到一"
"個新的 ``dict`` 中。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2902
msgid ""
"If the metaclass has no ``__prepare__`` attribute, then the class namespace "
"is initialised as an empty ordered mapping."
msgstr ""
"如果元類別沒有 ``__prepare__`` 屬性，則類別命名空間會被初始化為一個空的有序對"
"映。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2907
msgid ":pep:`3115` - Metaclasses in Python 3000"
msgstr ":pep:`3115` - Python 3000 中的元類別"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2908
msgid "Introduced the ``__prepare__`` namespace hook"
msgstr "引入了 ``__prepare__`` 命名空間掛鉤"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2912
msgid "Executing the class body"
msgstr "執行類別主體"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2917
msgid ""
"The class body is executed (approximately) as ``exec(body, globals(), "
"namespace)``. The key difference from a normal call to :func:`exec` is that "
"lexical scoping allows the class body (including any methods) to reference "
"names from the current and outer scopes when the class definition occurs "
"inside a function."
msgstr ""
"類別主體會（大致上）以 ``exec(body, globals(), namespace)`` 的方式執行。與一"
"般呼叫 :func:`exec` 的主要差別在於，當類別定義出現在函式內部時，詞法作用域 "
"(lexical scoping) 允許類別主體（包括其中的任何方法）參照目前作用域和外層作用"
"域中的名稱。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2923
msgid ""
"However, even when the class definition occurs inside the function, methods "
"defined inside the class still cannot see names defined at the class scope. "
"Class variables must be accessed through the first parameter of instance or "
"class methods, or through the implicit lexically scoped ``__class__`` "
"reference described in the next section."
msgstr ""
"然而，即使類別定義出現在函式內部，類別內部定義的方法仍然無法看見在類別作用域"
"中定義的名稱。類別變數必須透過實例方法或類別方法的第一個參數來存取，或是透過"
"下一節所述、隱式且具詞法作用域的 ``__class__`` 參照來存取。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2932
msgid "Creating the class object"
msgstr "建立類別物件"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2939
msgid ""
"Once the class namespace has been populated by executing the class body, the "
"class object is created by calling ``metaclass(name, bases, namespace, "
"**kwds)`` (the additional keywords passed here are the same as those passed "
"to ``__prepare__``)."
msgstr ""
"一旦執行類別主體、填好類別命名空間之後，就會呼叫 ``metaclass(name, bases, "
"namespace, **kwds)`` 來建立類別物件（此處傳入的額外關鍵字與傳給 "
"``__prepare__`` 的相同）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2944
msgid ""
"This class object is the one that will be referenced by the zero-argument "
"form of :func:`super`. ``__class__`` is an implicit closure reference "
"created by the compiler if any methods in a class body refer to either "
"``__class__`` or ``super``. This allows the zero argument form of :func:"
"`super` to correctly identify the class being defined based on lexical "
"scoping, while the class or instance that was used to make the current call "
"is identified based on the first argument passed to the method."
msgstr ""
"這個類別物件就是零引數形式的 :func:`super` 所參照的物件。``__class__`` 是一個"
"隱式閉包參照，當類別主體中有任何方法參照 ``__class__`` 或 ``super`` 時，由編"
"譯器建立。這讓零引數形式的 :func:`super` 能夠根據詞法作用域正確識別正在定義的"
"類別，而用來進行目前呼叫的類別或實例，則是根據傳給該方法的第一個引數來識別。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2954
msgid ""
"In CPython 3.6 and later, the ``__class__`` cell is passed to the metaclass "
"as a ``__classcell__`` entry in the class namespace. If present, this must "
"be propagated up to the ``type.__new__`` call in order for the class to be "
"initialised correctly. Failing to do so will result in a :exc:`RuntimeError` "
"in Python 3.8."
msgstr ""
"在 CPython 3.6 及之後的版本中，``__class__`` cell 會作為類別命名空間中的 "
"``__classcell__`` 項目傳給元類別。如果存在，則必須將它向上傳遞至 ``type."
"__new__`` 呼叫，類別才能被正確地初始化。若未這麼做，在 Python 3.8 中將會導"
"致 :exc:`RuntimeError`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2960
msgid ""
"When using the default metaclass :class:`type`, or any metaclass that "
"ultimately calls ``type.__new__``, the following additional customization "
"steps are invoked after creating the class object:"
msgstr ""
"當使用預設的元類別 :class:`type`，或任何最終會呼叫 ``type.__new__`` 的元類別"
"時，在建立類別物件之後會執行以下額外的自訂步驟："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2964
msgid ""
"The ``type.__new__`` method collects all of the attributes in the class "
"namespace that define a :meth:`~object.__set_name__` method;"
msgstr ""
"``type.__new__`` 方法會收集類別命名空間中所有定義了 :meth:`~object."
"__set_name__` 方法的屬性；"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2966
msgid ""
"Those ``__set_name__`` methods are called with the class being defined and "
"the assigned name of that particular attribute;"
msgstr ""
"這些 ``__set_name__`` 方法會以正在定義的類別和該特定屬性被指派的名稱來呼叫；"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2968
msgid ""
"The :meth:`~object.__init_subclass__` hook is called on the immediate parent "
"of the new class in its method resolution order."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~object.__init_subclass__` 掛鉤會在新類別的方法解析順序中的直接父類別"
"上被呼叫。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2971
msgid ""
"After the class object is created, it is passed to the class decorators "
"included in the class definition (if any) and the resulting object is bound "
"in the local namespace as the defined class."
msgstr ""
"類別物件建立之後，會被傳給類別定義中所包含的類別裝飾器（如果有的話），而產生"
"的物件會作為所定義的類別被繫結到區域命名空間中。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2975
msgid ""
"When a new class is created by ``type.__new__``, the object provided as the "
"namespace parameter is copied to a new ordered mapping and the original "
"object is discarded. The new copy is wrapped in a read-only proxy, which "
"becomes the :attr:`~type.__dict__` attribute of the class object."
msgstr ""
"當新類別由 ``type.__new__`` 建立時，作為命名空間參數提供的物件會被複製到一個"
"新的有序對映中，而原始物件則會被丟棄。新的副本會被包裝在一個唯讀代理中，成為"
"該類別物件的 :attr:`~type.__dict__` 屬性。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2982
msgid ":pep:`3135` - New super"
msgstr ":pep:`3135` - 新的 super"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2983
msgid "Describes the implicit ``__class__`` closure reference"
msgstr "描述隱式的 ``__class__`` 閉包參照"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2987
msgid "Uses for metaclasses"
msgstr "元類別的用途"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2989
msgid ""
"The potential uses for metaclasses are boundless. Some ideas that have been "
"explored include enum, logging, interface checking, automatic delegation, "
"automatic property creation, proxies, frameworks, and automatic resource "
"locking/synchronization."
msgstr ""
"元類別的潛在用途是無窮的。已被探索過的一些想法包括列舉 (enum)、日誌記錄、介面"
"檢查、自動委派、自動建立 property、代理、框架，以及自動資源鎖定/同步。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2996
msgid "Customizing instance and subclass checks"
msgstr "自訂實例與子類別檢查"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:2998
msgid ""
"The following methods are used to override the default behavior of the :func:"
"`isinstance` and :func:`issubclass` built-in functions."
msgstr ""
"以下方法用於覆寫內建函式 :func:`isinstance` 和 :func:`issubclass` 的預設行"
"為。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3001
msgid ""
"In particular, the metaclass :class:`abc.ABCMeta` implements these methods "
"in order to allow the addition of Abstract Base Classes (ABCs) as \"virtual "
"base classes\" to any class or type (including built-in types), including "
"other ABCs."
msgstr ""
"特別是，元類別 :class:`abc.ABCMeta` 實作了這些方法，以便能將抽象基底類別 "
"(ABC) 作為「虛擬基底類別」新增到任何類別或型別（包括內建型別）中，包括其他 "
"ABC。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3008
msgid ""
"Return true if *instance* should be considered a (direct or indirect) "
"instance of *class*. If defined, called to implement ``isinstance(instance, "
"class)``."
msgstr ""
"如果 *instance* 應被視為 *class* 的（直接或間接）實例，則回傳 true。如果有定"
"義，會被呼叫來實作 ``isinstance(instance, class)``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3015
msgid ""
"Return true if *subclass* should be considered a (direct or indirect) "
"subclass of *class*.  If defined, called to implement ``issubclass(subclass, "
"class)``."
msgstr ""
"如果 *subclass* 應被視為 *class* 的（直接或間接）子類別，則回傳 true。如果有"
"定義，會被呼叫來實作 ``issubclass(subclass, class)``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3020
msgid ""
"Note that these methods are looked up on the type (metaclass) of a class.  "
"They cannot be defined as class methods in the actual class.  This is "
"consistent with the lookup of special methods that are called on instances, "
"only in this case the instance is itself a class."
msgstr ""
"請注意，這些方法是在類別的型別（元類別）上查找的。它們不能在實際的類別中被定"
"義為類別方法。這與在實例上呼叫的特殊方法的查找方式一致，只是在這種情況下，實"
"例本身就是一個類別。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3027
msgid ":pep:`3119` - Introducing Abstract Base Classes"
msgstr ":pep:`3119` - 引入抽象基底類別"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3028
msgid ""
"Includes the specification for customizing :func:`isinstance` and :func:"
"`issubclass` behavior through :meth:`~type.__instancecheck__` and :meth:"
"`~type.__subclasscheck__`, with motivation for this functionality in the "
"context of adding Abstract Base Classes (see the :mod:`abc` module) to the "
"language."
msgstr ""
"包含透過 :meth:`~type.__instancecheck__` 和 :meth:`~type.__subclasscheck__` "
"自訂 :func:`isinstance` 和 :func:`issubclass` 行為的規格，以及在語言中新增抽"
"象基底類別（請參閱 :mod:`abc` 模組）的情境下，此功能的動機。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3036
msgid "Emulating generic types"
msgstr "模擬泛型型別"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3038
msgid ""
"When using :term:`type annotations<annotation>`, it is often useful to "
"*parameterize* a :term:`generic type` using Python's square-brackets "
"notation. For example, the annotation ``list[int]`` might be used to signify "
"a :class:`list` in which all the elements are of type :class:`int`."
msgstr ""
"在使用\\ :term:`型別註釋 <annotation>`\\ 時，使用 Python 的方括號標示法來\\ *"
"參數化*\\ 一個\\ :term:`泛型型別 <generic type>`\\ 通常很有用。例如，註釋 "
"``list[int]`` 可以用來表示一個所有元素皆為 :class:`int` 型別的 :class:"
"`list`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3045
msgid ":pep:`484` - Type Hints"
msgstr ":pep:`484` - 型別提示"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3046
msgid "Introducing Python's framework for type annotations"
msgstr "引入 Python 的型別註釋框架"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3048
msgid ":ref:`Generic Alias Types<types-genericalias>`"
msgstr ":ref:`泛型別名型別 <types-genericalias>`"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3049
msgid "Documentation for objects representing parameterized generic classes"
msgstr "表示參數化泛型類別之物件的文件"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3051
msgid ""
":ref:`Generics`, :ref:`user-defined generics<user-defined-generics>` and :"
"class:`typing.Generic`"
msgstr ""
":ref:`Generics`、:ref:`使用者定義泛型 <user-defined-generics>`\\ 和 :class:"
"`typing.Generic`"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3052
msgid ""
"Documentation on how to implement generic classes that can be parameterized "
"at runtime and understood by static type-checkers."
msgstr ""
"有關如何實作可以在 runtime 參數化並能被靜態型別檢查器理解的泛型類別的文件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3055
msgid ""
"A class can *generally* only be parameterized if it defines the special "
"class method ``__class_getitem__()``."
msgstr ""
"類別\\ *通常*\\ 只有在定義了特殊類別方法 ``__class_getitem__()`` 時才能被參數"
"化。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3060
msgid ""
"Return an object representing the specialization of a generic class by type "
"arguments found in *key*."
msgstr "回傳一個物件，表示泛型類別依據 *key* 中的型別引數所做的特化。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3063
msgid ""
"When defined on a class, ``__class_getitem__()`` is automatically a class "
"method. As such, there is no need for it to be decorated with :deco:"
"`classmethod` when it is defined."
msgstr ""
"當在類別上定義時，``__class_getitem__()`` 會自動成為類別方法。因此，定義它時"
"不需要以 :deco:`classmethod` 裝飾。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3069
msgid "The purpose of *__class_getitem__*"
msgstr "*__class_getitem__* 的目的"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3071
msgid ""
"The purpose of :meth:`~object.__class_getitem__` is to allow runtime "
"parameterization of standard-library generic classes in order to more easily "
"apply :term:`type hints<type hint>` to these classes."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~object.__class_getitem__` 的目的是允許標準函式庫的泛型類別在 runtime "
"進行參數化，以便更容易將\\ :term:`型別提示 <type hint>`\\ 應用於這些類別。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3075
msgid ""
"To implement custom generic classes that can be parameterized at runtime and "
"understood by static type-checkers, users should either inherit from a "
"standard library class that already implements :meth:`~object."
"__class_getitem__`, or inherit from :class:`typing.Generic`, which has its "
"own implementation of ``__class_getitem__()``."
msgstr ""
"若要實作可以在 runtime 參數化並能被靜態型別檢查器理解的自訂泛型類別，使用者應"
"該繼承自已經實作了 :meth:`~object.__class_getitem__` 的標準函式庫類別，或是繼"
"承自 :class:`typing.Generic`，它有自己的 ``__class_getitem__()`` 實作。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3081
msgid ""
"Custom implementations of :meth:`~object.__class_getitem__` on classes "
"defined outside of the standard library may not be understood by third-party "
"type-checkers such as mypy. Using ``__class_getitem__()`` on any class for "
"purposes other than type hinting is discouraged."
msgstr ""
"在標準函式庫以外定義的類別上自訂實作 :meth:`~object.__class_getitem__`，可能"
"無法被 mypy 等第三方型別檢查器理解。不建議在任何類別上將 "
"``__class_getitem__()`` 用於型別提示以外的目的。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3091
msgid "*__class_getitem__* versus *__getitem__*"
msgstr "*__class_getitem__* 與 *__getitem__*"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3093
msgid ""
"Usually, the :ref:`subscription<subscriptions>` of an object using square "
"brackets will call the :meth:`~object.__getitem__` instance method defined "
"on the object's class. However, if the object being subscribed is itself a "
"class, the class method :meth:`~object.__class_getitem__` may be called "
"instead. ``__class_getitem__()`` should return a :ref:`GenericAlias<types-"
"genericalias>` object if it is properly defined."
msgstr ""
"通常，使用方括號對物件進行\\ :ref:`下標 <subscriptions>`\\ 會呼叫定義在該物件"
"類別上的 :meth:`~object.__getitem__` 實例方法。然而，如果被下標的物件本身是一"
"個類別，則可能會改為呼叫類別方法 :meth:`~object.__class_getitem__`。如果 "
"``__class_getitem__()`` 定義正確，它應該回傳一個 :ref:`GenericAlias <types-"
"genericalias>` 物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3100
msgid ""
"Presented with the :term:`expression` ``obj[x]``, the Python interpreter "
"follows something like the following process to decide whether :meth:"
"`~object.__getitem__` or :meth:`~object.__class_getitem__` should be called::"
msgstr ""
"對於\\ :term:`運算式 <expression>` ``obj[x]``，Python 直譯器會遵循類似以下的"
"過程，來決定應該呼叫 :meth:`~object.__getitem__` 還是 :meth:`~object."
"__class_getitem__`： ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3105
msgid ""
"from inspect import isclass\n"
"\n"
"def subscribe(obj, x):\n"
"    \"\"\"Return the result of the expression 'obj[x]'\"\"\"\n"
"\n"
"    class_of_obj = type(obj)\n"
"\n"
"    # If the class of obj defines __getitem__,\n"
"    # call class_of_obj.__getitem__(obj, x)\n"
"    if hasattr(class_of_obj, '__getitem__'):\n"
"        return class_of_obj.__getitem__(obj, x)\n"
"\n"
"    # Else, if obj is a class and defines __class_getitem__,\n"
"    # call obj.__class_getitem__(x)\n"
"    elif isclass(obj) and hasattr(obj, '__class_getitem__'):\n"
"        return obj.__class_getitem__(x)\n"
"\n"
"    # Else, raise an exception\n"
"    else:\n"
"        raise TypeError(\n"
"            f\"'{class_of_obj.__name__}' object is not subscriptable\"\n"
"        )"
msgstr ""
"from inspect import isclass\n"
"\n"
"def subscribe(obj, x):\n"
"    \"\"\"Return the result of the expression 'obj[x]'\"\"\"\n"
"\n"
"    class_of_obj = type(obj)\n"
"\n"
"    # 如果 obj 的類別定義了 __getitem__，\n"
"    # 就呼叫 class_of_obj.__getitem__(obj, x)\n"
"    if hasattr(class_of_obj, '__getitem__'):\n"
"        return class_of_obj.__getitem__(obj, x)\n"
"\n"
"    # 否則，如果 obj 是一個類別並定義了 __class_getitem__，\n"
"    # 就呼叫 obj.__class_getitem__(x)\n"
"    elif isclass(obj) and hasattr(obj, '__class_getitem__'):\n"
"        return obj.__class_getitem__(x)\n"
"\n"
"    # 否則引發例外\n"
"    else:\n"
"        raise TypeError(\n"
"            f\"'{class_of_obj.__name__}' object is not subscriptable\"\n"
"        )"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3128
msgid ""
"In Python, all classes are themselves instances of other classes. The class "
"of a class is known as that class's :term:`metaclass`, and most classes have "
"the :class:`type` class as their metaclass. :class:`type` does not define :"
"meth:`~object.__getitem__`, meaning that expressions such as ``list[int]``, "
"``dict[str, float]`` and ``tuple[str, bytes]`` all result in :meth:`~object."
"__class_getitem__` being called::"
msgstr ""
"在 Python 中，所有類別本身都是其他類別的實例。一個類別的類別被稱為該類別的"
"\\ :term:`元類別 <metaclass>`，而大多數類別都以 :class:`type` 類別作為其元類"
"別。:class:`type` 沒有定義 :meth:`~object.__getitem__`，這意味著像 "
"``list[int]``、``dict[str, float]`` 和 ``tuple[str, bytes]`` 這樣的運算式都會"
"導致 :meth:`~object.__class_getitem__` 被呼叫： ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3135
msgid ""
">>> # list has class \"type\" as its metaclass, like most classes:\n"
">>> type(list)\n"
"<class 'type'>\n"
">>> type(dict) == type(list) == type(tuple) == type(str) == type(bytes)\n"
"True\n"
">>> # \"list[int]\" calls \"list.__class_getitem__(int)\"\n"
">>> list[int]\n"
"list[int]\n"
">>> # list.__class_getitem__ returns a GenericAlias object:\n"
">>> type(list[int])\n"
"<class 'types.GenericAlias'>"
msgstr ""
">>> # list 和大多數類別一樣，以類別 \"type\" 作為其元類別：\n"
">>> type(list)\n"
"<class 'type'>\n"
">>> type(dict) == type(list) == type(tuple) == type(str) == type(bytes)\n"
"True\n"
">>> # \"list[int]\" 會呼叫 \"list.__class_getitem__(int)\"\n"
">>> list[int]\n"
"list[int]\n"
">>> # list.__class_getitem__ 會回傳一個 GenericAlias 物件：\n"
">>> type(list[int])\n"
"<class 'types.GenericAlias'>"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3147
msgid ""
"However, if a class has a custom metaclass that defines :meth:`~object."
"__getitem__`, subscribing the class may result in different behaviour. An "
"example of this can be found in the :mod:`enum` module::"
msgstr ""
"然而，如果一個類別具有定義了 :meth:`~object.__getitem__` 的自訂元類別，對該類"
"別進行下標可能會產生不同的行為。在 :mod:`enum` 模組中可以找到這樣的例子： ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3151
msgid ""
">>> from enum import Enum\n"
">>> class Menu(Enum):\n"
"...     \"\"\"A breakfast menu\"\"\"\n"
"...     SPAM = 'spam'\n"
"...     BACON = 'bacon'\n"
"...\n"
">>> # Enum classes have a custom metaclass:\n"
">>> type(Menu)\n"
"<class 'enum.EnumMeta'>\n"
">>> # EnumMeta defines __getitem__,\n"
">>> # so __class_getitem__ is not called,\n"
">>> # and the result is not a GenericAlias object:\n"
">>> Menu['SPAM']\n"
"<Menu.SPAM: 'spam'>\n"
">>> type(Menu['SPAM'])\n"
"<enum 'Menu'>"
msgstr ""
">>> from enum import Enum\n"
">>> class Menu(Enum):\n"
"...     \"\"\"A breakfast menu\"\"\"\n"
"...     SPAM = 'spam'\n"
"...     BACON = 'bacon'\n"
"...\n"
">>> # Enum 類別具有自訂的元類別：\n"
">>> type(Menu)\n"
"<class 'enum.EnumMeta'>\n"
">>> # EnumMeta 定義了 __getitem__，\n"
">>> # 所以不會呼叫 __class_getitem__，\n"
">>> # 且結果不是 GenericAlias 物件：\n"
">>> Menu['SPAM']\n"
"<Menu.SPAM: 'spam'>\n"
">>> type(Menu['SPAM'])\n"
"<enum 'Menu'>"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3170
msgid ":pep:`560` - Core Support for typing module and generic types"
msgstr ":pep:`560` - typing 模組與泛型型別的核心支援"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3171
msgid ""
"Introducing :meth:`~object.__class_getitem__`, and outlining when a :ref:"
"`subscription<subscriptions>` results in ``__class_getitem__()`` being "
"called instead of :meth:`~object.__getitem__`"
msgstr ""
"引入 :meth:`~object.__class_getitem__`，並概述\\ :ref:`下標 "
"<subscriptions>`\\ 何時會導致呼叫 ``__class_getitem__()`` 而非 :meth:"
"`~object.__getitem__`"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3179
msgid "Emulating callable objects"
msgstr "模擬可呼叫物件"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3186
msgid ""
"Called when the instance is \"called\" as a function; if this method is "
"defined, ``x(arg1, arg2, ...)`` roughly translates to ``type(x).__call__(x, "
"arg1, ...)``. The :class:`object` class itself does not provide this method."
msgstr ""
"當實例被當作函式「呼叫」時會被呼叫；如果定義了此方法，``x(arg1, arg2, ...)`` "
"大致會轉換為 ``type(x).__call__(x, arg1, ...)``。:class:`object` 類別本身不提"
"供此方法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3194
msgid "Emulating container types"
msgstr "模擬容器型別"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3196
msgid ""
"The following methods can be defined to implement container objects. None of "
"them are provided by the :class:`object` class itself. Containers usually "
"are :term:`sequences <sequence>` (such as :class:`lists <list>` or :class:"
"`tuples <tuple>`) or :term:`mappings <mapping>` (like :term:`dictionaries "
"<dictionary>`), but can represent other containers as well.  The first set "
"of methods is used either to emulate a sequence or to emulate a mapping; the "
"difference is that for a sequence, the allowable keys should be the integers "
"*k* for which ``0 <= k < N`` where *N* is the length of the sequence, or :"
"class:`slice` objects, which define a range of items.  It is also "
"recommended that mappings provide the methods :meth:`!keys`, :meth:`!"
"values`, :meth:`!items`, :meth:`!get`, :meth:`!clear`, :meth:`!setdefault`, :"
"meth:`!pop`, :meth:`!popitem`, :meth:`!copy`, and :meth:`!update` behaving "
"similar to those for Python's standard :class:`dictionary <dict>` objects.  "
"The :mod:`collections.abc` module provides a :class:`~collections.abc."
"MutableMapping` :term:`abstract base class` to help create those methods "
"from a base set of :meth:`~object.__getitem__`, :meth:`~object."
"__setitem__`, :meth:`~object.__delitem__`, and :meth:`!keys`."
msgstr ""
"可以定義以下方法來實作容器物件。它們都不是由 :class:`object` 類別本身所提供"
"的。容器通常是\\ :term:`序列 <sequence>`\\ （例如\\ :class:`串列 <list>`\\ "
"或 :class:`tuple`）或\\ :term:`對映 <mapping>`\\ （例如\\ :term:`字典 "
"<dictionary>`），但也可以表示其他容器。第一組方法用於模擬序列或模擬對映；不同"
"之處在於，對於序列，允許的鍵應該是滿足 ``0 <= k < N`` 的整數 *k*\\ （其中 "
"*N* 是序列的長度），或是定義了項目範圍的 :class:`slice` 物件。也建議對映提"
"供 :meth:`!keys`、:meth:`!values`、:meth:`!items`、:meth:`!get`、:meth:`!"
"clear`、:meth:`!setdefault`、:meth:`!pop`、:meth:`!popitem`、:meth:`!copy` "
"和 :meth:`!update` 方法，其行為類似於 Python 標準\\ :class:`字典 <dict>`\\ 物"
"件的對應方法。:mod:`collections.abc` 模組提供了一個 :class:`~collections.abc."
"MutableMapping` :term:`抽象基底類別 <abstract base class>`，可以從 :meth:"
"`~object.__getitem__`、:meth:`~object.__setitem__`、:meth:`~object."
"__delitem__` 和 :meth:`!keys` 這組基本方法來建立那些方法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3215
msgid ""
"Mutable sequences should provide methods :meth:`~sequence.append`, :meth:"
"`~sequence.clear`, :meth:`~sequence.count`, :meth:`~sequence.extend`, :meth:"
"`~sequence.index`, :meth:`~sequence.insert`, :meth:`~sequence.pop`, :meth:"
"`~sequence.remove`, and :meth:`~sequence.reverse`, like Python standard :"
"class:`list` objects. Finally, sequence types should implement addition "
"(meaning concatenation) and multiplication (meaning repetition) by defining "
"the methods :meth:`~object.__add__`, :meth:`~object.__radd__`, :meth:"
"`~object.__iadd__`, :meth:`~object.__mul__`, :meth:`~object.__rmul__` and :"
"meth:`~object.__imul__` described below; they should not define other "
"numerical operators."
msgstr ""
"可變序列應該提供 :meth:`~sequence.append`、:meth:`~sequence.clear`、:meth:"
"`~sequence.count`、:meth:`~sequence.extend`、:meth:`~sequence.index`、:meth:"
"`~sequence.insert`、:meth:`~sequence.pop`、:meth:`~sequence.remove` 和 :meth:"
"`~sequence.reverse` 方法，就像 Python 標準的 :class:`list` 物件一樣。最後，序"
"列型別應該透過定義下面描述的 :meth:`~object.__add__`、:meth:`~object."
"__radd__`、:meth:`~object.__iadd__`、:meth:`~object.__mul__`、:meth:`~object."
"__rmul__` 和 :meth:`~object.__imul__` 方法來實作加法（意即串接）和乘法（意即"
"重複）；它們不應該定義其他數值運算子。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3227
msgid ""
"It is recommended that both mappings and sequences implement the :meth:"
"`~object.__contains__` method to allow efficient use of the ``in`` operator; "
"for mappings, ``in`` should search the mapping's keys; for sequences, it "
"should search through the values.  It is further recommended that both "
"mappings and sequences implement the :meth:`~object.__iter__` method to "
"allow efficient iteration through the container; for mappings, :meth:`!"
"__iter__` should iterate through the object's keys; for sequences, it should "
"iterate through the values."
msgstr ""
"建議對映和序列都實作 :meth:`~object.__contains__` 方法，以便有效率地使用 "
"``in`` 運算子；對於對映，``in`` 應該搜尋對映的鍵；對於序列，則應搜尋其中的"
"值。另外也建議對映和序列都實作 :meth:`~object.__iter__` 方法，以便有效率地疊"
"代整個容器；對於對映，:meth:`!__iter__` 應該疊代物件的鍵；對於序列，則應疊代"
"其中的值。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3242
msgid ""
"Called to implement the built-in function :func:`len`.  Should return the "
"length of the object, an integer ``>=`` 0.  Also, an object that doesn't "
"define a :meth:`~object.__bool__` method and whose :meth:`!__len__` method "
"returns zero is considered to be false in a Boolean context."
msgstr ""
"用來實作內建函式 :func:`len`。應回傳物件的長度，即一個 ``>=`` 0 的整數。此"
"外，沒有定義 :meth:`~object.__bool__` 方法且其 :meth:`!__len__` 方法回傳零的"
"物件，在預期布林值的情境中會被視為假。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3249
msgid ""
"In CPython, the length is required to be at most :data:`sys.maxsize`. If the "
"length is larger than :data:`!sys.maxsize` some features (such as :func:"
"`len`) may raise :exc:`OverflowError`.  To prevent raising :exc:`!"
"OverflowError` by truth value testing, an object must define a :meth:"
"`~object.__bool__` method."
msgstr ""
"在 CPython 中，長度最大只能是 :data:`sys.maxsize`。如果長度大於 :data:`!sys."
"maxsize`，某些功能（例如 :func:`len`）可能會引發 :exc:`OverflowError`。為了避"
"免在真值測試時引發 :exc:`!OverflowError`，物件必須定義 :meth:`~object."
"__bool__` 方法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3258
msgid ""
"Called to implement :func:`operator.length_hint`. Should return an estimated "
"length for the object (which may be greater or less than the actual length). "
"The length must be an integer ``>=`` 0. The return value may also be :data:"
"`NotImplemented`, which is treated the same as if the ``__length_hint__`` "
"method didn't exist at all. This method is purely an optimization and is "
"never required for correctness."
msgstr ""
"用來實作 :func:`operator.length_hint`。應回傳物件的估計長度（可能大於或小於實"
"際長度）。長度必須是一個 ``>=`` 0 的整數。回傳值也可以是 :data:"
"`NotImplemented`，這會被視為與 ``__length_hint__`` 方法完全不存在時相同。此方"
"法純粹是一種最佳化，對於正確性而言從來不是必要的。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3270
msgid ""
"Called to implement *subscription*, that is, ``self[subscript]``. See :ref:"
"`subscriptions` for details on the syntax."
msgstr ""
"用來實作\\ *下標*，也就是 ``self[subscript]``。語法的細節請見\\ :ref:"
"`subscriptions`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3273
msgid ""
"There are two types of built-in objects that support subscription via :meth:"
"`!__getitem__`:"
msgstr "有兩種內建物件透過 :meth:`!__getitem__` 支援下標："

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3276
msgid ""
"**sequences**, where *subscript* (also called :term:`index`) should be an "
"integer or a :class:`slice` object. See the :ref:`sequence documentation "
"<datamodel-sequences>` for the expected behavior, including handling :class:"
"`slice` objects and negative indices."
msgstr ""
"**序列**，其中 *subscript*\\ （也稱為\\ :term:`索引 <index>`）應為整數或 :"
"class:`slice` 物件。預期的行為（包括如何處理 :class:`slice` 物件與負索引）請"
"見\\ :ref:`序列的說明文件 <datamodel-sequences>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3280
msgid ""
"**mappings**, where *subscript* is also called the :term:`key`. See :ref:"
"`mapping documentation <datamodel-mappings>` for the expected behavior."
msgstr ""
"**對映**，其中 *subscript* 也稱為\\ :term:`鍵 <key>`。預期的行為請見\\ :ref:`"
"對映的說明文件 <datamodel-mappings>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3284
msgid ""
"If *subscript* is of an inappropriate type, :meth:`!__getitem__` should "
"raise :exc:`TypeError`. If *subscript* has an inappropriate value, :meth:`!"
"__getitem__` should raise an :exc:`LookupError` or one of its subclasses (:"
"exc:`IndexError` for sequences; :exc:`KeyError` for mappings)."
msgstr ""
"如果 *subscript* 的型別不適當，:meth:`!__getitem__` 應引發 :exc:`TypeError`。"
"如果 *subscript* 的值不適當，:meth:`!__getitem__` 應引發 :exc:`LookupError` "
"或其子類別之一（序列為 :exc:`IndexError`；對映為 :exc:`KeyError`）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3294
msgid ""
"Slicing is handled by :meth:`!__getitem__`, :meth:`~object.__setitem__`, "
"and :meth:`~object.__delitem__`. A call like ::"
msgstr ""
"切片由 :meth:`!__getitem__`、:meth:`~object.__setitem__` 和 :meth:`~object."
"__delitem__` 處理。像這樣的呼叫 ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3298
msgid "a[1:2] = b"
msgstr "a[1:2] = b"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3300
msgid "is translated to ::"
msgstr "會被轉換為 ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3302
msgid "a[slice(1, 2, None)] = b"
msgstr "a[slice(1, 2, None)] = b"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3304
msgid "and so forth. Missing slice items are always filled in with ``None``."
msgstr "依此類推。缺少的切片項目一律以 ``None`` 填入。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3308
msgid ""
"The sequence iteration protocol (used, for example, in :keyword:`for` "
"loops), expects that an :exc:`IndexError` will be raised for illegal indexes "
"to allow proper detection of the end of a sequence."
msgstr ""
"序列疊代協定（例如在 :keyword:`for` 迴圈中使用）預期不合法的索引會引發 :exc:"
"`IndexError`，以便正確偵測序列的結尾。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3314
msgid ""
"When :ref:`subscripting <subscriptions>` a *class*, the special class "
"method :meth:`~object.__class_getitem__` may be called instead of :meth:`!"
"__getitem__`. See :ref:`classgetitem-versus-getitem` for more details."
msgstr ""
"對一個\\ *類別*\\ 進行\\ :ref:`下標 <subscriptions>`\\ 時，可能會呼叫特殊類別"
"方法 :meth:`~object.__class_getitem__` 而非 :meth:`!__getitem__`。更多細節請"
"見 :ref:`classgetitem-versus-getitem`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3322
msgid ""
"Called to implement assignment to ``self[key]``.  Same note as for :meth:"
"`__getitem__`.  This should only be implemented for mappings if the objects "
"support changes to the values for keys, or if new keys can be added, or for "
"sequences if elements can be replaced.  The same exceptions should be raised "
"for improper *key* values as for the :meth:`__getitem__` method."
msgstr ""
"用來實作對 ``self[key]`` 的賦值。注意事項與 :meth:`__getitem__` 相同。對於對"
"映，只有在物件支援更改鍵所對應的值、或可以新增鍵時，才應實作此方法；對於序"
"列，則只有在元素可以被替換時才應實作。對於不適當的 *key* 值，應引發與 :meth:"
"`__getitem__` 方法相同的例外。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3331
msgid ""
"Called to implement deletion of ``self[key]``.  Same note as for :meth:"
"`__getitem__`.  This should only be implemented for mappings if the objects "
"support removal of keys, or for sequences if elements can be removed from "
"the sequence.  The same exceptions should be raised for improper *key* "
"values as for the :meth:`__getitem__` method."
msgstr ""
"用來實作 ``self[key]`` 的刪除。注意事項與 :meth:`__getitem__` 相同。對於對"
"映，只有在物件支援移除鍵時才應實作此方法；對於序列，則只有在元素可以從序列中"
"移除時才應實作。對於不適當的 *key* 值，應引發與 :meth:`__getitem__` 方法相同"
"的例外。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3340
msgid ""
"Called by :class:`dict`\\ .\\ :meth:`__getitem__` to implement ``self[key]`` "
"for dict subclasses when key is not in the dictionary."
msgstr ""
"當鍵不在字典中時，由 :class:`dict`\\ .\\ :meth:`__getitem__` 呼叫，用來為 "
"dict 子類別實作 ``self[key]``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3346
msgid ""
"This method is called when an :term:`iterator` is required for a container. "
"This method should return a new iterator object that can iterate over all "
"the objects in the container.  For mappings, it should iterate over the keys "
"of the container."
msgstr ""
"當容器需要一個\\ :term:`疊代器 <iterator>`\\ 時會呼叫此方法。此方法應回傳一個"
"新的疊代器物件，能夠疊代容器中的所有物件。對於對映，它應該疊代容器的鍵。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3354
msgid ""
"Called (if present) by the :func:`reversed` built-in to implement reverse "
"iteration.  It should return a new iterator object that iterates over all "
"the objects in the container in reverse order."
msgstr ""
"由內建函式 :func:`reversed` 呼叫（如果有定義的話）以實作反向疊代。它應回傳一"
"個新的疊代器物件，以相反的順序疊代容器中的所有物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3358
msgid ""
"If the :meth:`__reversed__` method is not provided, the :func:`reversed` "
"built-in will fall back to using the sequence protocol (:meth:`__len__` and :"
"meth:`__getitem__`).  Objects that support the sequence protocol should only "
"provide :meth:`__reversed__` if they can provide an implementation that is "
"more efficient than the one provided by :func:`reversed`."
msgstr ""
"如果沒有提供 :meth:`__reversed__` 方法，內建函式 :func:`reversed` 會退回使用"
"序列協定（:meth:`__len__` 和 :meth:`__getitem__`）。支援序列協定的物件，只有"
"在能提供比 :func:`reversed` 所提供的更有效率的實作時，才應提供 :meth:"
"`__reversed__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3365
msgid ""
"The membership test operators (:keyword:`in` and :keyword:`not in`) are "
"normally implemented as an iteration through a container. However, container "
"objects can supply the following special method with a more efficient "
"implementation, which also does not require the object be iterable."
msgstr ""
"成員測試運算子（:keyword:`in` 和 :keyword:`not in`）通常以疊代整個容器的方式"
"實作。然而，容器物件可以用更有效率的實作來提供以下特殊方法，而且這種實作也不"
"要求物件必須是可疊代的。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3372
msgid ""
"Called to implement membership test operators.  Should return true if *item* "
"is in *self*, false otherwise.  For mapping objects, this should consider "
"the keys of the mapping rather than the values or the key-item pairs."
msgstr ""
"用來實作成員測試運算子。若 *item* 在 *self* 中應回傳 true，否則回傳 false。對"
"於對映物件，應該考慮的是對映的鍵，而不是值或鍵值對。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3376
msgid ""
"For objects that don't define :meth:`__contains__`, the membership test "
"first tries iteration via :meth:`__iter__`, then the old sequence iteration "
"protocol via :meth:`__getitem__`, see :ref:`this section in the language "
"reference <membership-test-details>`."
msgstr ""
"對於沒有定義 :meth:`__contains__` 的物件，成員測試會先嘗試透過 :meth:"
"`__iter__` 進行疊代，接著再嘗試透過 :meth:`__getitem__` 使用舊式的序列疊代協"
"定，請見\\ :ref:`語言參考手冊中的這一節 <membership-test-details>`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3385
msgid "Emulating numeric types"
msgstr "模擬數值型別"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3387
msgid ""
"The following methods can be defined to emulate numeric objects. Methods "
"corresponding to operations that are not supported by the particular kind of "
"number implemented (e.g., bitwise operations for non-integral numbers) "
"should be left undefined."
msgstr ""
"可以定義以下方法來模擬數值物件。對於所實作的特定種類數字不支援的運算（例如對"
"非整數的數字進行位元運算），其對應的方法應保持未定義。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3413
msgid ""
"These methods are called to implement the binary arithmetic operations "
"(``+``, ``-``, ``*``, ``@``, ``/``, ``//``, ``%``, :func:`divmod`, :func:"
"`pow`, ``**``, ``<<``, ``>>``, ``&``, ``^``, ``|``).  For instance, to "
"evaluate the expression ``x + y``, where *x* is an instance of a class that "
"has an :meth:`__add__` method, ``type(x).__add__(x, y)`` is called.  The :"
"meth:`__divmod__` method should be the equivalent to using :meth:"
"`__floordiv__` and :meth:`__mod__`; it should not be related to :meth:"
"`__truediv__`.  Note that :meth:`__pow__` should be defined to accept an "
"optional third argument if the three-argument version of the built-in :func:"
"`pow` function is to be supported."
msgstr ""
"這些方法用來實作二元算術運算（``+``、``-``、``*``、``@``、``/``、``//``、"
"``%``、:func:`divmod`、:func:`pow`、``**``、``<<``、``>>``、``&``、``^``、``|"
"``）。舉例來說，要對運算式 ``x + y`` 求值，其中 *x* 是一個具有 :meth:"
"`__add__` 方法之類別的實例，會呼叫 ``type(x).__add__(x, y)``。:meth:"
"`__divmod__` 方法應等同於使用 :meth:`__floordiv__` 和 :meth:`__mod__`；它不應"
"與 :meth:`__truediv__` 有關。請注意，如果要支援內建函式 :func:`pow` 的三引數"
"版本，:meth:`__pow__` 應被定義為可接受第三個可選引數。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3424
msgid ""
"If one of those methods does not support the operation with the supplied "
"arguments, it should return :data:`NotImplemented`."
msgstr ""
"如果這些方法之一不支援以所提供的引數進行該運算，它應回傳 :data:"
"`NotImplemented`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3447
msgid ""
"These methods are called to implement the binary arithmetic operations "
"(``+``, ``-``, ``*``, ``@``, ``/``, ``//``, ``%``, :func:`divmod`, :func:"
"`pow`, ``**``, ``<<``, ``>>``, ``&``, ``^``, ``|``) with reflected (swapped) "
"operands.  These functions are only called if the operands are of different "
"types, when the left operand does not support the corresponding operation "
"[#]_, or the right operand's class is derived from the left operand's class. "
"[#]_ For instance, to evaluate the expression ``x - y``, where *y* is an "
"instance of a class that has an :meth:`__rsub__` method, ``type(y)."
"__rsub__(y, x)`` is called if ``type(x).__sub__(x, y)`` returns :data:"
"`NotImplemented` or ``type(y)`` is a subclass of ``type(x)``. [#]_"
msgstr ""
"這些方法用來以反轉（交換）的運算元實作二元算術運算（``+``、``-``、``*``、"
"``@``、``/``、``//``、``%``、:func:`divmod`、:func:`pow`、``**``、``<<``、"
"``>>``、``&``、``^``、``|``）。只有在運算元型別不同，且左運算元不支援對應的運"
"算\\ [#]_\\ 或右運算元的類別衍生自左運算元的類別時，才會呼叫這些函式。\\ "
"[#]_\\ 舉例來說，要對運算式 ``x - y`` 求值，其中 *y* 是一個具有 :meth:"
"`__rsub__` 方法之類別的實例，若 ``type(x).__sub__(x, y)`` 回傳 :data:"
"`NotImplemented` 或 ``type(y)`` 是 ``type(x)`` 的子類別，就會呼叫 ``type(y)."
"__rsub__(y, x)``。\\ [#]_"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3458
msgid ""
"Note that :meth:`__rpow__` should be defined to accept an optional third "
"argument if the three-argument version of the built-in :func:`pow` function "
"is to be supported."
msgstr ""
"請注意，如果要支援內建函式 :func:`pow` 的三引數版本，:meth:`__rpow__` 應被定"
"義為可接受第三個可選引數。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3464
msgid ""
"Three-argument :func:`pow` now try calling :meth:`~object.__rpow__` if "
"necessary. Previously it was only called in two-argument :func:`!pow` and "
"the binary power operator."
msgstr ""
"三引數的 :func:`pow` 現在會在必要時嘗試呼叫 :meth:`~object.__rpow__`。先前它"
"只會在雙引數的 :func:`!pow` 和二元次方運算子中被呼叫。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3470
msgid ""
"If the right operand's type is a subclass of the left operand's type and "
"that subclass provides a different implementation of the reflected method "
"for the operation, this method will be called before the left operand's non-"
"reflected method. This behavior allows subclasses to override their "
"ancestors' operations."
msgstr ""
"如果右運算元的型別是左運算元型別的子類別，且該子類別為該運算提供了不同的反轉"
"方法實作，則會在左運算元的非反轉方法之前呼叫此方法。此行為讓子類別可以覆寫其"
"祖先的運算。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3490
msgid ""
"These methods are called to implement the augmented arithmetic assignments "
"(``+=``, ``-=``, ``*=``, ``@=``, ``/=``, ``//=``, ``%=``, ``**=``, ``<<=``, "
"``>>=``, ``&=``, ``^=``, ``|=``).  These methods should attempt to do the "
"operation in-place (modifying *self*) and return the result (which could be, "
"but does not have to be, *self*).  If a specific method is not defined, or "
"if that method returns :data:`NotImplemented`, the augmented assignment "
"falls back to the normal methods.  For instance, if *x* is an instance of a "
"class with an :meth:`__iadd__` method, ``x += y`` is equivalent to ``x = x."
"__iadd__(y)`` . If :meth:`__iadd__` does not exist, or if ``x.__iadd__(y)`` "
"returns :data:`!NotImplemented`, ``x.__add__(y)`` and ``y.__radd__(x)`` are "
"considered, as with the evaluation of ``x + y``. In certain situations, "
"augmented assignment can result in unexpected errors (see :ref:`faq-"
"augmented-assignment-tuple-error`), but this behavior is in fact part of the "
"data model."
msgstr ""
"這些方法用來實作擴增算術賦值（``+=``、``-=``、``*=``、``@=``、``/=``、``//"
"=``、``%=``、``**=``、``<<=``、``>>=``、``&=``、``^=``、``|=``）。這些方法應"
"嘗試原地 (in-place) 進行運算（修改 *self*）並回傳結果（結果可以是 *self*，但"
"不一定要是）。如果沒有定義特定的方法，或該方法回傳 :data:`NotImplemented`，擴"
"增賦值會退回使用一般的方法。舉例來說，如果 *x* 是一個具有 :meth:`__iadd__` 方"
"法之類別的實例，``x += y`` 等同於 ``x = x.__iadd__(y)``。如果 :meth:"
"`__iadd__` 不存在，或 ``x.__iadd__(y)`` 回傳 :data:`!NotImplemented`，則會如"
"同對 ``x + y`` 求值時一樣考慮 ``x.__add__(y)`` 和 ``y.__radd__(x)``。在某些情"
"況下，擴增賦值可能會導致意料之外的錯誤（請見\\ :ref:`faq-augmented-"
"assignment-tuple-error`），但此行為實際上是資料模型的一部分。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3513
msgid ""
"Called to implement the unary arithmetic operations (``-``, ``+``, :func:"
"`abs` and ``~``)."
msgstr "用來實作一元算術運算（``-``、``+``、:func:`abs` 和 ``~``）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3526
msgid ""
"Called to implement the built-in functions :func:`complex`, :func:`int` and :"
"func:`float`.  Should return a value of the appropriate type."
msgstr ""
"用來實作內建函式 :func:`complex`、:func:`int` 和 :func:`float`。應回傳適當型"
"別的值。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3533
msgid ""
"Called to implement :func:`operator.index`, and whenever Python needs to "
"losslessly convert the numeric object to an integer object (such as in "
"slicing, or in the built-in :func:`bin`, :func:`hex` and :func:`oct` "
"functions). Presence of this method indicates that the numeric object is an "
"integer type.  Must return an integer."
msgstr ""
"用來實作 :func:`operator.index`；每當 Python 需要將數值物件無損地轉換為整數物"
"件時（例如在切片中，或在內建函式 :func:`bin`、:func:`hex` 和 :func:`oct` "
"中），也會呼叫此方法。此方法的存在表示該數值物件是整數型別。必須回傳整數。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3539
msgid ""
"If :meth:`__int__`, :meth:`__float__` and :meth:`__complex__` are not "
"defined then corresponding built-in functions :func:`int`, :func:`float` "
"and :func:`complex` fall back to :meth:`__index__`."
msgstr ""
"如果沒有定義 :meth:`__int__`、:meth:`__float__` 和 :meth:`__complex__`，則對"
"應的內建函式 :func:`int`、:func:`float` 和 :func:`complex` 會退回使用 :meth:"
"`__index__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3551
msgid ""
"Called to implement the built-in function :func:`round` and :mod:`math` "
"functions :func:`~math.trunc`, :func:`~math.floor` and :func:`~math.ceil`. "
"Unless *ndigits* is passed to :meth:`!__round__` all these methods should "
"return the value of the object truncated to an :class:`~numbers.Integral` "
"(typically an :class:`int`)."
msgstr ""
"用來實作內建函式 :func:`round` 以及 :mod:`math` 的函式 :func:`~math.trunc`、:"
"func:`~math.floor` 和 :func:`~math.ceil`。除非有傳遞 *ndigits* 給 :meth:`!"
"__round__`，否則這些方法都應回傳將物件值截斷為 :class:`~numbers.Integral`\\ "
"（通常是 :class:`int`）後的結果。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3557
msgid ""
":func:`int` no longer delegates to the :meth:`~object.__trunc__` method."
msgstr ":func:`int` 不再委派給 :meth:`~object.__trunc__` 方法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3564
msgid "With Statement Context Managers"
msgstr "With 陳述式的情境管理器"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3566
msgid ""
"A :dfn:`context manager` is an object that defines the runtime context to be "
"established when executing a :keyword:`with` statement. The context manager "
"handles the entry into, and the exit from, the desired runtime context for "
"the execution of the block of code.  Context managers are normally invoked "
"using the :keyword:`!with` statement (described in section :ref:`with`), but "
"can also be used by directly invoking their methods."
msgstr ""
":dfn:`情境管理器 (context manager)` 是一個物件，定義了執行 :keyword:`with` 陳"
"述式時所要建立的 runtime 情境。情境管理器負責處理進入與離開所需 runtime 情境"
"的過程，以執行該程式碼區塊。情境管理器通常透過 :keyword:`!with` 陳述式呼叫"
"（說明於 :ref:`with`\\ 章節），但也可以透過直接呼叫其方法來使用。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3577
msgid ""
"Typical uses of context managers include saving and restoring various kinds "
"of global state, locking and unlocking resources, closing opened files, etc."
msgstr ""
"情境管理器的典型用途包括儲存和還原各種全域狀態、鎖定和解鎖資源、關閉已開啟的"
"檔案等。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3580
msgid ""
"For more information on context managers, see :ref:`typecontextmanager`. "
"The :class:`object` class itself does not provide the context manager "
"methods."
msgstr ""
"關於情境管理器的更多資訊，請見\\ :ref:`typecontextmanager`。:class:`object` "
"類別本身並不提供情境管理器的方法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3586
msgid ""
"Enter the runtime context related to this object. The :keyword:`with` "
"statement will bind this method's return value to the target(s) specified in "
"the :keyword:`!as` clause of the statement, if any."
msgstr ""
"進入與此物件相關的 runtime 情境。:keyword:`with` 陳述式會將此方法的回傳值繫結"
"到該陳述式 :keyword:`!as` 子句中所指定的目標（如果有的話）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3593
msgid ""
"Exit the runtime context related to this object. The parameters describe the "
"exception that caused the context to be exited. If the context was exited "
"without an exception, all three arguments will be :const:`None`."
msgstr ""
"離開與此物件相關的 runtime 情境。參數描述了導致離開情境的例外。如果離開情境時"
"沒有發生例外，三個引數都會是 :const:`None`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3597
msgid ""
"If an exception is supplied, and the method wishes to suppress the exception "
"(i.e., prevent it from being propagated), it should return a true value. "
"Otherwise, the exception will be processed normally upon exit from this "
"method."
msgstr ""
"如果有提供例外，且此方法希望抑制該例外（即防止它被傳播），它應該回傳 true "
"值。否則，該例外會在離開此方法時正常處理。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3601
msgid ""
"Note that :meth:`~object.__exit__` methods should not reraise the passed-in "
"exception; this is the caller's responsibility."
msgstr ""
"請注意，:meth:`~object.__exit__` 方法不應重新引發傳入的例外；這是呼叫者的責"
"任。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3607
msgid ":pep:`343` - The \"with\" statement"
msgstr ":pep:`343` - \"with\" 陳述式"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3608
msgid ""
"The specification, background, and examples for the Python :keyword:`with` "
"statement."
msgstr "Python :keyword:`with` 陳述式的規格、背景和範例。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3615
msgid "Customizing positional arguments in class pattern matching"
msgstr "在類別模式匹配中自訂位置引數"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3617
msgid ""
"When using a class name in a pattern, positional arguments in the pattern "
"are not allowed by default, i.e. ``case MyClass(x, y)`` is typically invalid "
"without special support in ``MyClass``. To be able to use that kind of "
"pattern, the class needs to define a *__match_args__* attribute."
msgstr ""
"在模式中使用類別名稱時，預設不允許在模式中使用位置引數，也就是說，若 "
"``MyClass`` 沒有特別支援，``case MyClass(x, y)`` 通常是無效的。要能夠使用這種"
"模式，類別需要定義一個 *__match_args__* 屬性。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3624
msgid ""
"This class variable can be assigned a tuple of strings. When this class is "
"used in a class pattern with positional arguments, each positional argument "
"will be converted into a keyword argument, using the corresponding value in "
"*__match_args__* as the keyword. The absence of this attribute is equivalent "
"to setting it to ``()``."
msgstr ""
"這個類別變數可以被賦值為一個由字串組成的 tuple。當此類別被用於帶有位置引數的"
"類別模式時，每個位置引數都會被轉換為關鍵字引數，並使用 *__match_args__* 中對"
"應的值作為關鍵字。沒有此屬性等同於將其設為 ``()``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3630
msgid ""
"For example, if ``MyClass.__match_args__`` is ``(\"left\", \"center\", "
"\"right\")`` that means that ``case MyClass(x, y)`` is equivalent to ``case "
"MyClass(left=x, center=y)``. Note that the number of arguments in the "
"pattern must be smaller than or equal to the number of elements in "
"*__match_args__*; if it is larger, the pattern match attempt will raise a :"
"exc:`TypeError`."
msgstr ""
"舉例來說，如果 ``MyClass.__match_args__`` 是 ``(\"left\", \"center\", "
"\"right\")``，表示 ``case MyClass(x, y)`` 等同於 ``case MyClass(left=x, "
"center=y)``。請注意，模式中的引數數量必須小於或等於 *__match_args__* 中的元素"
"數量；如果超過，模式匹配的嘗試會引發 :exc:`TypeError`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3640
msgid ":pep:`634` - Structural Pattern Matching"
msgstr ":pep:`634` - 結構模式匹配"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3641
msgid "The specification for the Python ``match`` statement."
msgstr "Python ``match`` 陳述式的規格。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3647
msgid "Emulating buffer types"
msgstr "模擬緩衝區型別"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3649
msgid ""
"The :ref:`buffer protocol <bufferobjects>` provides a way for Python objects "
"to expose efficient access to a low-level memory array. This protocol is "
"implemented by builtin types such as :class:`bytes` and :class:`memoryview`, "
"and third-party libraries may define additional buffer types."
msgstr ""
":ref:`緩衝區協定 <bufferobjects>`\\ 提供了一種方式，讓 Python 物件能對外提供"
"對低階記憶體陣列的高效存取。此協定由 :class:`bytes` 和 :class:`memoryview` 等"
"內建型別實作，第三方函式庫也可以定義額外的緩衝區型別。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3654
msgid ""
"While buffer types are usually implemented in C, it is also possible to "
"implement the protocol in Python."
msgstr "雖然緩衝區型別通常以 C 實作，但也可以用 Python 實作此協定。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3659
msgid ""
"Called when a buffer is requested from *self* (for example, by the :class:"
"`memoryview` constructor). The *flags* argument is an integer representing "
"the kind of buffer requested, affecting for example whether the returned "
"buffer is read-only or writable. :class:`inspect.BufferFlags` provides a "
"convenient way to interpret the flags. The method must return a :class:"
"`memoryview` object."
msgstr ""
"當從 *self* 請求緩衝區時呼叫（例如由 :class:`memoryview` 建構函式請求）。"
"*flags* 引數是一個整數，代表所請求的緩衝區種類，例如會影響回傳的緩衝區是唯讀"
"還是可寫入。:class:`inspect.BufferFlags` 提供了一種解讀這些旗標的便利方式。此"
"方法必須回傳一個 :class:`memoryview` 物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3666
msgid ""
"**Thread safety:** In :term:`free-threaded <free threading>` Python, "
"implementations must manage any internal export counter using atomic "
"operations. The method must be safe to call concurrently from multiple "
"threads, and the returned buffer's underlying data must remain valid until "
"the corresponding :meth:`~object.__release_buffer__` call completes. See :"
"ref:`thread-safety-memoryview` for details."
msgstr ""
"**執行緒安全：**\\ 在\\ :term:`自由執行緒 (free-threaded) <free threading>` "
"Python 中，實作必須使用原子操作來管理任何內部的匯出計數器。此方法必須能安全地"
"從多個執行緒並行呼叫，且回傳之緩衝區的底層資料必須保持有效，直到對應的 :meth:"
"`~object.__release_buffer__` 呼叫完成為止。詳情請見 :ref:`thread-safety-"
"memoryview`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3675
msgid ""
"Called when a buffer is no longer needed. The *buffer* argument is a :class:"
"`memoryview` object that was previously returned by :meth:`~object."
"__buffer__`. The method must release any resources associated with the "
"buffer. This method should return ``None``."
msgstr ""
"當不再需要緩衝區時呼叫。*buffer* 引數是先前由 :meth:`~object.__buffer__` 回傳"
"的 :class:`memoryview` 物件。此方法必須釋放與該緩衝區相關的所有資源。此方法應"
"回傳 ``None``。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3680
msgid ""
"**Thread safety:** In :term:`free-threaded <free threading>` Python, any "
"export counter decrement must use atomic operations. Resource cleanup must "
"be thread-safe, as the final release may race with concurrent releases from "
"other threads."
msgstr ""
"**執行緒安全：**\\ 在\\ :term:`自由執行緒 <free threading>` Python 中，任何匯"
"出計數器的遞減都必須使用原子操作。資源清理必須是執行緒安全的，因為最後一次釋"
"放可能會與其他執行緒的並行釋放發生競爭。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3685
msgid ""
"Buffer objects that do not need to perform any cleanup are not required to "
"implement this method."
msgstr "不需要執行任何清理的緩衝區物件，不需要實作此方法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3692
msgid ":pep:`688` - Making the buffer protocol accessible in Python"
msgstr ":pep:`688` - 使緩衝區協定可在 Python 中存取"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3693
msgid ""
"Introduces the Python ``__buffer__`` and ``__release_buffer__`` methods."
msgstr "引入 Python 的 ``__buffer__`` 和 ``__release_buffer__`` 方法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3695
msgid ":class:`collections.abc.Buffer`"
msgstr ":class:`collections.abc.Buffer`"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3696
msgid "ABC for buffer types."
msgstr "緩衝區型別的抽象基底類別。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3699
msgid "Annotations"
msgstr "註釋"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3701
msgid ""
"Functions, classes, and modules may contain :term:`annotations "
"<annotation>`, which are a way to associate information (usually :term:`type "
"hints <type hint>`) with a symbol."
msgstr ""
"函式、類別和模組可以包含\\ :term:`註釋 <annotation>`，這是一種將資訊（通常是"
"\\ :term:`型別提示 <type hint>`）與符號關聯起來的方式。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3707
msgid ""
"This attribute contains the annotations for an object. It is :ref:`lazily "
"evaluated <lazy-evaluation>`, so accessing the attribute may execute "
"arbitrary code and raise exceptions. If evaluation is successful, the "
"attribute is set to a dictionary mapping from variable names to annotations."
msgstr ""
"此屬性包含物件的註釋。它是\\ :ref:`惰性求值 <lazy-evaluation>`\\ 的，因此存取"
"此屬性可能會執行任意程式碼並引發例外。如果求值成功，此屬性會被設為一個將變數"
"名稱對映到註釋的字典。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3712
msgid "Annotations are now lazily evaluated."
msgstr "註釋現在是惰性求值的。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3717
msgid ""
"An :term:`annotate function`. Returns a new dictionary object mapping "
"attribute/parameter names to their annotation values."
msgstr ""
"一個\\ :term:`註釋函式 <annotate function>`。回傳一個新的字典物件，將屬性/參"
"數名稱對映到其註釋值。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3720
msgid ""
"Takes a format parameter specifying the format in which annotations values "
"should be provided. It must be a member of the :class:`annotationlib.Format` "
"enum, or an integer with a value corresponding to a member of the enum."
msgstr ""
"接受一個格式參數，用來指定註釋值應以何種格式提供。它必須是 :class:"
"`annotationlib.Format` 列舉的成員，或是一個值對應於該列舉成員的整數。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3724
msgid ""
"If an annotate function doesn't support the requested format, it must raise :"
"exc:`NotImplementedError`. Annotate functions must always support :attr:"
"`~annotationlib.Format.VALUE` format; they must not raise :exc:"
"`NotImplementedError()` when called with this format."
msgstr ""
"如果註釋函式不支援所請求的格式，它必須引發 :exc:`NotImplementedError`。註釋函"
"式必須始終支援 :attr:`~annotationlib.Format.VALUE` 格式；以此格式呼叫時，它們"
"不得引發 :exc:`NotImplementedError()`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3729
msgid ""
"When called with  :attr:`~annotationlib.Format.VALUE` format, an annotate "
"function may raise :exc:`NameError`; it must not raise :exc:`!NameError` "
"when called requesting any other format."
msgstr ""
"以 :attr:`~annotationlib.Format.VALUE` 格式呼叫時，註釋函式可以引發 :exc:"
"`NameError`；以其他任何格式呼叫時，則不得引發 :exc:`!NameError`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3732
msgid ""
"If an object does not have any annotations, :attr:`~object.__annotate__` "
"should preferably be set to ``None`` (it can’t be deleted), rather than set "
"to a function that returns an empty dict."
msgstr ""
"如果物件沒有任何註釋，:attr:`~object.__annotate__` 最好設為 ``None``\\ （它無"
"法被刪除），而不是設為一個回傳空字典的函式。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3739
msgid ":pep:`649` --- Deferred evaluation of annotation using descriptors"
msgstr ":pep:`649` --- 使用描述器延遲註釋的求值"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3740
msgid ""
"Introduces lazy evaluation of annotations and the ``__annotate__`` function."
msgstr "引入註釋的惰性求值以及 ``__annotate__`` 函式。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3746
msgid "Special method lookup"
msgstr "特殊方法查找"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3748
msgid ""
"For custom classes, implicit invocations of special methods are only "
"guaranteed to work correctly if defined on an object's type, not in the "
"object's instance dictionary.  That behaviour is the reason why the "
"following code raises an exception::"
msgstr ""
"對於自訂類別，特殊方法的隱式呼叫只有在定義於物件的型別上（而非物件的實例字典"
"中）時，才保證能正確運作。這個行為就是以下程式碼會引發例外的原因： ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3753
msgid ""
">>> class C:\n"
"...     pass\n"
"...\n"
">>> c = C()\n"
">>> c.__len__ = lambda: 5\n"
">>> len(c)\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\n"
"TypeError: object of type 'C' has no len()"
msgstr ""
">>> class C:\n"
"...     pass\n"
"...\n"
">>> c = C()\n"
">>> c.__len__ = lambda: 5\n"
">>> len(c)\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\n"
"TypeError: object of type 'C' has no len()"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3763
msgid ""
"The rationale behind this behaviour lies with a number of special methods "
"such as :meth:`~object.__hash__` and :meth:`~object.__repr__` that are "
"implemented by all objects, including type objects. If the implicit lookup "
"of these methods used the conventional lookup process, they would fail when "
"invoked on the type object itself::"
msgstr ""
"這個行為背後的理由在於有些特殊方法（例如 :meth:`~object.__hash__` 和 :meth:"
"`~object.__repr__`）是由所有物件實作的，包括型別物件。如果這些方法的隱式查找"
"使用傳統的查找過程，那麼在型別物件本身上呼叫它們時就會失敗： ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3770
msgid ""
">>> 1 .__hash__() == hash(1)\n"
"True\n"
">>> int.__hash__() == hash(int)\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\n"
"TypeError: descriptor '__hash__' of 'int' object needs an argument"
msgstr ""
">>> 1 .__hash__() == hash(1)\n"
"True\n"
">>> int.__hash__() == hash(int)\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\n"
"TypeError: descriptor '__hash__' of 'int' object needs an argument"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3777
msgid ""
"Incorrectly attempting to invoke an unbound method of a class in this way is "
"sometimes referred to as 'metaclass confusion', and is avoided by bypassing "
"the instance when looking up special methods::"
msgstr ""
"以這種方式錯誤地嘗試呼叫類別的未繫結方法，有時被稱為「元類別混淆 (metaclass "
"confusion)」，而在查找特殊方法時繞過實例就可以避免這個問題： ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3781
msgid ""
">>> type(1).__hash__(1) == hash(1)\n"
"True\n"
">>> type(int).__hash__(int) == hash(int)\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> type(1).__hash__(1) == hash(1)\n"
"True\n"
">>> type(int).__hash__(int) == hash(int)\n"
"True"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3786
msgid ""
"In addition to bypassing any instance attributes in the interest of "
"correctness, implicit special method lookup generally also bypasses the :"
"meth:`~object.__getattribute__` method even of the object's metaclass::"
msgstr ""
"除了為了正確性而繞過任何實例屬性之外，隱式特殊方法查找通常也會繞過 :meth:"
"`~object.__getattribute__` 方法，即使是物件之元類別的該方法也一樣： ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3790
msgid ""
">>> class Meta(type):\n"
"...     def __getattribute__(*args):\n"
"...         print(\"Metaclass getattribute invoked\")\n"
"...         return type.__getattribute__(*args)\n"
"...\n"
">>> class C(object, metaclass=Meta):\n"
"...     def __len__(self):\n"
"...         return 10\n"
"...     def __getattribute__(*args):\n"
"...         print(\"Class getattribute invoked\")\n"
"...         return object.__getattribute__(*args)\n"
"...\n"
">>> c = C()\n"
">>> c.__len__()                 # Explicit lookup via instance\n"
"Class getattribute invoked\n"
"10\n"
">>> type(c).__len__(c)          # Explicit lookup via type\n"
"Metaclass getattribute invoked\n"
"10\n"
">>> len(c)                      # Implicit lookup\n"
"10"
msgstr ""
">>> class Meta(type):\n"
"...     def __getattribute__(*args):\n"
"...         print(\"Metaclass getattribute invoked\")\n"
"...         return type.__getattribute__(*args)\n"
"...\n"
">>> class C(object, metaclass=Meta):\n"
"...     def __len__(self):\n"
"...         return 10\n"
"...     def __getattribute__(*args):\n"
"...         print(\"Class getattribute invoked\")\n"
"...         return object.__getattribute__(*args)\n"
"...\n"
">>> c = C()\n"
">>> c.__len__()                 # 透過實例的明確查找\n"
"Class getattribute invoked\n"
"10\n"
">>> type(c).__len__(c)          # 透過型別的明確查找\n"
"Metaclass getattribute invoked\n"
"10\n"
">>> len(c)                      # 隱式查找\n"
"10"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3812
msgid ""
"Bypassing the :meth:`~object.__getattribute__` machinery in this fashion "
"provides significant scope for speed optimisations within the interpreter, "
"at the cost of some flexibility in the handling of special methods (the "
"special method *must* be set on the class object itself in order to be "
"consistently invoked by the interpreter)."
msgstr ""
"以這種方式繞過 :meth:`~object.__getattribute__` 機制，為直譯器內的速度最佳化"
"提供了相當大的空間，代價是在處理特殊方法時失去一些彈性（特殊方法\\ *必須*\\ "
"設定在類別物件本身上，直譯器才能一致地呼叫它）。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3823
msgid "Coroutines"
msgstr "協程"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3827
msgid "Awaitable Objects"
msgstr "可等待物件"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3829
msgid ""
"An :term:`awaitable` object generally implements an :meth:`~object."
"__await__` method. :term:`Coroutine objects <coroutine>` returned from :"
"keyword:`async def` functions are awaitable."
msgstr ""
"一個\\ :term:`可等待 <awaitable>`\\ 物件通常會實作 :meth:`~object.__await__` "
"方法。從 :keyword:`async def` 函式回傳的\\ :term:`協程物件 <coroutine>`\\ 是"
"可等待的。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3835
msgid ""
"The :term:`generator iterator` objects returned from generators decorated "
"with :func:`types.coroutine` are also awaitable, but they do not implement :"
"meth:`~object.__await__`."
msgstr ""
"從以 :func:`types.coroutine` 裝飾的產生器所回傳的\\ :term:`產生器疊代器 "
"<generator iterator>`\\ 物件也是可等待的，但它們並未實作 :meth:`~object."
"__await__`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3841
msgid ""
"Must return an :term:`iterator`.  Should be used to implement :term:"
"`awaitable` objects.  For instance, :class:`asyncio.Future` implements this "
"method to be compatible with the :keyword:`await` expression. The :class:"
"`object` class itself is not awaitable and does not provide this method."
msgstr ""
"必須回傳一個\\ :term:`疊代器 <iterator>`。應被用來實作\\ :term:`可等待 "
"<awaitable>`\\ 物件。例如 :class:`asyncio.Future` 實作此方法以相容於 :"
"keyword:`await` 運算式。:class:`object` 類別本身不是可等待的，也不提供此方"
"法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3849
msgid ""
"The language doesn't place any restriction on the type or value of the "
"objects yielded by the iterator returned by ``__await__``, as this is "
"specific to the implementation of the asynchronous execution framework (e."
"g. :mod:`asyncio`) that will be managing the :term:`awaitable` object."
msgstr ""
"語言本身不對 ``__await__`` 所回傳之疊代器所產出 (yield) 的物件型別或值做任何"
"限制，因為這取決於將管理該\\ :term:`可等待 <awaitable>`\\ 物件的非同步執行框"
"架（例如 :mod:`asyncio`）的實作。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3857
msgid ":pep:`492` for additional information about awaitable objects."
msgstr "關於可等待物件的更多資訊請見 :pep:`492`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3863
msgid "Coroutine Objects"
msgstr "協程物件"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3865
msgid ""
":term:`Coroutine objects <coroutine>` are :term:`awaitable` objects. A "
"coroutine's execution can be controlled by calling :meth:`~object.__await__` "
"and iterating over the result.  When the coroutine has finished executing "
"and returns, the iterator raises :exc:`StopIteration`, and the exception's :"
"attr:`~StopIteration.value` attribute holds the return value.  If the "
"coroutine raises an exception, it is propagated by the iterator.  Coroutines "
"should not directly raise unhandled :exc:`StopIteration` exceptions."
msgstr ""
":term:`協程物件 <coroutine>`\\ 是\\ :term:`可等待 <awaitable>`\\ 物件。協程的"
"執行可以透過呼叫 :meth:`~object.__await__` 並疊代其結果來控制。當協程執行完畢"
"並回傳時，疊代器會引發 :exc:`StopIteration`，而該例外的 :attr:"
"`~StopIteration.value` 屬性會保存回傳值。如果協程引發例外，該例外會由疊代器傳"
"播出去。協程不應直接引發未處理的 :exc:`StopIteration` 例外。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3873
msgid ""
"Coroutines also have the methods listed below, which are analogous to those "
"of generators (see :ref:`generator-methods`).  However, unlike generators, "
"coroutines do not directly support iteration."
msgstr ""
"協程也具有以下列出的方法，它們類似於產生器的方法（請見 :ref:`generator-"
"methods`）。然而，與產生器不同，協程並不直接支援疊代。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3877
msgid ""
"Coroutines are :ref:`generic <generics>` over the types of their yield, "
"send, and return values, respectively."
msgstr ""
"協程是\\ :ref:`泛型 <generics>`\\ 的，其型別參數依序為 yield 值、send 值和回"
"傳值的型別。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3880
msgid "It is a :exc:`RuntimeError` to await on a coroutine more than once."
msgstr "對一個協程 await 超過一次會引發 :exc:`RuntimeError`。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3886
msgid ""
"Starts or resumes execution of the coroutine.  If *value* is ``None``, this "
"is equivalent to advancing the iterator returned by :meth:`~object."
"__await__`.  If *value* is not ``None``, this method delegates to the :meth:"
"`~generator.send` method of the iterator that caused the coroutine to "
"suspend.  The result (return value, :exc:`StopIteration`, or other "
"exception) is the same as when iterating over the :meth:`!__await__` return "
"value, described above."
msgstr ""
"開始或恢復協程的執行。如果 *value* 是 ``None``，這等同於推進 :meth:`~object."
"__await__` 所回傳的疊代器。如果 *value* 不是 ``None``，此方法會委派給導致協程"
"暫停之疊代器的 :meth:`~generator.send` 方法。結果（回傳值、:exc:"
"`StopIteration` 或其他例外）與上述疊代 :meth:`!__await__` 回傳值時相同。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3897
msgid ""
"Raises the specified exception in the coroutine.  This method delegates to "
"the :meth:`~generator.throw` method of the iterator that caused the "
"coroutine to suspend, if it has such a method.  Otherwise, the exception is "
"raised at the suspension point.  The result (return value, :exc:"
"`StopIteration`, or other exception) is the same as when iterating over the :"
"meth:`~object.__await__` return value, described above.  If the exception is "
"not caught in the coroutine, it propagates back to the caller."
msgstr ""
"在協程中引發指定的例外。此方法會委派給導致協程暫停之疊代器的 :meth:"
"`~generator.throw` 方法（如果它有這個方法的話）。否則，例外會在暫停點被引發。"
"結果（回傳值、:exc:`StopIteration` 或其他例外）與上述疊代 :meth:`~object."
"__await__` 回傳值時相同。如果例外沒有在協程中被捕捉，它會傳播回呼叫者。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3908
msgid ""
"The second signature \\(type\\[, value\\[, traceback\\]\\]\\) is deprecated "
"and may be removed in a future version of Python."
msgstr ""
"第二種簽名 \\(type\\[, value\\[, traceback\\]\\]\\) 已被棄用，並可能在未來的 "
"Python 版本中移除。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3913
msgid ""
"Causes the coroutine to clean itself up and exit.  If the coroutine is "
"suspended, this method first delegates to the :meth:`~generator.close` "
"method of the iterator that caused the coroutine to suspend, if it has such "
"a method.  Then it raises :exc:`GeneratorExit` at the suspension point, "
"causing the coroutine to immediately clean itself up. Finally, the coroutine "
"is marked as having finished executing, even if it was never started."
msgstr ""
"使協程清理自身並結束。如果協程處於暫停狀態，此方法會先委派給導致協程暫停之疊"
"代器的 :meth:`~generator.close` 方法（如果它有這個方法的話）。接著它會在暫停"
"點引發 :exc:`GeneratorExit`，使協程立即清理自身。最後，協程會被標記為已執行完"
"畢，即使它從未被啟動過。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3921
msgid ""
"Coroutine objects are automatically closed using the above process when they "
"are about to be destroyed."
msgstr "協程物件在即將被摧毀時，會自動使用上述過程關閉。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3927
msgid "Asynchronous Iterators"
msgstr "非同步疊代器"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3929
msgid ""
"An *asynchronous iterator* can call asynchronous code in its ``__anext__`` "
"method."
msgstr "*非同步疊代器*\\ 可以在其 ``__anext__`` 方法中呼叫非同步程式碼。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3932
msgid ""
"Asynchronous iterators can be used in an :keyword:`async for` statement."
msgstr "非同步疊代器可以用於 :keyword:`async for` 陳述式中。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3934 ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3983
msgid "The :class:`object` class itself does not provide these methods."
msgstr ":class:`object` 類別本身並不提供這些方法。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3939
msgid "Must return an *asynchronous iterator* object."
msgstr "必須回傳一個\\ *非同步疊代器*\\ 物件。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3943
msgid ""
"Must return an *awaitable* resulting in a next value of the iterator.  "
"Should raise a :exc:`StopAsyncIteration` error when the iteration is over."
msgstr ""
"必須回傳一個\\ *可等待物件*，其結果為疊代器的下一個值。疊代結束時應引發 :exc:"
"`StopAsyncIteration` 錯誤。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3946
msgid "An example of an asynchronous iterable object::"
msgstr "一個非同步可疊代物件的範例： ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3948
msgid ""
"class Reader:\n"
"    async def readline(self):\n"
"        ...\n"
"\n"
"    def __aiter__(self):\n"
"        return self\n"
"\n"
"    async def __anext__(self):\n"
"        val = await self.readline()\n"
"        if val == b'':\n"
"            raise StopAsyncIteration\n"
"        return val"
msgstr ""
"class Reader:\n"
"    async def readline(self):\n"
"        ...\n"
"\n"
"    def __aiter__(self):\n"
"        return self\n"
"\n"
"    async def __anext__(self):\n"
"        val = await self.readline()\n"
"        if val == b'':\n"
"            raise StopAsyncIteration\n"
"        return val"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3963
msgid ""
"Prior to Python 3.7, :meth:`~object.__aiter__` could return an *awaitable* "
"that would resolve to an :term:`asynchronous iterator <asynchronous "
"iterator>`."
msgstr ""
"在 Python 3.7 之前，:meth:`~object.__aiter__` 可以回傳一個在 await 後會得到"
"\\ :term:`非同步疊代器 <asynchronous iterator>`\\ 的\\ *可等待物件*。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3968
msgid ""
"Starting with Python 3.7, :meth:`~object.__aiter__` must return an "
"asynchronous iterator object.  Returning anything else will result in a :exc:"
"`TypeError` error."
msgstr ""
"從 Python 3.7 開始，:meth:`~object.__aiter__` 必須回傳一個非同步疊代器物件。"
"回傳其他任何東西都會導致 :exc:`TypeError` 錯誤。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3976
msgid "Asynchronous Context Managers"
msgstr "非同步情境管理器"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3978
msgid ""
"An *asynchronous context manager* is a *context manager* that is able to "
"suspend execution in its ``__aenter__`` and ``__aexit__`` methods."
msgstr ""
"*非同步情境管理器* (asynchronous context manager) 是一種能夠在其 "
"``__aenter__`` 和 ``__aexit__`` 方法中暫停執行的\\ *情境管理器*。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3981
msgid ""
"Asynchronous context managers can be used in an :keyword:`async with` "
"statement."
msgstr "非同步情境管理器可以用於 :keyword:`async with` 陳述式中。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3987
msgid ""
"Semantically similar to :meth:`~object.__enter__`, the only difference being "
"that it must return an *awaitable*."
msgstr ""
"語意上類似於 :meth:`~object.__enter__`，唯一的差別是它必須回傳一個\\ *可等待"
"物件*。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3992
msgid ""
"Semantically similar to :meth:`~object.__exit__`, the only difference being "
"that it must return an *awaitable*."
msgstr ""
"語意上類似於 :meth:`~object.__exit__`，唯一的差別是它必須回傳一個\\ *可等待物"
"件*。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3995
msgid "An example of an asynchronous context manager class::"
msgstr "一個非同步情境管理器類別的範例： ::"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:3997
msgid ""
"class AsyncContextManager:\n"
"    async def __aenter__(self):\n"
"        await log('entering context')\n"
"\n"
"    async def __aexit__(self, exc_type, exc, tb):\n"
"        await log('exiting context')"
msgstr ""
"class AsyncContextManager:\n"
"    async def __aenter__(self):\n"
"        await log('entering context')\n"
"\n"
"    async def __aexit__(self, exc_type, exc, tb):\n"
"        await log('exiting context')"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:4008
msgid "Footnotes"
msgstr "註解"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:4009
msgid ""
"It *is* possible in some cases to change an object's type, under certain "
"controlled conditions. It generally isn't a good idea though, since it can "
"lead to some very strange behaviour if it is handled incorrectly."
msgstr ""
"在某些受控的條件下，有時\\ *確實*\\ 可以改變物件的型別。不過這通常不是個好主"
"意，因為如果處理不當，可能會導致一些非常奇怪的行為。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:4013
msgid ""
"The :meth:`~object.__hash__`, :meth:`~object.__iter__`, :meth:`~object."
"__reversed__`, :meth:`~object.__contains__`, :meth:`~object."
"__class_getitem__` and :meth:`~os.PathLike.__fspath__` methods have special "
"handling for this. Others will still raise a :exc:`TypeError`, but may do so "
"by relying on the behavior that ``None`` is not callable."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~object.__hash__`、:meth:`~object.__iter__`、:meth:`~object."
"__reversed__`、:meth:`~object.__contains__`、:meth:`~object."
"__class_getitem__` 和 :meth:`~os.PathLike.__fspath__` 方法對此有特殊處理。其"
"他方法仍會引發 :exc:`TypeError`，但可能是依賴 ``None`` 不可呼叫這個行為來達成"
"的。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:4020
msgid ""
"\"Does not support\" here means that the class has no such method, or the "
"method returns :data:`NotImplemented`.  Do not set the method to ``None`` if "
"you want to force fallback to the right operand's reflected method—that will "
"instead have the opposite effect of explicitly *blocking* such fallback."
msgstr ""
"這裡的「不支援」是指類別沒有這樣的方法，或該方法回傳 :data:`NotImplemented`。"
"如果你想強制退回使用右運算元的反轉方法，請不要將該方法設為 ``None`` --- 這反"
"而會產生相反的效果，明確地\\ *阻止*\\ 這種退回。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:4026
msgid ""
"For operands of the same type, it is assumed that if the non-reflected "
"method (such as :meth:`~object.__add__`) fails then the operation is not "
"supported, which is why the reflected method is not called."
msgstr ""
"對於相同型別的運算元，會假設如果非反轉方法（例如 :meth:`~object.__add__`）失"
"敗，則該運算不受支援，這就是不會呼叫反轉方法的原因。"

#: ../../reference/datamodel.rst:4030
msgid ""
"If the right operand's type is a subclass of the left operand's type, the "
"reflected method having precedence allows subclasses to override their "
"ancestors' operations."
msgstr ""
"如果右運算元的型別是左運算元型別的子類別，反轉方法具有優先權，可讓子類別覆寫"
"其祖先的運算。"

